INSERT INTO `procedures` VALUES (1,'Cath Lab','procedures/banners/e4c7d5f5-d7c0-426a-8fa5-01f654231c08.webp',NULL,'cath-lab','<p>Cath Lab in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals, recognized as one of the best cath labs in Bangalore and part of a best hospital in Bengaluru, offers advanced diagnostic and interventional cardiac procedures for patients with heart and blood vessel conditions. A Cath Lab (Catheterization Laboratory) uses specialized imaging technology and minimally invasive techniques to diagnose and treat cardiac disorders with precision. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent serious heart complications, improve recovery outcomes, and support better long-term heart health.</p><p>Equipped with modern imaging technology, the Cath Lab plays a crucial role in detecting blockages, assessing heart function, and performing life-saving cardiac interventions.</p>','<p>A Cath Lab (Catheterization Laboratory) is a specialized hospital unit where heart and blood vessel conditions are diagnosed and treated using thin, flexible tubes called catheters. These catheters are inserted through a blood vessel in the wrist or groin and guided to the heart under real-time imaging.</p><p>Cath Lab procedures help evaluate coronary artery blockages, heart valve conditions, congenital heart defects, and heart rhythm disorders. Most procedures are minimally invasive, allowing faster recovery and reduced hospital stay</p>','[{\"value\":\"Symptoms or clinical findings that require Cath Lab for clearer diagnosis\"},{\"value\":\"Unresolved or unexplained complaints after initial clinical evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Need to confirm disease extent, severity, or organ involvement\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring of a known condition where imaging or testing guides next steps\"},{\"value\":\"Pre-treatment planning where accurate assessment is required\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Clinical suspicion of disease based on history and examination\"},{\"value\":\"Abnormal blood reports or previous investigation findings\"},{\"value\":\"Need to differentiate between similar conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Assessment before starting medical or surgical treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up of previously diagnosed disease or treatment response\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Heart conditions cannot always be managed with medicines alone. When blockages or structural heart problems are detected, Cath Lab procedures are the most effective and life-saving treatment options.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Coronary Angiography\", \"description\": \"A thin catheter is inserted through the wrist or groin artery.\\nContrast dye is injected to visualize heart arteries.\\nX-ray imaging detects blockages or narrowing in coronary arteries.\\nHelps doctors decide further treatment like angioplasty or surgery.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Angioplasty (PTCA)\", \"description\": \"A balloon catheter is guided to the blocked artery.\\nThe balloon is inflated to open the narrowed artery.\\nImproves blood flow to the heart muscle.\\nReduces chest pain and risk of heart attack.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Stent Placement\", \"description\": \"A small mesh tube (stent) is placed inside the artery.\\nKeeps the artery open after angioplasty.\\nPrevents re-narrowing of the artery.\\nDrug-eluting stents release medicine to reduce blockage recurrence.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Pacemaker Implantation\", \"description\": \"A small electronic device is implanted under the skin.\\nHelps control abnormal heart rhythms.\\nSends electrical impulses to regulate heartbeat.\\nUsed for slow heart rates or heart block conditions.\"}, {\"name\": \"5. Cardiac Device & Emergency Interventions\", \"description\": \"Temporary pacemaker for critical patients.\\nEmergency angioplasty during heart attacks.\\nCardiac pressure measurements and valve assessments.\\nAdvanced interventional cardiac procedures under imaging guidance.\"}]','[{\"stage\": \"Immediate\", \"details\": \"Vision improves within 24–48 hours.\"}, {\"stage\": \"Short-term\", \"details\": \":Mild irritation, redness, or blurred vision may occur.\"}, {\"stage\": \"Long-term\", \"details\": \"Full recovery in 4–6 weeks\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Cath Lab procedures are life-saving and often life-changing. Early diagnosis and timely intervention help restore blood flow, relieve symptoms, and prevent major cardiac events. With appropriate lifestyle changes, medications, and follow-up care, patients can lead an active and healthy life after Cath Lab treatment.</p>','<p>Cataracts are a natural part of aging, but they need not mean permanent vision loss. With timely diagnosis and surgery, patients can enjoy clear vision and an active lifestyle. Cataract surgery is safe, effective, and one of the most rewarding medical procedures worldwide.</p>','Best Cath Lab in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Best Cath Lab in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals offering accurate heart diagnosis, advanced cardiac procedures, and expert patient-focused cardiac care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-04 07:06:03','2026-07-29 00:28:07','best Advanced Cath Lab in Bangalore'),(2,'Cesarean Section ','procedures/banners/01KGMH8E5TQXBG436PBGTKKD7N.jpg',NULL,'cesarean-section','<p>Cesarean Section in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top delivery options for mothers requiring a safe and planned childbirth experience. As a best hospital in Bangalore for maternity and women&#039;s healthcare, Nano Hospitals provides advanced C-section procedures performed by experienced obstetricians using modern surgical techniques. Early prenatal care, timely diagnosis, and expert medical guidance help ensure the safety and well-being of both mother and baby throughout the delivery journey.</p>','<p>A C‑section is a surgical delivery procedure. It involves:Making an incision in the abdominal wall (usually horizontal, just above the pubic hairline).Opening the uterus to deliver the baby.Removing the placenta and closing the uterus and abdominal layers.It can be <strong>planned (elective)</strong> or <strong>emergency</strong> depending on the situation.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Labour that is not progressing safely\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal distress or abnormal heart-rate patterns\"},{\"value\":\"Heavy bleeding or placental complications\"},{\"value\":\"Breech or other non-head-first baby position\"},{\"value\":\"Prior C-section or uterine surgery requiring planned delivery\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Emergency concerns for mother or baby during labour\"},{\"value\":\"Placenta previa or other placental problems\"},{\"value\":\"Multiple pregnancy or large baby\"},{\"value\":\"Obstructed labour or cephalopelvic disproportion\"},{\"value\":\"Medical conditions where vaginal delivery is higher risk\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>A cesarean section is a surgical delivery performed when vaginal birth is unsafe or not possible. An incision is made in the abdomen and uterus so the baby can be delivered safely, followed by careful closure and postnatal monitoring for mother and newborn.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Pain relief and wound care\"},{\"value\":\"Early gentle mobilisation\"},{\"value\":\"Breastfeeding and newborn support\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring for fever, bleeding, or wound issues\"},{\"value\":\"Activity guidance during the healing period\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding or infection\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to nearby organs in rare cases\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed recovery compared with uncomplicated vaginal birth\"},{\"value\":\"Possible implications for future pregnancies\"}]','<p>Most women recover fully and go on to have healthy pregnancies. However, multiple C‑sections increase risks of placenta problems and uterine rupture. Counseling and careful planning are essential for future pregnancies.</p>','<p>Cesarean section is a life‑saving surgery when complications arise during childbirth. While vaginal delivery remains the natural route, C‑section ensures safe outcomes for mother and baby in high‑risk situations. With modern surgical techniques, anesthesia, and post‑operative care, recovery is smooth, and long‑term outcomes are positive.</p>','Best & Top Cesarean Section in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Cesarean Section in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers safe C-section delivery with expert obstetricians and advanced maternity care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-04 08:06:24','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Cesarean Section in Bangalore'),(4,'Appendectomy ','procedures/banners/f6e7aa9b-7e4c-49d8-8bf3-658f034c899b.webp',NULL,'appendectomy','<p>Appendectomy in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from appendicitis and appendix-related complications. As a best hospital in Bangalore for general and laparoscopic surgery, Nano Hospitals provides advanced appendix removal procedures using modern surgical techniques to ensure accurate treatment, minimal discomfort, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent appendix rupture, serious infections, and other life-threatening complications.</p><p>This article explains appendectomy in detail: what appendicitis is, its symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>Appendicitis occurs when the appendix becomes inflamed, swollen, and infected. The appendix has no essential function, but when blocked, it can cause severe pain and infection.</p><p>Appendectomy is the definitive treatment — either <strong>open surgery</strong> or <strong>laparoscopic surgery</strong></p>','[{\"value\":\"Pain that starts near the navel and shifts to the lower right abdomen\"},{\"value\":\"Loss of appetite, nausea, or vomiting\"},{\"value\":\"Low-grade fever\"},{\"value\":\"Abdominal tenderness that worsens with movement\"},{\"value\":\"Bloating or difficulty passing gas\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Blockage of the appendix opening\"},{\"value\":\"Infection leading to inflammation of the appendix\"},{\"value\":\"Hardened stool (fecalith) obstructing the appendix\"},{\"value\":\"Swollen lymphoid tissue\"},{\"value\":\"Rarely, tumors or other local pathology\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Appendectomy is the standard treatment for appendicitis. The inflamed appendix is removed, usually by laparoscopic surgery when suitable, to prevent rupture and spread of infection. Prompt evaluation is important if classic symptoms appear.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tOpen Appendectomy\", \"description\": \"o\\tSingle incision in lower right abdomen.\\no\\tAppendix removed directly.\\no\\tPreferred if appendix ruptured or abscess present.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tLaparoscopic Appendectomy\", \"description\": \"o\\t2–3 small incisions.\\no\\tCamera and instruments used to remove appendix.\\no\\tLess pain, faster recovery.\\n\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Pain control and early walking\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual restart of oral intake\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and hygiene\"},{\"value\":\"Watch for fever or increasing abdominal pain\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up review before returning to strenuous activity\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection or abscess\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to nearby bowel in rare cases\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed return of bowel function\"},{\"value\":\"Wound-related complications\"}]','<p>Appendectomy is highly successful. Once removed, the appendix does not grow back, and patients live normal lives. Early surgery prevents life-threatening complications.</p>','<p>Appendectomy is a safe, effective, and life-saving procedure for appendicitis. With modern surgical techniques, recovery is quick, and risks are minimal. Patients should seek immediate medical care for sudden abdominal pain to avoid rupture and complications.</p>','Best & Top Appendectomy in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Appendectomy in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced appendix removal surgery with expert surgeons and faster recovery.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 10:32:12','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Appendectomy in Bangalore '),(6,'Cholecystectomy ','procedures/banners/f4437791-3980-4fa9-b609-d801efef35fb.webp',NULL,'cholecystectomy','<p>Cholecystectomy in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from gallstones, gallbladder inflammation, and other gallbladder disorders. As a best hospital in Bangalore for gastrointestinal and laparoscopic surgery, Nano Hospitals provides advanced gallbladder removal procedures using modern minimally invasive techniques to ensure effective treatment, reduced pain, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent serious complications such as gallbladder infection, bile duct obstruction, and pancreatitis.</p><p>This article provides a comprehensive overview of gallbladder disease and cholecystectomy — symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The gallbladder stores bile, which helps digest fats. When bile becomes imbalanced, stones form. These stones can block ducts, leading to pain and infection.</p><p>Cholecystectomy removes the gallbladder entirely, preventing recurrence of gallstones.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Severe pain in the upper right abdomen or under the ribs\"},{\"value\":\"Pain after fatty meals\"},{\"value\":\"Nausea or vomiting\"},{\"value\":\"Bloating and indigestion\"},{\"value\":\"Fever or jaundice if infection or bile-duct blockage occurs\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Gallstones blocking bile flow\"},{\"value\":\"Inflammation of the gallbladder (cholecystitis)\"},{\"value\":\"Biliary colic from intermittent stone obstruction\"},{\"value\":\"Gallbladder polyps or dysfunction in selected cases\"},{\"value\":\"Complications such as pancreatitis related to gallstones\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Cholecystectomy removes the gallbladder, most often laparoscopically, to treat symptomatic gallstones and related inflammation. Removing the gallbladder prevents recurrent biliary pain and reduces the risk of serious stone-related complications.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tLaparoscopic Cholecystectomy\", \"description\": \"Minimally invasive, 3–4 small incisions.Camera and instruments used to remove gallbladder.Faster recovery, less pain.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tOpen Cholecystectomy\", \"description\": \"Larger incision in abdomen.Used if gallbladder is severely inflamed or scarred\\n\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Early mobilisation and pain control\"},{\"value\":\"Light diet progressing as tolerated\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care for port sites\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring for fever, jaundice, or severe pain\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual return to normal activity\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding or infection\"},{\"value\":\"Bile leak\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to the bile duct in rare cases\"},{\"value\":\"Retained stones in the bile duct\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary digestive changes after surgery\"}]','<p>Patients live normal lives without a gallbladder. Bile flows directly from liver to intestine. Some may experience mild digestive changes, but most adapt well.</p>','<p>Cholecystectomy is a safe and effective treatment for gallstones and gallbladder disease. With modern laparoscopic techniques, recovery is quick, and risks are minimal. Patients regain comfort, avoid recurrent attacks, and enjoy a healthy life after surgery.</p>','Best & Top Cholecystectomy in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Cholecystectomy in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced gallbladder removal surgery with expert surgeons and faster recovery.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 11:38:33','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Cholecystectomy in Bangalore'),(7,'Knee Replacement Surgery ','procedures/banners/cdebd0f2-c7fc-40f5-8f9e-f655414815a1.webp',NULL,'knee-replacement-surgery','<p>Knee Replacement Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from chronic knee pain, arthritis, and joint damage. As a best hospital in Bangalore for orthopedic care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced knee replacement procedures using modern surgical techniques and personalized treatment plans. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help improve mobility, reduce pain, and enhance overall quality of life.</p><p>This article explains knee replacement comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>Knee arthritis is the progressive wear and tear of the knee joint, leading to pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. The most common type is <strong>osteoarthritis</strong>, where cartilage wears away, causing bones to rub together. Other causes include <strong>rheumatoid arthritis</strong> and post-traumatic arthritis.</p><p>When conservative treatments fail, knee replacement surgery becomes necessary.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Chronic knee pain that interferes with walking or climbing stairs\"},{\"value\":\"Knee stiffness and swelling that does not settle with rest\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty straightening or bending the knee fully\"},{\"value\":\"Pain at night or while resting\"},{\"value\":\"Feeling that the knee may give way or lock\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Advanced osteoarthritis of the knee\"},{\"value\":\"Rheumatoid arthritis or inflammatory arthritis\"},{\"value\":\"Post-traumatic arthritis after injury or fracture\"},{\"value\":\"Severe cartilage loss and joint deformity\"},{\"value\":\"Long-standing wear-and-tear changes in the knee joint\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Knee replacement is advised when severe arthritis or joint damage causes persistent pain and disability despite medicines, injections, physiotherapy, and lifestyle changes. Damaged joint surfaces are replaced with prosthetic components to restore alignment, reduce pain, and improve walking ability.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Functional assessment – impact on daily life\", \"description\": \"Entire knee joint replaced with prosthesis\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Knee Replacement (PKR) \", \"description\": \"Only damaged part replaced.\"}, {\"name\": \"Revision Knee Replacement \", \"description\": \"Replacement of failed or worn-out implant.\"}]','[{\"stage\":\"First few days\",\"details\":\"Hospital recovery with pain management and assisted walking.\"},{\"stage\":\"2\\u20136 weeks\",\"details\":\"Home physiotherapy, reduced swelling, and improving knee bend.\"},{\"stage\":\"6\\u201312 weeks\",\"details\":\"Greater independence for daily walking and light activities.\"},{\"stage\":\"3\\u20136 months\",\"details\":\"Continued strength gains and return to most routine activities.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Early mobilisation and supervised physiotherapy\"},{\"value\":\"Pain and swelling control\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and scheduled follow-up reviews\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual strengthening and gait training\"},{\"value\":\"Return to routine activities as advised by the surgical team\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection or delayed wound healing\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Stiffness or limited knee bending\"},{\"value\":\"Implant wear or loosening over time\"},{\"value\":\"Nerve irritation or ongoing discomfort in some cases\"}]','<p>Knee replacement is highly successful — over <strong>90% of patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility</strong>. Modern implants last 15–20 years, and many patients return to active lifestyles.</p>','<p>Knee replacement surgery transforms lives by relieving pain and restoring independence. With proper patient selection, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, outcomes are excellent. Patients can look forward to walking comfortably, climbing stairs, and enjoying daily activities without the burden of chronic knee pain.</p>','Best & Top Knee Replacement Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Knee Replacement Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced orthopedic care, expert surgeons, and faster recovery.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 11:49:13','2026-07-29 00:13:31','Best & Top Knee Replacement Surgery in Bangalore'),(8,'Hip Replacement Surgery ','procedures/banners/0d44d9ee-4961-4ee6-b9ec-d8a0de35764d.webp',NULL,'hip-replacement-surgery','<p>Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from severe hip pain, arthritis, and reduced joint mobility. As a best hospital in Bangalore for orthopedic care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hip replacement procedures using modern surgical techniques and high-quality implants to restore movement and improve quality of life. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help reduce pain, enhance mobility, and prevent further joint deterioration.</p><p>This article explains hip replacement comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The hip is a ball-and-socket joint. In arthritis, the cartilage cushioning the joint wears away, causing bones to rub together. This leads to pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. Hip replacement replaces the damaged joint with artificial components made of metal, ceramic, or plastic.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Persistent hip pain that limits walking, climbing stairs, or daily activities\"},{\"value\":\"Stiffness in the hip joint, especially after sitting or resting\"},{\"value\":\"Pain that continues even while resting or at night\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced range of motion and difficulty bending to put on shoes or socks\"},{\"value\":\"Limping or an uneven walking pattern due to joint discomfort\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Osteoarthritis causing cartilage wear in the hip joint\"},{\"value\":\"Rheumatoid arthritis or other inflammatory joint disease\"},{\"value\":\"Avascular necrosis (loss of blood supply to the femoral head)\"},{\"value\":\"Hip fracture or previous traumatic injury\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital hip dysplasia or long-standing joint deformity\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Hip replacement surgery is considered when pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility no longer improve with medicines, physiotherapy, activity modification, or walking aids. The damaged ball-and-socket surfaces of the hip are replaced with artificial components to restore smoother movement and reduce pain.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, orthopedic specialists evaluate joint damage with clinical examination and imaging, then recommend total or partial hip replacement based on the severity of arthritis, fracture pattern, age, and overall health.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Total Hip Replacement (THR)\", \"description\": \"Both the femoral head (ball) and acetabulum (socket) are replaced.\\n\\nDamaged cartilage and bone are removed.\\n\\nArtificial components made of metal, ceramic, or polyethylene are implanted.\\nRecommended for severe arthritis or advanced joint damage.\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"Only the femoral head is replaced.\\n\\nThe natural socket (acetabulum) is preserved.\\n\\nCommonly performed for hip fractures in elderly patients.\"}]','[{\"stage\":\"Hospital stay (usually 2\\u20134 days)\",\"details\":\"Pain control, wound care, and first steps with a walker or support under physiotherapy supervision.\"},{\"stage\":\"First 2\\u20136 weeks\",\"details\":\"Home recovery with walking aids, hip precautions, and progressive physiotherapy to rebuild strength and confidence.\"},{\"stage\":\"6\\u201312 weeks\",\"details\":\"Most patients regain greater independence for daily activities; driving and light work may resume based on surgeon advice.\"},{\"stage\":\"3\\u20136 months\",\"details\":\"Continued improvement in mobility and endurance, with many patients returning to an active lifestyle.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Early walking with support under physiotherapy guidance\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and swelling management as advised by the care team\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and follow-up visits to monitor healing\"},{\"value\":\"Hip precautions and safe movement techniques during early recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual return to daily activities with strengthening exercises\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection around the surgical site or prosthesis\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots in the legs or lungs\"},{\"value\":\"Hip dislocation or implant loosening over time\"},{\"value\":\"Leg length difference or temporary nerve irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding, swelling, or delayed wound healing\"}]','<p>Hip replacement is highly successful — over <strong>90% of patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility</strong>. Modern implants last 15–20 years, and many patients return to active lifestyles.</p>','<p>Hip replacement surgery transforms lives by relieving pain and restoring independence. With proper patient selection, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, outcomes are excellent. Patients can look forward to walking comfortably, climbing stairs, and enjoying daily activities without the burden of chronic hip pain.</p>','Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hip replacement procedures with expert orthopedic care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 12:02:00','2026-07-29 00:13:02','Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore'),(9,'Hernia Repair Surgery ','procedures/banners/898b87bf-26c5-4d3c-814f-8768f84cb930.webp',NULL,'hernia-repair-surgery','<p>Hernia Repair Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from inguinal, umbilical, incisional, and other types of hernias. As a best hospital in Bangalore for general and laparoscopic surgery, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hernia repair procedures using modern surgical techniques to ensure effective treatment, minimal discomfort, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent complications such as strangulation, obstruction, and severe pain while improving overall quality of life.</p><p>This article explains hernia repair comprehensively — what a hernia is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"A bulge in the groin, abdomen, or prior surgical scar\"},{\"value\":\"Discomfort or pain that worsens with coughing or lifting\"},{\"value\":\"Heaviness or pressure at the hernia site\"},{\"value\":\"Bulge that reduces when lying down in some cases\"},{\"value\":\"Severe pain, redness, or vomiting if the hernia becomes trapped\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Weakness in the abdominal wall or groin muscles\"},{\"value\":\"Increased abdominal pressure from heavy lifting or chronic cough\"},{\"value\":\"Previous abdominal surgery (incisional hernia)\"},{\"value\":\"Pregnancy-related abdominal wall strain\"},{\"value\":\"Age-related tissue weakening\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Hernia repair returns displaced tissue to its proper place and strengthens the weakened area, often with mesh reinforcement. Surgery may be open or laparoscopic depending on hernia type, size, and patient factors.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tOpen Hernia Repair\", \"description\": \"Single incision over hernia site.Tissue pushed back, muscle wall repaired.\\nMesh often used to reinforce.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tLaparoscopic Hernia Repair\", \"description\": \"Small incisions, camera used.Mesh placed internally.Less pain, faster recovery.\\n\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Activity restriction and avoid heavy lifting initially\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and wound care\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual return to walking and daily routines\"},{\"value\":\"Watch for increasing swelling, redness, or fever\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up to confirm sound healing of the repair\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Recurrence of the hernia\"},{\"value\":\"Infection or seroma\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic discomfort at the repair site\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to nearby nerves or vessels in rare cases\"},{\"value\":\"Mesh-related issues in a small number of patients\"}]','<p>Hernia repair is highly successful. Mesh reinforcement reduces recurrence rates significantly. Most patients return to normal activities and enjoy long-term relief.</p>','<p>Hernia repair is a safe and effective surgery that prevents serious complications like strangulation and obstruction. With modern techniques, recovery is quick, and outcomes are excellent. Patients regain comfort, confidence, and quality of life after surgery.</p>','Best & Top Hernia Repair Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Hernia Repair Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hernia treatment with expert surgeons and faster recovery.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 12:08:52','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Hernia Repair Surgery in Bangalore'),(10,'Breast Surgery ','procedures/banners/6bbe5bcf-5aaa-48aa-8106-b8917e920929.webp',NULL,'breast-surgery','<p>Breast Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients with breast lumps, breast cancer, benign breast conditions, and cosmetic or reconstructive breast concerns. As a best hospital in Bangalore for breast care and surgical treatment, Nano Hospitals provides advanced breast surgery procedures using modern techniques to ensure precise treatment, improved outcomes, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help detect serious conditions at an early stage and support better long-term health.</p><p>This article explains breast surgery comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>Breast cancer occurs when abnormal cells grow uncontrollably in breast tissue. It may present as a lump, nipple discharge, or skin changes. Surgery is often the first line of treatment, combined with therapies like chemotherapy, radiation, or hormone therapy.</p>','[{\"value\":\"A breast lump or thickening\"},{\"value\":\"Nipple discharge, inversion, or skin dimpling\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent breast pain or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Changes in breast shape or skin texture\"},{\"value\":\"Enlarged lymph nodes under the arm in some cases\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Breast cancer requiring surgical removal of disease\"},{\"value\":\"Benign breast lumps that need excision\"},{\"value\":\"High-risk lesions found on biopsy\"},{\"value\":\"Infection or abscess needing drainage in selected cases\"},{\"value\":\"Reconstructive needs after cancer surgery\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Breast surgery ranges from lumpectomy to mastectomy and may include lymph-node evaluation. The plan depends on diagnosis, tumor size, and patient goals, and is often coordinated with oncology, radiology, and reconstructive care.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Breast-Conserving Surgery (Lumpectomy)\", \"description\": \"Only the tumor and a small margin of surrounding healthy tissue are removed.\\n\\nThe rest of the breast is preserved.\\n\\nUsually followed by radiation therapy.\\n\\nSuitable for early-stage breast cancer.\"}, {\"name\": \"Mastectomy\", \"description\": \"Simple (Total) Mastectomy – Entire breast removed, lymph nodes not removed.\\n\\nModified Radical Mastectomy – Breast tissue + some underarm (axillary) lymph nodes removed.\\n\\nSkin-Sparing Mastectomy – Most skin preserved for reconstruction.\\n\\nNipple-Sparing Mastectomy – Nipple and skin preserved when oncologically safe.\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Wound and drain care as advised\"},{\"value\":\"Arm mobility exercises when recommended\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and swelling support\"},{\"value\":\"Pathology review and next-step oncology planning\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up for healing and rehabilitation\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding, infection, or seroma\"},{\"value\":\"Changes in breast shape or sensation\"},{\"value\":\"Lymphedema after lymph-node surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Scarring or delayed wound healing\"},{\"value\":\"Need for further treatment based on pathology\"}]','<p>Breast surgery significantly improves survival in cancer patients. With reconstruction, cosmetic outcomes are excellent. Regular follow-up and adjuvant therapies ensure long-term success.</p>','<p>Breast surgery — whether lumpectomy or mastectomy — is a cornerstone of breast cancer treatment. It saves lives, restores confidence, and offers hope. With modern surgical techniques and reconstruction, patients can look forward to both survival and quality of life.</p>','Best & Top Breast Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Breast Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced breast procedures with expert surgeons and compassionate care.','breast surgery, mastectomy, lumpectomy, breast cancer surgery, breast reconstruction, breast lump removal, Nano Hospital oncology',1,'2026-02-18 12:21:24','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Breast Surgery in Bangalore'),(11,'Tonsillectomy','procedures/banners/8ebd14a9-db37-43ca-8b30-9e072d1c49de.webp',NULL,'tonsillectomy','<p>Tonsillectomy in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients experiencing recurrent tonsillitis, enlarged tonsils, and breathing difficulties. As a best hospital in Bangalore for ENT care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced tonsil removal procedures using modern surgical techniques to ensure patient safety and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent recurring infections, improve breathing, and enhance overall quality of life.</p>','<p>The procedure is usually performed under general anesthesia through the mouth without external cuts. The ENT surgeon removes the tonsils using specialized surgical instruments, electrocautery, coblation, or other advanced techniques. Tonsillectomy may be recommended for: Recurrent throat infections Enlarged tonsils causing obstruction Sleep-disordered breathing Recurrent tonsil abscess Difficulty swallowing due to enlarged tonsils The surgery is commonly performed in children but may also be required in adults.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Recurrent sore throat\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty swallowing\"},{\"value\":\"Snoring or sleep apnea\"},{\"value\":\"Fever with throat infections\"},{\"value\":\"Enlarged tonsils causing breathing difficulty\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Tonsillectomy is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding after surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Throat pain during recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Infection\"},{\"value\":\"Dehydration due to painful swallowing\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary voice changes\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Tonsillectomy is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>The procedure is usually performed under general anesthesia through the mouth without external cuts. The ENT surgeon removes the tonsils using specialized surgical instruments, electrocautery, coblation, or other advance...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Eat soft and cool foods initially\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid spicy or hard foods temporarily\"},{\"value\":\"Take prescribed pain medications regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for bleeding or fever immediately\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding after surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Throat pain during recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Infection\"},{\"value\":\"Dehydration due to painful swallowing\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary voice changes\"}]','<p>Tonsillectomy significantly reduces recurrent throat infections and improves breathing and sleep quality. Most patients experience long-term relief and improved overall health.</p>','<p></p>','Best & Top Tonsillectomy in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Tonsillectomy in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced tonsil removal surgery with expert ENT specialists and quality care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 12:29:37','2026-07-29 00:28:07','Best & Top Tonsillectomy in Bangalore'),(12,'Hysterectomy ','procedures/banners/757507cf-6af7-425f-88a4-062345f217f7.webp',NULL,'hysterectomy','<p>Hysterectomy in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for women experiencing uterine fibroids, abnormal uterine bleeding, endometriosis, and other gynecological conditions. As a best hospital in Bangalore for women&#039;s healthcare, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hysterectomy procedures using modern surgical techniques to ensure safety, faster recovery, and improved quality of life. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent complications and support long-term reproductive health and well-being.</p><p>This article explains hysterectomy comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>A hysterectomy involves removing the uterus, sometimes along with the cervix, ovaries, and fallopian tubes depending on the condition. After hysterectomy, menstruation stops, and pregnancy is no longer possible.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Severe pelvic pain or pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Symptoms from fibroids, endometriosis, or adenomyosis\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic organ prolapse symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Cancer-related bleeding or abnormal findings\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Symptomatic uterine fibroids\"},{\"value\":\"Endometriosis or adenomyosis not controlled medically\"},{\"value\":\"Abnormal uterine bleeding unresponsive to other treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Uterine, cervical, or ovarian cancer in selected cases\"},{\"value\":\"Severe pelvic organ prolapse\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Hysterectomy removes the uterus and, when required, related structures. Approach may be vaginal, laparoscopic, or open depending on the condition. It is considered when symptoms or disease are significant and other treatments are unsuitable or unsuccessful.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Total Hysterectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of the entire uterus including the cervix.\\n\\nOvaries may or may not be removed.\\n\\nCommonly performed for fibroids, abnormal bleeding, or cancer.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Subtotal (Partial / Supracervical) Hysterectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of the upper part of the uterus.\\n\\nCervix is left intact.\\n\\nMay be chosen in selected non-cancer cases.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Radical Hysterectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of uterus, cervix, surrounding tissues, and part of the vagina.\\n\\nOften includes removal of nearby lymph nodes.\\n\\nTypically performed for certain gynecological cancers.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Hysterectomy with Bilateral Salpingo-Oophorectomy (BSO)\", \"description\": \"Uterus + both fallopian tubes + both ovaries are removed.\\n\\nCauses immediate surgical menopause if premenopausal.\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Pain control and gradual mobilisation\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic rest as advised by the surgeon\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and monitoring for fever or heavy bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Hormone counselling if ovaries are removed\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up before returning to exercise or intercourse\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding or infection\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to bladder, bowel, or ureters in rare cases\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Early menopause if ovaries are removed\"},{\"value\":\"Changes in pelvic support or sexual comfort for some patients\"}]','<p>Hysterectomy is highly effective for treating severe gynecological conditions. With proper counseling and support, patients regain health and quality of life.</p>','<p>Hysterectomy is a major but often necessary surgery. It provides relief from pain, bleeding, and cancer risks, allowing women to live healthier lives.</p>','Best & Top Hysterectomy in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Hysterectomy in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hysterectomy procedures with expert gynecologists and personalized care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 12:36:09','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Hysterectomy in Bangalore'),(13,'Prostate Surgery ','procedures/banners/ee0925a7-18e0-4033-9d77-fe438e9c999e.webp',NULL,'prostate-surgery','<p>Prostate Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for men suffering from prostate enlargement, urinary problems, prostate cancer, and other urological conditions. As a best hospital in Bangalore for urology care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced prostate surgery procedures using modern surgical techniques to ensure precise treatment, improved urinary function, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent complications, improve quality of life, and support long-term urinary health.</p><p>This article explains prostate surgery comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<ul><li><p><strong>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH)</strong>: Non-cancerous enlargement of the prostate, common in older men.</p></li><li><p><strong>Prostate Cancer</strong>: Malignant growth of prostate cells, one of the most common cancers in men.</p></li></ul><p>Both conditions may require surgical intervention when symptoms are severe or life-threatening.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Weak urine stream or difficulty starting urination\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination, especially at night\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete bladder emptying\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary urgency or intermittent stopping of flow\"},{\"value\":\"Blood in urine or suspected prostate cancer findings\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)\"},{\"value\":\"Prostate cancer requiring surgical treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary obstruction from prostate enlargement\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent urinary retention or infections related to obstruction\"},{\"value\":\"Failure of medicines to control prostate-related symptoms\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Prostate surgery may relieve obstruction from BPH or treat prostate cancer. Options range from endoscopic procedures that open the urinary channel to radical prostatectomy when cancer surgery is indicated. Choice depends on diagnosis, prostate size, and patient priorities.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tTransurethral Resection of the Prostate (TURP)\", \"description\": \"Common for BPH.Resects prostate tissue via urethra using a scope.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tProstatectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of part or all of the prostate.\\nTypes: \\nSimple prostatectomy – for BPH.\\nRadical prostatectomy – for cancer (removes prostate, seminal vesicles, sometimes lymph nodes).\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"3.\\tLaser Surgery\", \"description\": \"Minimally invasive.Uses laser to vaporize or enucleate prostate tissue\\n\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Catheter care for the prescribed duration\"},{\"value\":\"Hydration and monitoring of urine output\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic floor exercises when advised\"},{\"value\":\"Activity restrictions during early healing\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up PSA or symptom review based on diagnosis\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding or infection\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary or longer-term urinary incontinence\"},{\"value\":\"Erectile dysfunction after some cancer surgeries\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary stricture or need for catheter support\"},{\"value\":\"Retrograde ejaculation after certain BPH procedures\"}]','<p>Prostate surgery is highly effective. TURP relieves urinary symptoms in BPH, while radical prostatectomy offers cure for localized cancer. With modern techniques (laparoscopic, robotic), recovery is faster and complications fewer.</p>','<p>Prostate surgery is a vital treatment for men with severe prostate disease. It restores urinary function, prevents complications, and saves lives in cancer cases. With proper diagnosis, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, patients regain health and quality of life.</p>','Best & Top Prostate Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Prostate Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced prostate treatments with expert urologists and personalized care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 12:43:10','2026-07-29 00:15:55','Best & Top Prostate Surgery in Bangalore'),(14,'Spinal Surgery ','procedures/banners/f2bec02d-bc48-4a76-8b9f-1ae4cbe8c0c8.webp',NULL,'spinal-surgery','<p>Spinal surgery is one of the most common orthopedic and neurosurgical procedures worldwide, performed to treat conditions such as <strong>herniated discs, spinal stenosis, scoliosis, fractures, and chronic back pain</strong>. The spine is the body’s central support structure, housing the spinal cord and nerves. When spinal problems cause severe pain, disability, or nerve compression, surgery may be necessary to restore function and quality of life.</p><p>This article explains spinal surgery comprehensively — what spinal conditions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedures, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The spine is made up of vertebrae, discs, ligaments, and nerves. Common conditions requiring surgery include:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Herniated disc</strong> – disc material presses on nerves.</p></li><li><p><strong>Spinal stenosis</strong> – narrowing of spinal canal compresses nerves.</p></li><li><p><strong>Scoliosis</strong> – abnormal curvature of spine.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fractures</strong> – due to trauma or osteoporosis.</p></li><li><p><strong>Degenerative disc disease</strong> – age-related wear and tear.</p></li></ul>','[\"Chronic back or neck pain\", \"Pain radiating to arms or legs (sciatica)\", \"Numbness or tingling in limbs\", \"Muscle weakness\", \"Difficulty walking or standing\", \"Loss of bladder or bowel control (severe cases)\"]','[\"Degenerative changes – aging, arthritis\", \"Trauma – accidents, falls, sports injuries\", \"Congenital deformities – scoliosis, spina bifida\", \"Infections or tumors\", \"Lifestyle factors – poor posture, obesity, sedentary habits\"]','[\"Chronic pain and disability\", \"Permanent nerve damage\", \"Paralysis in severe cases\", \"Loss of independence\", \"Depression and reduced quality of life\"]','[\"Maintain healthy weight\", \"Regular exercise to strengthen back muscles\", \"Good posture and ergonomics\", \"Avoid smoking (reduces bone health)\", \"Early treatment of back injuries\"]','[\"Physical exam – assess pain, mobility, reflexes\", \"X-rays – show bone alignment and fractures\", \"MRI – detailed view of discs and nerves\", \"CT scan – cross-sectional imaging\", \"Nerve conduction studies – assess nerve damage\"]','<p>Spinal surgery is considered for selected disc, stenosis, deformity, fracture, or nerve-compression problems when pain, weakness, or neurological symptoms persist despite conservative care. The goal is to relieve nerve pressure, stabilize the spine when needed, and restore safer mobility.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Discectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of a herniated or damaged intervertebral disc.\\n\\nRelieves pressure on spinal nerves.\\n\\nCommonly performed for slipped disc causing sciatica.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Laminectomy (Decompression Surgery)\", \"description\": \"Removal of part of the vertebral bone (lamina).\\n\\nCreates more space for the spinal cord or nerves.\\n\\nUsed in spinal stenosis.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Spinal Fusion\", \"description\": \"Two or more vertebrae are permanently joined together.\\n\\nBone graft and metal screws/rods are used for stability.\\n\\nPerformed for instability, severe arthritis, or deformity.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Artificial Disc Replacement\", \"description\": \"Damaged disc is removed and replaced with an artificial implant.\\n\\nPreserves motion between vertebrae.\\n\\nAlternative to fusion in selected patients.\"}]','[{\"stage\":\"Hospital phase\",\"details\":\"Pain control, wound care, and early assisted mobilisation.\"},{\"stage\":\"First 4\\u20136 weeks\",\"details\":\"Activity modification, physiotherapy, and gradual increase in walking.\"},{\"stage\":\"6\\u201312 weeks\",\"details\":\"Progressive strengthening and return to light routines as cleared by the surgeon.\"},{\"stage\":\"3+ months\",\"details\":\"Continued rehabilitation toward durable pain relief and function.\"}]','[\"Pain management with medications.\", \"Physiotherapy to restore strength and flexibility.\", \"Avoid heavy lifting for several months.\", \"Wound care and hygiene.\", \"Regular follow-up with surgeon.\"]','[\"Infection at surgical site\", \"Bleeding\", \"Nerve injury → weakness or paralysis\", \"Failed back surgery syndrome (persistent pain)\", \"Hardware failure in fusion surgeries\"]','<p>Spinal surgery is highly effective when performed for the right indications. Most patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility. Rehabilitation and lifestyle changes are crucial for long-term success.</p>','<p>Spinal surgery is a vital treatment for severe back and nerve conditions. With modern techniques, outcomes are excellent, and patients regain independence and quality of life. Proper diagnosis, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation ensure the best results.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-18 12:51:50','2026-07-29 00:15:56',NULL),(15,'Skin Surgery ','procedures/banners/7629e2f5-7d3f-4138-a426-ec76884239ad.webp',NULL,'skin-surgery','<p>Skin Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients with skin growths, cysts, moles, skin cancers, and other dermatological conditions. As a best hospital in Bangalore for surgical and dermatological care, Nano Hospitals offers advanced skin surgery procedures using modern techniques to ensure precise treatment and optimal cosmetic outcomes. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent complications, promote faster healing, and improve overall skin health.</p><p>This article explains skin surgery comprehensively — what skin lesions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>Skin lesions are abnormal growths or changes in the skin. They may be:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Benign</strong>: moles, cysts, lipomas, warts.</p></li><li><p><strong>Premalignant</strong>: actinic keratosis (sun-damaged patches).</p></li><li><p><strong>Malignant</strong>: basal cell carcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, melanoma.</p></li></ul>','[{\"value\":\"A changing mole, growth, or non-healing skin lesion\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding, crusting, or ulceration of a skin spot\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cysts, lipomas, or painful skin lumps\"},{\"value\":\"Suspected skin cancer on clinical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Scarring or lesions needing excision for diagnosis or comfort\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Benign skin tumors or cysts\"},{\"value\":\"Suspected or confirmed skin cancer\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic non-healing lesions\"},{\"value\":\"Infected or repeatedly inflamed skin swellings\"},{\"value\":\"Diagnostic biopsy needs\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Skin surgery removes or samples abnormal skin lesions for diagnosis and treatment. Procedures may include excision, biopsy, or reconstructive closure depending on lesion type, size, and location.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Excisional Surgery\", \"description\": \"Complete removal of a skin lesion or tumor.\\n\\nA margin of healthy skin may also be removed.\\n\\nCommonly performed for skin cancers, cysts, or suspicious moles.\\n\\nWound closed with sutures.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Mohs Micrographic Surgery\", \"description\": \"Layer-by-layer removal of skin cancer.\\n\\nEach layer examined under a microscope during surgery.\\n\\nPreserves maximum healthy tissue.\\n\\nHigh cure rate for basal cell and squamous cell carcinoma.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Cryosurgery\", \"description\": \"Uses liquid nitrogen to freeze abnormal tissue.\\n\\nPerformed for warts, precancerous lesions, and small skin cancers.\\n\\nMinimally invasive with quick recovery.\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Wound dressing and hygiene guidance\"},{\"value\":\"Suture care or removal as scheduled\"},{\"value\":\"Sun protection of the healing area\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring for redness, discharge, or fever\"},{\"value\":\"Pathology follow-up when tissue is sent for testing\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding, infection, or delayed healing\"},{\"value\":\"Scarring or pigment change\"},{\"value\":\"Nerve irritation in sensitive areas\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete margins requiring further treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrence of some lesions\"}]','<p>Skin surgery is highly successful. Benign lesions are cured, and malignant cancers are controlled if detected early. Cosmetic outcomes are excellent with modern techniques.</p>','<p>Skin surgery is a safe and effective procedure for removing abnormal skin growths. It ensures accurate diagnosis, prevents cancer spread, and restores confidence. With proper care and follow-up, patients enjoy excellent outcomes and peace of mind.</p>','Best & Top Skin Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Skin Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced skin procedures, expert care, and personalized treatment.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 13:03:20','2026-07-29 00:15:56','Best & Top Skin Surgery in Bangalore'),(16,'Colorectal Surgery ','procedures/banners/bf8d8f28-9330-40ec-b60c-ab56d02c2a4b.webp',NULL,'colorectal-surgery','<p>Colorectal Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from colorectal diseases, including colon cancer, rectal disorders, inflammatory bowel disease, and hemorrhoids. As a best hospital in Bangalore for gastrointestinal and colorectal care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced surgical treatments using modern techniques to ensure accurate diagnosis, effective treatment, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely intervention can help prevent complications and improve long-term digestive health and quality of life.</p><p>This article explains colorectal surgery comprehensively — what colorectal conditions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedures, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The colon and rectum are parts of the large intestine responsible for absorbing water and eliminating waste. Common conditions requiring surgery include:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Colorectal cancer</strong> – malignant growth in colon or rectum.</p></li><li><p><strong>Diverticulitis</strong> – inflamed pouches in colon wall.</p></li><li><p><strong>Inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)</strong> – Crohn’s disease, ulcerative colitis.</p></li><li><p><strong>Polyps</strong> – precancerous growths.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hemorrhoids</strong> – swollen rectal veins.</p></li><li><p><strong>Anal fistulas and fissures</strong>.</p></li></ul>','[{\"value\":\"Rectal bleeding or black stools\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent change in bowel habits\"},{\"value\":\"Abdominal pain or bloating\"},{\"value\":\"Unexplained weight loss or anemia\"},{\"value\":\"Anal pain, swelling, or discharge in local anorectal disease\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Colorectal cancer or polyps\"},{\"value\":\"Diverticular disease complications\"},{\"value\":\"Inflammatory bowel disease complications\"},{\"value\":\"Bowel obstruction or perforation\"},{\"value\":\"Hemorrhoids, fistula, or other anorectal conditions\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Colorectal surgery treats diseases of the colon, rectum, and anus. Depending on the diagnosis, surgery may remove diseased bowel, relieve obstruction, or correct anorectal problems, often as part of a wider gastroenterology and oncology plan.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tColectomy \", \"description\": \"removal of part or all of colon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tProctectomy \", \"description\": \"removal of rectum.\"}, {\"name\": \"3.\\tColostomy/Ileostomy \", \"description\": \"opening created in abdomen for waste elimination.\"}, {\"name\": \"4.\\tPolypectomy\", \"description\": \"removal of polyps.\"}, {\"name\": \"5.\\tHemorrhoidectomy \", \"description\": \"removal of hemorrhoids.\"}, {\"name\": \"6.\\tFistula repair \", \"description\": \"closure of abnormal tract.\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Gradual diet advancement\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and early walking\"},{\"value\":\"Wound and drain care\"},{\"value\":\"Stoma education when applicable\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up for pathology and further treatment planning\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding or infection\"},{\"value\":\"Anastomotic leak after bowel joining\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary or permanent stoma in selected cases\"},{\"value\":\"Ileus or delayed bowel recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots or cardiorespiratory complications\"}]','<p>Colorectal surgery is highly effective. Cancer survival rates improve significantly with early surgery. Patients with IBD or diverticulitis experience relief from chronic symptoms. With modern laparoscopic and robotic techniques, recovery is faster and outcomes are excellent.</p>','<p>Colorectal surgery is a vital treatment for serious digestive conditions. It saves lives, restores bowel function, and improves quality of life. With proper diagnosis, surgical expertise, and follow-up care, patients can look forward to long-term health and well-being.</p>','Best & Top Colorectal Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Colorectal Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced colorectal procedures with expert surgeons and personalized care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 13:10:30','2026-07-29 00:15:56','Best & Top Colorectal Surgery in Bangalore'),(17,'Liver Surgery ','procedures/banners/70525f02-314f-4e8c-a0f2-ce630915b414.webp',NULL,'liver-surgery','<p>Liver Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from liver tumors, liver cancer, cysts, trauma, and other liver disorders. As a best hospital in Bangalore for gastrointestinal and hepatobiliary care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced liver surgery procedures using modern surgical techniques to ensure precise treatment, enhanced safety, and faster recovery. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help prevent serious complications, preserve</p><p>This article explains liver surgery comprehensively — what liver conditions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedures, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The liver can be affected by:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Primary liver cancer</strong> (hepatocellular carcinoma).</p></li><li><p><strong>Secondary liver cancer</strong> (metastasis from colon, breast, or lung).</p></li><li><p><strong>Benign tumors</strong> (hemangiomas, adenomas).</p></li><li><p><strong>Cysts or abscesses</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Trauma</strong> (accidents causing liver rupture).</p></li><li><p><strong>End-stage liver disease</strong> requiring transplantation.</p></li></ul>','[{\"value\":\"Pain or discomfort in the right upper abdomen\"},{\"value\":\"Jaundice or unexplained itching\"},{\"value\":\"Abdominal fullness from a liver mass\"},{\"value\":\"Loss of appetite or weight loss\"},{\"value\":\"Abnormal imaging or blood tests suggesting a liver lesion\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Liver tumors, benign or malignant\"},{\"value\":\"Metastatic disease involving the liver\"},{\"value\":\"Selected cystic or parasitic liver lesions\"},{\"value\":\"Trauma requiring operative control\"},{\"value\":\"Biliary obstruction related to liver pathology\"}]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Liver surgery removes diseased portions of the liver or treats complex lesions while preserving as much healthy liver tissue as possible. Careful imaging, liver-function assessment, and specialist planning guide whether resection or another approach is safest.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tLiver Resection (Hepatectomy)\", \"description\": \"Removal of part of the liver.Can be partial (segmental) or total (lobe).\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tLiver Transplantation\", \"description\": \"Diseased liver replaced with healthy donor liver.Used for end-stage liver disease or unresectable cancer.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"3.\\tAblation Techniques\", \"description\": \"Radiofrequency or microwave ablation to destroy tumors.\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Close monitoring of liver function and drains\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and breathing exercises\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual nutrition support\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and infection surveillance\"},{\"value\":\"Scheduled imaging and specialist follow-up\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Bile leak\"},{\"value\":\"Infection or abscess\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary liver dysfunction\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots or prolonged recovery in major resections\"}]','<p>Liver surgery is highly effective when performed for the right indications. Patients with benign disease recover fully. Cancer outcomes depend on stage and type, but surgery offers the best chance of cure. Transplantation provides new life for patients with end-stage disease.</p>','<p>Liver surgery is a complex but life-saving procedure. With modern techniques, anesthesia, and post-operative care, outcomes are excellent. Patients regain health, energy, and quality of life when surgery is combined with lifestyle changes and regular monitoring.</p>','Best & Top Liver Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Looking for the best and top Liver Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced liver procedures with expert surgeons and comprehensive care.',NULL,1,'2026-02-18 13:18:42','2026-07-29 00:15:56','Best & Top Liver Surgery in Bangalore'),(18,'Kidney Surgery ','procedures/banners/9cfbd737-9037-4282-bef0-2a7c0794672a.webp',NULL,'kidney-surgery','<p>Kidney surgery is one of the most common urological procedures worldwide, performed to treat <strong>kidney cancer, kidney stones, cysts, trauma, or end-stage kidney disease requiring transplantation</strong>. The kidneys are vital organs that filter waste, balance fluids, and regulate blood pressure. When they are damaged or diseased, surgery may be necessary to restore health or save life.</p><p>This article explains kidney surgery comprehensively — what kidney conditions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedures, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The kidneys can be affected by:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Kidney cancer</strong> (renal cell carcinoma).</p></li><li><p><strong>Kidney stones</strong> causing obstruction and infection.</p></li><li><p><strong>Polycystic kidney disease</strong> (multiple cysts).</p></li><li><p><strong>Trauma</strong> (accidents causing rupture).</p></li></ul><p><strong>End-stage renal disease</strong> requiring transplantation</p>','[\"Flank pain (side or back pain)\", \"Blood in urine (hematuria)\", \"Frequent urinary tract infections\", \"Swelling in legs and ankles\", \"Fatigue and weakness\", \"High blood pressure\", \"Unexplained weight loss (in cancer cases)\"]','[\"Genetics – family history of kidney disease\", \"Chronic hypertension\", \"Diabetes – leading cause of kidney failure\", \"Smoking – increases cancer risk\", \"Obesity\", \"Recurrent infections or stones\"]','[\"Kidney failure requiring dialysis\", \"Spread of cancer to other organs\", \"Severe infection and sepsis\", \"Chronic pain and disability\", \"Death in advanced cases\"]','[\"Maintain healthy blood pressure and blood sugar\", \"Drink adequate water to prevent stones\", \"Avoid smoking and alcohol\", \"Healthy diet low in salt and processed foods\", \"Regular kidney function tests for high-risk patients\"]','[\"Blood tests – kidney function (creatinine, urea).\", \"Urine tests – protein, blood, infection.\", \"Ultrasound – detects stones, cysts, tumors.\", \"CT/MRI scans – detailed imaging.\", \"Biopsy – confirms cancer or disease type.\"]','<p>Kidney surgery treats stones, cysts, tumors, obstruction, trauma, or advanced disease requiring removal or reconstruction. Approaches may be endoscopic, laparoscopic, or open depending on the condition, with the aim of preserving kidney function whenever safely possible.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tNephrectomy \", \"description\": \"removal of part or all of kidney.\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tPyelolithotomy / Nephrolithotomy \", \"description\": \"removal of kidney stones.\"}, {\"name\": \"3.\\tKidney Transplantation \", \"description\": \"diseased kidney replaced with healthy donor kidney.\"}]','[]','[\"Pain management with medications.\", \"Adequate hydration.\", \"Balanced diet low in salt and protein (if one kidney remains).\", \"Regular follow-up for kidney function tests.\", \"Counseling for transplant patients (immunosuppressive therapy).\"]','[\"Infection at surgical site\", \"Bleeding\", \"Injury to nearby organs\", \"Injury to nearby organs\", \"Rejection in transplant cases\"]','<p>Kidney surgery is highly effective. Patients with one healthy kidney can live normal lives. Transplantation offers new life for patients with end-stage disease. Cancer outcomes depend on stage, but surgery provides the best chance of cure.</p>','<p>Kidney surgery is a vital treatment for serious kidney conditions. With modern techniques, anesthesia, and post-operative care, outcomes are excellent. Patients regain health, independence, and quality of life when surgery is combined with lifestyle changes and regular monitoring.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-18 13:28:39','2026-07-29 00:15:56',NULL),(19,'Bladder Surgery ','procedures/banners/d562663a-9c97-4790-840a-0cf13e2a7733.webp',NULL,'bladder-surgery','<p>Bladder surgery is a common urological procedure performed to treat <strong>bladder cancer, bladder stones, congenital abnormalities, trauma, or severe urinary dysfunction</strong>. The bladder is a hollow organ that stores urine before it is excreted. When disease or damage affects its function, surgery may be necessary to restore health and quality of life.</p><p>This article explains bladder surgery comprehensively — what bladder conditions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedures, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The bladder can be affected by:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Bladder cancer</strong> – malignant growth in bladder lining.</p></li><li><p><strong>Bladder stones</strong> – mineral deposits causing obstruction.</p></li><li><p><strong>Congenital abnormalities</strong> – structural defects present at birth.</p></li><li><p><strong>Trauma</strong> – accidents causing bladder rupture.</p></li><li><p><strong>Neurogenic bladder</strong> – nerve damage affecting bladder control.</p></li></ul>','[\"Blood in urine (hematuria)\", \"Painful urination (dysuria)\", \"Frequent urination or urgency\", \"Difficulty emptying bladder\", \"Pelvic pain\", \"Incontinence (loss of bladder control)\"]','[\"Smoking – major risk factor for bladder cancer\", \"Chronic infections\", \"Radiation exposure\", \"Genetics\", \"Diet high in processed foods\", \"Neurological disorders (spinal cord injury, multiple sclerosis)\"]','[\"Cancer progression and spread\", \"Severe urinary obstruction\", \"Kidney damage due to back pressure\", \"Chronic pain and disability\", \"Life-threatening infection (urosepsis)\"]','[\"Avoid smoking\", \"Drink plenty of water\", \"Maintain good urinary hygiene\", \"Early treatment of infections\", \"Routine screening for high-risk patients\"]','[\"Urine tests – detect blood, infection, or cancer cells.\", \"Cystoscopy – camera inserted into bladder.\", \"Ultrasound / CT / MRI – imaging of bladder.\", \"Biopsy – confirms cancer.\", \"Urodynamic studies – assess bladder function\"]','<p></p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tTransurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor (TURBT)\", \"description\": \"Endoscopic removal of bladder tumor.\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tCystectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of part (partial cystectomy) or all bladder (radical cystectomy).\\nRadical cystectomy often combined with urinary diversion.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"3.\\tStone Removal\", \"description\": \"Endoscopic or open removal of bladder stones.\"}, {\"name\": \"Bladder Reconstruction / Augmentation\", \"description\": \"Enlarging bladder using intestinal tissue.\\nCreating new bladder (neobladder) after cystectomy.\\n\"}]','[]','[\"Pain management with medications.\", \"Catheter or stoma care.\", \"Balanced diet and hydration.\", \"Counseling for lifestyle changes (urinary diversion).\", \"Regular follow-up for cancer surveillance.\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Bleeding\", \"Urinary leakage\", \"Kidney damage\", \"Recurrence of cancer\", \"Emotional impact (body image, lifestyle changes)\"]','<p>Bladder surgery is highly effective. TURBT cures early-stage cancer, while cystectomy offers survival in advanced cases. Reconstruction techniques allow patients to live normal lives after bladder removal</p>','<p>Bladder surgery is a vital treatment for serious bladder conditions. With modern techniques, outcomes are excellent, and patients regain health, independence, and quality of life. Proper diagnosis, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation ensure the best results.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-18 13:35:34','2026-03-03 05:00:52',NULL),(20,'Pancreatic Surgery ','procedures/banners/e3ae5325-c520-4174-a9e9-534725736cbe.webp',NULL,'pancreatic-surgery','<p>Pancreatic surgery is one of the most challenging abdominal procedures, performed to treat <strong>pancreatic cancer, cysts, chronic pancreatitis, or trauma</strong>. The pancreas is a vital organ that produces digestive enzymes and hormones like insulin. Because of its deep location and critical functions, pancreatic surgery requires advanced expertise and careful post-operative care.</p><p>This article explains pancreatic surgery comprehensively — what pancreatic conditions are, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedures, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>','<p>The pancreas can be affected by:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Pancreatic cancer</strong> (adenocarcinoma, neuroendocrine tumors).</p></li><li><p><strong>Chronic pancreatitis</strong> – long-term inflammation causing pain and dysfunction.</p></li><li><p><strong>Pancreatic cysts or pseudocysts</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Trauma</strong> – accidents causing rupture.</p></li><li><p><strong>Congenital abnormalities</strong>.</p></li></ul>','[\"Persistent abdominal pain radiating to back\", \"Jaundice (yellowing of skin and eyes)\", \"Unexplained weight loss\", \"Loss of appetite\", \"Nausea and vomiting\", \"Fatigue and weakness\", \"Diabetes (if insulin production affected)\"]','[\"Smoking and alcohol abuse\", \"Chronic pancreatitis\", \"Genetic mutations (BRCA, Lynch syndrome)\", \"Obesity and poor diet\", \"Family history of pancreatic cancer\", \"Trauma or infections\"]','[\"Cancer progression and spread\", \"Severe pain and disability\", \"Malnutrition due to poor digestion\", \"Diabetes and metabolic complications\", \"Death in advanced cases\"]','[\"Avoid smoking and alcohol\", \"Healthy diet rich in fruits and vegetables\", \"Maintain healthy weight\", \"Regular screening for high-risk individuals\", \"Early treatment of pancreatitis\"]','[\"Blood tests – liver function, pancreatic enzymes, tumor markers (CA 19-9).\", \"Ultrasound / CT / MRI – imaging of pancreas.\", \"Endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) – detailed view and biopsy\", \"ERCP (Endoscopic Retrograde Cholangiopancreatography) – evaluates bile and pancreatic ducts.\", \"Biopsy – confirms cancer.\"]','<p></p>','[{\"name\": \"1.\\tWhipple Procedure (Pancreaticoduodenectomy)\", \"description\": \"Removes head of pancreas, part of stomach, duodenum, gallbladder, and bile duct.Most common for pancreatic cancer.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"2.\\tDistal Pancreatectomy\", \"description\": \"Removes body and tail of pancreas.Often includes spleen removal.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"3.\\tTotal Pancreatectomy\", \"description\": \"Removes entire pancreas.\\nPatient requires lifelong insulin and enzyme replacement.\\n\"}, {\"name\": \"4.\\tDrainage Procedures\", \"description\": \"For pseudocysts or chronic pancreatitis.\"}]','[]','[\"Pain management with medications.\", \"Nutritional support (enzyme supplements).\", \"Insulin therapy if diabetes develops.\", \"Regular follow-up for cancer surveillance.\", \"Counseling for lifestyle changes.\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Bleeding\", \"Leakage from surgical connections\", \"Diabetes (if pancreas removed)\", \"Malnutrition\", \"Recurrence of cancer\"]','<p>Pancreatic surgery is life-saving but complex. Outcomes depend on disease stage. For cancer, early surgery offers the best chance of survival. With enzyme and insulin replacement, patients can live healthy lives after partial or total removal.</p>','<p>Pancreatic surgery is a vital treatment for serious pancreatic conditions. With modern techniques, outcomes are improving, and patients regain health and quality of life. Proper diagnosis, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation are key to success.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-18 13:45:27','2026-03-03 05:02:12',NULL),(21,'Coronary Angiography','procedures/banners/6f08786d-e17d-4551-ac4e-ebdd971fd832.webp',NULL,'coronary-angiography','<p>Coronary angiography is a specialized diagnostic procedure used to examine the coronary arteries that supply blood to the heart muscle. It helps doctors identify blockages, narrowing, or abnormalities in these arteries that may lead to chest pain, heart attacks, or other cardiovascular complications. The procedure involves inserting a thin catheter into a blood vessel, usually through the wrist or groin, and guiding it toward the heart. A special contrast dye is then injected, and X-ray images are taken to clearly visualize the blood flow through the coronary arteries.</p>','<p>This test plays a critical role in diagnosing coronary artery disease and determining the most appropriate treatment options. By accurately identifying the location and severity of arterial blockages, cardiologists can decide whether medications, angioplasty, stent placement, or bypass surgery is required. Coronary angiography is considered a safe and widely used procedure in modern cardiology.</p>','[\"Chest pain or pressure (angina)\", \"Shortness of breath\", \"Fatigue during physical activity\", \"Irregular heartbeat\", \"Abnormal stress test results\"]','[\"Coronary artery disease\", \"Cholesterol plaque buildup in arteries\", \"High blood pressure\", \"Diabetes\", \"Smoking and unhealthy lifestyle\"]','[\"Bleeding or bruising at the catheter site\", \"Allergic reaction to contrast dye\", \"Blood vessel damage\", \"Irregular heartbeat\", \"Infection\"]','[]','[]','<p></p>','[{\"name\": \"Radial Angiography\", \"description\": \"Catheter inserted through the wrist (radial artery).\"}, {\"name\": \"Femoral Angiography\", \"description\": \"Catheter inserted through the groin (femoral artery).\"}, {\"name\": \"CT Coronary Angiography (CTCA)\", \"description\": \"Non-invasive scan using CT imaging and contrast dye to visualize coronary arteries\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the insertion site clean and dry.\", \"Avoid heavy lifting and strenuous activity for a few days.\", \"Drink plenty of fluids to flush out the contrast dye.\", \"Monitor for bleeding, swelling, or redness at the catheter site.\", \"Take prescribed medications as advised by the doctor.\"]','[\"Bleeding or bruising at the catheter site\", \"Allergic reaction to contrast dye\", \"Blood vessel damage\", \"Irregular heartbeat\", \"Infection\"]','<p></p>','<p>Coronary angiography plays a crucial role in detecting heart disease at an early stage and preventing serious complications such as heart attacks. Once blockages are identified, doctors can begin appropriate treatment to restore healthy blood flow to the heart. Patients who follow medical advice, take prescribed medications, and adopt heart-healthy habits often experience improved heart function and quality of life.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-14 09:01:42','2026-03-16 05:44:15',NULL),(22,'Coronary Angioplasty ','procedures/banners/e03b4ce1-e0e3-4db0-b455-8e6ef6edebaf.webp',NULL,'coronary-angioplasty','<p>Coronary angioplasty is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat narrowed or blocked coronary arteries that restrict blood flow to the heart muscle. The procedure involves inserting a thin catheter with a small balloon at its tip into the affected artery. Once positioned at the blockage site, the balloon is inflated to widen the artery and improve blood flow. In most cases, a small mesh tube called a stent is placed inside the artery to keep it open permanently.</p>','<p>Angioplasty is commonly recommended for patients with coronary artery disease who experience chest pain or are at risk of heart attacks. The procedure significantly improves circulation, reduces symptoms, and prevents further complications. It is widely considered an effective treatment for restoring proper heart function.</p>','[\"Chest pain or pressure\", \"Shortness of breath\", \"Fatigue during activity\", \"Heart attack symptoms\"]','[\"Coronary artery disease\", \"Cholesterol buildup in arteries\", \"High blood pressure\", \"Diabetes and smoking\"]','[\"Blood clot formation in the stent\", \"Bleeding at catheter site\", \"Rare artery damage\"]','[]','[]','<p>Balloon angioplasty is performed to widen the blocked artery. A stent is then placed to keep the artery open and ensure proper blood flow.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Balloon Angioplasty\", \"description\": \"A small balloon is inflated to open the blocked artery.\"}, {\"name\": \"Stent Placement Angioplasty\", \"description\": \"A mesh stent is placed to keep the artery open.\"}, {\"name\": \"Drug-Eluting Stent (DES) Angioplast\", \"description\": \"A stent coated with medication to prevent re-narrowing.\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the catheter insertion area clean and dry\", \"Avoid heavy lifting or strenuous activity for a few days\", \"Take prescribed medications (especially blood thinners) regularly\", \"Drink plenty of fluids to flush out the contrast dye\", \"Monitor for swelling, bleeding, or redness at the insertion site\"]','[\"Blood clot formation in the stent\", \"Bleeding at catheter site\", \"Rare artery damage\"]','<p></p>','<p>Coronary angioplasty significantly improves blood flow to the heart and relieves symptoms such as chest pain and breathlessness. Most patients notice an immediate improvement in their ability to perform daily activities. Long-term success depends on following prescribed medications, particularly blood thinners, and maintaining healthy lifestyle habits.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-14 09:54:00','2026-03-16 05:41:52',NULL),(23,'Dialysis Treatment ','procedures/banners/353deb13-e60f-4886-93dc-d1e16c8f2620.webp',NULL,'dialysis-treatment','<p>Dialysis is a life-saving treatment for individuals whose kidneys have lost the ability to properly filter waste products and excess fluids from the blood. Hemodialysis is the most common type of dialysis, where blood is passed through a special filter called a dialyzer that removes toxins and excess water before returning the purified blood to the body.</p>','<p>Dialysis helps maintain a balance of essential minerals such as potassium and sodium in the blood and prevents the buildup of harmful waste substances. It is commonly used for patients with advanced chronic kidney disease or kidney failure. While dialysis does not cure kidney disease, it plays a vital role in supporting the body&#039;s functions and improving patient survival.</p>','[\"Chest pain or pressure\", \"Shortness of breath\", \"Fatigue during activity\", \"Heart attack symptoms\"]','[\"Swelling in legs and ankles\", \"Fatigue and weakness\", \"Reduced urine output\", \"Shortness of breath\"]','[\"Low blood pressure\", \"Muscle cramps\", \"Infection at access site\"]','[]','[]','<p>Hemodialysis sessions are typically performed two to three times per week using specialized dialysis machines under medical supervision.</p>','[{\"name\": \"In-Center Hemodialysis\", \"description\": \"Performed at a hospital or dialysis center.\"}, {\"name\": \"Home Hemodialysis\", \"description\": \"Nocturnal Hemodialys\"}, {\"name\": \"Short Daily Hemodialysis\", \"description\": \"More frequent but shorter dialysis sessions.\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the dialysis access site clean and dry\", \"Avoid heavy lifting with the access arm\", \"Follow the recommended diet and fluid restrictions\", \"Take prescribed medications regularly\", \"Monitor the access site for redness, swelling, or pain\"]','[\"Low blood pressure during dialysis\", \"Muscle cramps\", \"Infection at the access site\"]','<p>Dialysis helps patients maintain stable health when kidney function is severely reduced. With regular dialysis sessions and proper medical care, many individuals can continue their daily routines and live for many years.</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-14 10:11:38','2026-03-16 05:39:43',NULL),(24,'Kidney Stone Laser Surgery ','procedures/banners/444c1a3f-0ebf-4b41-be18-d240da0da983.webp',NULL,'kidney-stone-laser-surgery','<p>Kidney stone laser surgery is a minimally invasive procedure used to remove stones from the urinary tract. The procedure involves inserting a thin flexible scope through the urethra into the urinary system to locate the stone. A laser is then used to break the stone into tiny fragments that can be removed or passed naturally through urine.</p>','<p>This advanced technique allows doctors to treat kidney stones without making large surgical incisions. It is considered highly effective and provides quick relief from severe pain and urinary obstruction caused by stones.</p>','[\"Severe pain in the lower back or side\", \"Painful urination\", \"Blood in urine\", \"Nausea and vomiting\"]','[\"Dehydration\", \"High mineral concentration in urine\", \"High salt diet\", \"Genetic factors\", \"Blood in urine for a short time\"]','[\"Bleeding\", \"Urinary tract infection\", \"Injury to the ureter or kidney\", \"Pain or burning during urination\"]','[]','[]','<p>Laser lithotripsy is performed to break the stones into smaller fragments using specialized instruments.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Ureteroscopy with Laser Lithotripsy\", \"description\": \"Laser used through a scope to break stones in the ureter or kidney\"}, {\"name\": \"Flexible Ureteroscopy (FURS\", \"description\": \"Flexible scope used to reach and treat stones inside the kidney\"}]','[{\"stage\": \"Retrograde Intrarenal Surgery (RIRS)\", \"details\": \"Laser treatment for kidney stones using a flexible ureteroscope without external incision\"}]','[\"Drink plenty of water to help flush out stone fragments\", \"Take prescribed antibiotics and pain medications\", \"Avoid heavy physical activity for a few days\", \"Monitor for fever, severe pain, or difficulty urinating\", \"Follow the doctor’s diet advice to prevent future stones\"]','[\"Urinary tract infection\", \"Injury to the ureter or kidney\", \"Pain or burning during urination\", \"Blood in urine for a short time\", \"Rarely blockage of the ureter\"]','<p>Dialysis helps patients maintain stable health when kidney function is severely reduced. With regular dialysis sessions and proper medical care, many individuals can continue their daily routines and live for many years.</p><p>Following a kidney-friendly diet, controlling fluid intake, and taking prescribed medications are essential for long-term health. Regular medical monitoring helps manage complications and maintain overall well-being. In some cases, dialysis may serve as a temporary treatment until a kidney transplant becomes available.</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-14 10:40:07','2026-03-16 05:41:20',NULL),(25,'Gallbladder Stone Removal Surgery','procedures/banners/2c4ac9f9-3a83-4e93-983a-caaab20fe05a.webp',NULL,'gallbladder-stone-removal-surgery','<p>Gallbladder stone removal surgery, known as cholecystectomy, is performed to treat gallstones that cause pain, infection, or digestive problems. Gallstones are hardened deposits that form in the gallbladder and may block the flow of bile, leading to severe abdominal discomfort.</p>','<p>Today, most gallbladder surgeries are performed using laparoscopic techniques, which involve small incisions and specialized surgical instruments. This approach reduces pain, shortens hospital stay, and allows faster recovery compared to traditional surgery.</p>','[\"Severe pain in upper abdomen\", \"Nausea and vomiting\", \"Indigestion after fatty meals\", \"Fever in case of infection\"]','[\"High cholesterol in bile\", \"Obesity\", \"Hormonal changes\", \"Poor diet\"]','[\"Bleeding\", \"Infection\", \"Injury to nearby organs\", \"Bile leakage\", \"Blood clots\"]','[]','[]','<p>Laparoscopic surgery is performed to remove the gallbladder and eliminate gallstones.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Laparoscopic Cholecystectomy\", \"description\": \"Minimally invasive surgery using small incisions to remove the gallbladder\"}, {\"name\": \"Open Cholecystectomy\", \"description\": \"Traditional surgery with a larger incision to remove the gallbladder\"}, {\"name\": \"ERCP (Endoscopic Retrograde Cholangiopancreatography\", \"description\": \"Endoscopic procedure used to remove stones from the bile duct if present\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Avoid heavy lifting for a few weeks\", \"Follow a light, low-fat diet initially\", \"Take prescribed medications as directed\", \"Walk gently to improve circulation\"]','[]','<p>Gallbladder removal surgery permanently eliminates the risk of gallstone attacks and related complications. After surgery, the body gradually adapts to digesting food without the gallbladder. Most patients experience complete relief from abdominal pain and digestive discomfort. Maintaining a balanced diet and healthy lifestyle helps support digestion and overall well-being. In the long term, patients can live normal and active lives without major dietary restrictions.</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-14 10:59:19','2026-03-16 05:40:54',NULL),(26,'Varicose Vein Laser Treatment','procedures/banners/53070611-fe1a-4348-af74-49bf823f171c.webp',NULL,'varicose-vein-laser-treatment','<p>Varicose veins are enlarged, twisted veins that usually appear in the legs due to poor blood circulation. They occur when vein valves become weak, causing blood to pool in the veins. This condition may lead to pain, swelling, heaviness in the legs, and cosmetic concerns.</p>','<p>Laser treatment for varicose veins is a minimally invasive procedure that uses laser energy to close the affected veins. Once closed, blood flow is redirected to healthy veins, improving circulation and reducing symptoms.</p>','[\"Visible enlarged veins\", \"Leg pain or heaviness\", \"Swelling in legs\", \"Burning or throbbing sensation\"]','[\"Weak vein valves\", \"Prolonged standing\", \"Obesity\", \"Pregnancy\"]','[\"Mild bruising\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Skin irritation\"]','[]','[]','<p>Laser energy is used to seal the damaged veins, allowing blood to flow through healthy veins.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Endovenous Laser Treatment (EVLT)\", \"description\": \"Laser fiber inserted into the vein to close it from inside\"}, {\"name\": \"Surface Laser Treatment\", \"description\": \"Laser applied on the skin surface to treat small varicose veins and spider veins\"}]','[]','[\"Wear compression stockings as advised\", \"Walk regularly to improve blood circulation\", \"Avoid prolonged standing or sitting\"]','[\"Mild bruising\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Skin irritation\"]','<p>Laser treatment for varicose veins offers effective long-term improvement in circulation and leg comfort. Patients often notice reduced swelling, pain, and heaviness after treatment. The treated veins gradually fade while blood flow is redirected to healthy veins. Although treated veins do not return, maintaining a healthy weight and staying active can help prevent new varicose veins from developing. With proper lifestyle care, patients enjoy lasting relief and improved leg health</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-14 11:22:59','2026-03-16 05:38:30',NULL),(27,'Thyroid Surgery','procedures/banners/19aa3988-1fbb-4693-9f79-3288b13632e4.webp',NULL,'thyroid-surgery','<p>Thyroid surgery is performed to remove part or all of the thyroid gland to treat conditions<br>such as thyroid nodules, goiter, hyperthyroidism, or thyroid cancer. The thyroid gland plays a<br>vital role in regulating metabolism, energy levels, and hormone balance in the body.<br></p>','<p>Surgery is recommended when the thyroid gland becomes enlarged, causes breathing or<br>swallowing difficulties, or when cancer is suspected. Modern surgical techniques ensure safe<br>and effective treatment with minimal complications.</p>','[\"Lump or swelling in the neck\", \"Difficulty swallowing\", \"Hoarseness of voice\", \"Hormonal imbalance symptoms\"]','[\"Thyroid nodules\", \"Goiter\", \"Thyroid cancer\", \"Hyperthyroidism\"]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Partial or complete removal of the thyroid gland depending on the medical condition.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Total Thyroidectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of the entire thyroid gland\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Thyroidectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of one lobe of the thyroid\"}, {\"name\": \"Subtotal Thyroidectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of most of the thyroid gland\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the surgical incision clean and dry\", \"Avoid strenuous activities for a few weeks\", \"Monitor for swelling, pain, or signs of infection\", \"Attend regular follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Injury to vocal cord nerves (voice changes)\", \"Low calcium levels due to parathyroid gland damage\", \"Difficulty swallowing\", \"Scar formation\"]','<p>Thyroid surgery provides effective treatment for various thyroid disorders and improves overall health. Most patients return to normal daily activities after recovery. If the entire thyroid gland is removed, hormone replacement therapy may be required to maintain normal metabolism. Regular medical monitoring ensures balanced hormone levels and prevents complications. With proper treatment and follow-up care, patients can maintain a healthy and active lifestyle.</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 06:56:09','2026-03-16 06:56:32',NULL),(28,'Breast Lump Removal Surgery','procedures/banners/9858cd38-c0e1-44a0-ab1f-084d70064ab8.webp',NULL,'breast-lump-removal-surgery','<p>Breast lump removal surgery is performed to remove abnormal lumps or growths in the breast tissue. While many breast lumps are non-cancerous, it is important to evaluate and remove suspicious lumps to confirm their nature and prevent possible complications. During the procedure, the surgeon carefully removes the lump and may send the tissue for laboratory examination to determine whether it is benign or malignant.</p>','<p>Modern surgical techniques focus on preserving healthy breast tissue while effectively removing the abnormal growth. Early diagnosis and timely surgical treatment play an important role in maintaining breast health and preventing serious conditions.</p>','[\"Lump or thickening in the breast\", \"Breast pain or tenderness\", \"Changes in breast shape\", \"Skin changes around the breast\"]','[\"Hormonal changes\", \"Breast cysts\", \"Benign tumors\", \"Breast cancer\"]','[]','[]','[]','<p>Surgical removal of the lump followed by laboratory analysis to determine its nature.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Lumpectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of the lump along with a small margin of surrounding tissue\"}, {\"name\": \"Excisional Biopsy\", \"description\": \"Surgical removal of the lump for detailed examinatio\"}, {\"name\": \"Wide Local Excision\", \"description\": \"Removal of the lump with a larger area of surrounding tissue to ensure complete remova\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Avoid heavy lifting or strenuous activity for a few days\", \"Wear a supportive bra as advised\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain or infection\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Bleeding\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Scarring\"]','<p>Breast lump removal surgery provides both diagnostic and therapeutic benefits. In many cases, the lump is benign, giving reassurance and peace of mind to patients. If cancer is detected early, timely treatment significantly improves survival and recovery rates. Regular breast examinations and medical screenings are important for maintaining long-term breast health. With proper follow-up care and healthy lifestyle practices, most patients recover fully and continue normal daily activities without complications.</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 07:01:15','2026-03-16 07:01:15',NULL),(29,'Piles Surgery ','procedures/banners/260511e5-c984-4ff9-a710-62ed9e660eb7.webp',NULL,'piles-surgery','<p>Piles, also known as hemorrhoids, are swollen veins in the rectal area that can cause pain, bleeding, and discomfort during bowel movements. Piles surgery is recommended when conservative treatments such as medication and lifestyle changes fail to provide relief. Modern procedures such as laser piles surgery offer effective treatment with minimal pain and faster recovery.</p>','<p></p>','[\"Rectal bleeding during bowel movements\", \"Pain or itching around the anus\", \"Swelling near the anal region\", \"Discomfort while sitting\"]','[\"Chronic constipation\", \"Straining during bowel movements\", \"Prolonged sitting\", \"Low-fiber diet\"]','[\"Mild bleeding\", \"Infection\", \"Temporary discomfort\"]','[]','[]','<p>Surgical removal of hemorrhoids or laser therapy to shrink swollen veins.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Hemorrhoidectomy\", \"description\": \"Surgical removal of hemorrhoids\"}, {\"name\": \"Stapled Hemorrhoidopexy\", \"description\": \"Stapling technique to reposition hemorrhoids\"}, {\"name\": \"Laser Hemorrhoidoplasty\", \"description\": \"Laser used to shrink hemorrhoids\"}]','[]','[\"Eat a high-fiber diet to prevent constipation\", \"Drink plenty of water\", \"Take prescribed pain relief and stool softeners\", \"Maintain proper anal hygiene\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Pain during bowel movements\", \"Anal swelling\", \"Recurrence of hemorrhoids\"]','<p>Piles surgery provides long-lasting relief from the pain and discomfort associated with hemorrhoids. Modern techniques such as laser treatment allow faster healing and minimal complications. After surgery, adopting healthy bowel habits plays an important role in preventing recurrence. A diet rich in fiber, adequate hydration, and regular physical activity help maintain healthy digestion. With proper lifestyle changes, patients can enjoy long-term comfort and improved quality of life.</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 07:06:14','2026-03-16 07:06:14',NULL),(30,'Fistula Surgery','procedures/banners/4b39172d-9b9c-4763-81da-76ddf1ee6f8b.webp',NULL,'fistula-surgery','<p>An anal fistula is an abnormal tunnel that forms between the anal canal and the skin near the anus. It usually develops after an infection or abscess in the anal glands. Fistula surgery is performed to remove the infected tract and prevent recurrent infections or discomfort.</p>','<p></p>','[\"Pain near the anal region\", \"Swelling or redness\", \"Pus or discharge\", \"Irritation around the anus\"]','[\"Anal gland infection\", \"Previous abscess formation\", \"Crohn’s disease\", \"Chronic inflammation\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Recurrence of fistula\", \"Mild bleeding\"]','[]','[]','<p>Surgical removal or closure of the fistula tract.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Fistulotomy\", \"description\": \"Opening the fistula tract to allow healing\"}, {\"name\": \"Seton Placement\", \"description\": \"A surgical thread placed to help drain the fistula\"}, {\"name\": \"Advancement Flap Surgery\", \"description\": \"Tissue flap used to close the internal opening\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the anal area clean and dry\", \"Take prescribed antibiotics and pain medications\", \"Take warm sitz baths to reduce pain and promote healing\", \"Eat a high-fiber diet to prevent constipation\"]','[\"Pain or discomfort\", \"Recurrence of fistula\", \"Delay in wound healing\", \"Infection\"]','<p>Fistula surgery is highly effective in eliminating the abnormal tract and preventing recurrent infections. Most patients experience complete relief from symptoms after proper surgical treatment. Maintaining good hygiene and attending follow-up visits are important for successful healing. Early treatment also prevents complications such as repeated abscess formation. With proper care, patients can return to normal activities and maintain good anal health</p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 08:29:38','2026-03-16 08:29:38',NULL),(31,'Diabetic Foot Treatment ','procedures/banners/185aaeb7-c83d-4591-b28d-00a3dcc73288.webp',NULL,'diabetic-foot-treatment','<p>Diabetic foot treatment addresses infections, ulcers, or tissue damage that occur due to poor circulation and nerve damage in people with diabetes. Early medical care is essential to prevent serious complications.</p>','<p>nerve damage in people with diabetes. Early medical care is essential to prevent serious complications.</p>','[\"Foot ulcers\", \"Numbness or tingling\", \"Swelling or redness\", \"Slow wound healing\"]','[\"Poor blood circulation\", \"Nerve damage from diabetes\", \"Uncontrolled blood sugar levels\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Tissue damage\", \"Risk of amputation in severe cases\"]','[]','[]','<p>Treatment may include wound care, infection control, or surgery if necessary.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Wound Debridement\", \"description\": \"Removal of dead or infected tissue\"}, {\"name\": \"Antibiotic Therapy\", \"description\": \"Treatment to control infection\"}, {\"name\": \"Vascular Treatment\", \"description\": \"Procedures to improve blood flow\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the wound clean and properly dressed\", \"Maintain good blood sugar control\", \"Avoid pressure on the affected foot\", \"Wear proper diabetic footwear\"]','[\"Infection of the wound\", \"Delayed wound healing\", \"Tissue damage or ulcers\"]','<p>Proper treatment and preventive care can significantly reduce the risk of serious diabetic foot complications. Maintaining good blood sugar control is essential for long-term healing and prevention.</p>','<p>Regular foot examinations help detect problems early before they become severe. Wearing protective footwear and maintaining foot hygiene are also important. With proper care and monitoring, patients can maintain mobility and prevent major complications.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 10:13:28','2026-03-16 10:13:28',NULL),(32,'Trauma & Fracture Surgery','procedures/banners/a4832516-8c19-40af-9b73-b9de40bd35de.webp',NULL,'trauma-fracture-surgery','<p>Trauma and fracture surgery is performed to treat broken bones and injuries caused by accidents, falls, or sports injuries</p>','<p>The goal is to restore normal bone alignment and function.</p>','[\"Severe pain at injury site\", \"Swelling or bruising\", \"Inability to move the affected limb\", \"Visible bone deformity\"]','[\"Road accidents\", \"Falls or sports injuries\", \"High-impact trauma\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Delayed bone healing\", \"Implant irritation\"]','[]','[]','<p>Surgical fixation using plates, rods, or screws to stabilize the bone.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Open Reduction and Internal Fixation\", \"description\": \"Bones are realigned and fixed with plates, screws, or rods\"}, {\"name\": \"External Fixation\", \"description\": \"Metal pins and rods placed outside the body to stabilize the bone\"}, {\"name\": \"Intramedullary Nailing\", \"description\": \"A metal rod inserted inside the bone to hold it in place\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Follow the doctor’s instructions for rest and movement\", \"Take prescribed pain medications and antibiotics\", \"Attend physiotherapy for proper recovery\"]','[\"Bleeding\", \"Blood clots\", \"Delayed or improper bone healing\", \"Implant or hardware problems\"]','<p>Trauma and fracture surgery helps restore bone structure and mobility after serious injuries. With proper treatment and rehabilitation, most fractures heal successfully. Physiotherapy plays a crucial role in strengthening muscles and restoring joint movement.</p>','<p>Patients who follow recovery programs usually regain their normal physical activities. Long-term outcomes are generally excellent when proper medical care and rehabilitation are followed.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 10:19:42','2026-03-16 10:20:14',NULL),(33,'Minimally Invasive Spine Surgery','procedures/banners/6aadf413-5170-42df-a4f4-c525dd1a3c8a.webp',NULL,'minimally-invasive-spine-surgery','<p>Minimally invasive spine surgery is used to treat spinal conditions such as herniated discs, spinal stenosis, and chronic back pain.</p>','<p>The procedure uses small incisions and specialized instruments to reduce tissue damage.</p>','[\"Chronic back pain\", \"Numbness in legs\", \"Tingling or weakness\", \"Difficulty walking\"]','[\"Herniated disc\", \"Spinal degeneration\", \"Injury to spine\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Nerve irritation\", \"Bleeding\"]','[]','[]','<p>Small-incision surgical techniques relieve pressure on nerves and stabilize the spine.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Microdiscectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of a herniated disc pressing on a nerve\"}, {\"name\": \"Minimally Invasive Laminectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of a small part of bone to relieve pressure on the spinal cord\"}, {\"name\": \"Minimally Invasive Spinal Fusion\", \"description\": \"Joining two or more vertebrae to stabilize the spine\"}]','[]','[\"Avoid heavy lifting and strenuous activities\", \"Follow physiotherapy exercises as advised\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain and inflammation\", \"Maintain proper posture while sitting and walking\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Nerve irritation\", \"Bleeding\"]','<p>Minimally invasive spine surgery provides significant relief from chronic back pain and nerve compression. Because the procedure involves smaller incisions, recovery is faster and postoperative discomfort is reduced.</p>','<p>Many patients regain mobility and return to normal daily activities sooner. Regular physiotherapy and maintaining good posture help support spinal health. With proper care and lifestyle adjustments, patients can enjoy long-term improvement in mobility and quality of life.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 10:27:55','2026-03-16 10:27:55',NULL),(34,'Laparoscopic Appendix Surgery','procedures/banners/f9718fa6-91ec-4934-b206-803409114c8f.webp',NULL,'laparoscopic-appendix-surgery','<p>Laparoscopic appendix surgery, also called appendectomy, is performed to remove an inflamed appendix in cases of appendicitis.</p>','<p>The procedure uses small incisions and a camera to safely remove the appendix.</p>','[\"Severe pain in lower right abdomen\", \"Fever\", \"Nausea and vomiting\", \"Loss of appetite\"]','[\"Blockage of appendix\", \"Infection or inflammation\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Bleeding\", \"Rare complications\"]','[]','[]','<p>Laparoscopic removal of the appendix.</p>','[{\"name\": \"Laparoscopic Appendectomy\", \"description\": \"Minimally invasive surgery using small incisions and a camera to remove the appendix\"}, {\"name\": \"Open Appendectomy\", \"description\": \"Traditional surgery with a larger incision to remove the appendix\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the incision sites clean and dry\", \"Avoid heavy lifting for a few weeks\", \"Take prescribed antibiotics and pain medications\"]','[\"Bleeding\", \"Infection\", \"Reaction to anesthesia\"]','<p>Appendix removal surgery permanently treats appendicitis and prevents future attacks. Since the appendix does not play a vital role in digestion, the body functions normally without it. Most patients recover quickly and return to their daily routines without restrictions.</p>','<p>Maintaining general health and attending follow-up visits ensures smooth recovery. Long-term outcomes are excellent, and patients typically experience no lasting complications after the procedure.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 10:32:59','2026-03-16 10:32:59',NULL),(35,'IVF Treatment (In Vitro Fertilization)','procedures/banners/f1570b04-702d-444d-bcf5-78c6937ae973.webp',NULL,'in-vitro-fertilization','<p>In Vitro Fertilization (IVF) is an advanced fertility treatment that helps couples who are unable to conceive naturally. In this procedure, the egg and sperm are fertilized outside the body in a specialized laboratory, and the resulting embryo is transferred into the uterus.</p>','<p>IVF is widely used to treat different types of infertility and has helped many couples achieve successful pregnancies. Modern fertility technologies and expert medical care have significantly improved the success rates of IVF treatment.</p>','[\"Difficulty conceiving for a long period\", \"Irregular ovulation\", \"Repeated miscarriages\", \"Male infertility issues\"]','[\"Ovulation disorders such as PCOS\", \"Endometriosis\", \"Low sperm count or poor sperm quality\", \"Age-related fertility decline\"]','[]','[]','[]','<p>IVF treatment involves stimulating the ovaries to produce eggs, retrieving the eggs, fertilizing them with sperm in a laboratory</p>','[{\"name\": \"Conventional IVF\", \"description\": \"Eggs and sperm combined in a laboratory to form embryos\"}, {\"name\": \"ICSI (Intracytoplasmic Sperm Injection)\", \"description\": \"A single sperm injected directly into an egg\"}, {\"name\": \"Frozen Embryo Transfer (FET)\", \"description\": \"Previously frozen embryos transferred to the uterus\"}]','[]','[\"Take prescribed fertility medications as directed\", \"Avoid strenuous physical activity\", \"Maintain a healthy diet and proper hydration\", \"Avoid smoking, alcohol, and stress\"]','[\"Ectopic pregnancy\", \"Bleeding or infection during egg retrieval\", \"Emotional stress and hormonal side effects\", \"Rare complications from anesthesia\"]','<p>IVF treatment has helped many couples overcome infertility and achieve successful pregnancies. Advances in reproductive medicine continue to improve the safety and success of this procedure. The long-term outlook depends on factors such as age, overall health, and the cause of infertility.</p>','<p>With proper medical care and guidance from fertility specialists, many couples are able to fulfill their dream of parenthood. Even if the first cycle is not successful, additional IVF attempts may increase the chances of pregnancy.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-16 10:39:06','2026-03-16 10:39:06',NULL),(38,'Total Knee Replacement (TKR)','procedures/banners/57b30862-6135-41f3-99fe-f87e41c64d50.webp',NULL,'total-knee-replacement-tkr','<p>Total Knee Replacement is a surgical procedure performed to replace a damaged knee joint with an artificial implant. It is commonly recommended for patients with severe arthritis or knee damage that causes chronic pain and difficulty in movement.</p>','<p>Total Knee Replacement is a procedure where the damaged parts of the knee joint are removed and replaced with artificial components to restore joint function and relieve pain.</p>','[\"Severe knee pain\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Difficulty walking or climbing stairs\", \"Swelling around the knee\"]','[\"Osteoarthritis\", \"Rheumatoid arthritis\", \"Knee injury or trauma\", \"Degenerative joint disease\"]','[\"Obesity\", \"Advanced age\", \"Previous knee injuries\", \"Genetic joint disorders\"]','[\"Maintain a healthy weight\", \"Exercise regularly to strengthen knee muscles\", \"Avoid excessive strain on knee joints\", \"Treat knee injuries early\"]','[\"Physical examination\", \"X-ray imaging of the knee\", \"MRI scan for detailed joint evaluation\", \"Blood tests for inflammatory arthritis\"]','<p>When medications and physiotherapy fail to relieve chronic knee pain, Total Knee Replacement surgery may be recommended. The damaged cartilage and bone are removed and replaced with artificial implants that restore joint movement and reduce pain.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Traditional Total Knee Replacement\", \"description\": \"The entire knee joint surface is replaced with artificial metal and plastic components to restore function and relieve pain.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Minimally Invasive Knee Replacement\", \"description\": \"A smaller surgical incision is used which may reduce tissue damage and speed up recovery.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Partial Knee Replacement\", \"description\": \"Only the damaged portion of the knee joint is replaced instead of the entire joint.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Computer-Assisted Knee Replacement\", \"description\": \"Advanced navigation systems help surgeons position implants more accurately.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Take prescribed medications as directed\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Attend follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Blood clots\", \"Implant loosening or wear\", \"Nerve damage (rare)\"]','<p>Total knee replacement significantly improves mobility and quality of life for most patients. With proper rehabilitation and physiotherapy, patients can return to daily activities with minimal pain. Modern implants are designed to last many years and allow improved joint function. Maintaining a healthy weight and staying active can help prolong the lifespan of the implant.</p>','<p>Total Knee Replacement surgery is one of the most successful orthopedic procedures. With proper rehabilitation and follow-up care, most patients regain mobility and experience significant pain relief.</p>','Total Knee Replacement Surgery | Nano hospitals','Learn about Total Knee Replacement surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment, surgery types, recovery timeline and risks.','total knee replacement, knee replacement surgery, TKR surgery, knee arthritis treatment',1,'2026-03-17 07:31:48','2026-03-19 10:04:17',NULL),(39,'Total Hip Replacement (THR)','procedures/banners/72e0f77d-ae20-4ea5-971e-6312eb94f851.webp',NULL,'total-hip-replacement','<p>Total Hip Replacement is a surgical procedure used to replace a damaged hip joint with an artificial implant. It is commonly performed when severe hip pain and stiffness interfere with daily activities.</p>','<p>Total Hip Replacement is a procedure in which the damaged parts of the hip joint are removed and replaced with artificial components to restore joint movement and relieve pain.</p>','[\"Hip pain during movement\", \"Difficulty walking\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Reduced range of motion\"]','[\"Osteoarthritis\", \"Hip fractures\", \"Rheumatoid arthritis\", \"Degenerative joint conditions\"]','[\"Advanced age\", \"Obesity\", \"Previous hip injuries\", \"Family history of joint disorders\"]','[\"Maintain a healthy weight\", \"Regular physical activity to strengthen hip muscles\", \"Avoid repetitive stress on hip joints\", \"Early treatment of joint injuries\"]','[\"Physical examination\", \"X-ray imaging of the hip joint\", \"MRI scan for detailed joint evaluation\", \"Blood tests to rule out inflammatory arthritis\"]','<p>Total Hip Replacement surgery removes the damaged hip joint and replaces it with a prosthetic implant made of metal, ceramic, or plastic. This procedure helps restore joint function, relieve pain, and improve mobility when other treatments such as medications or physiotherapy are not effective.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Traditional Total Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"The damaged hip joint is removed and replaced with a prosthetic ball-and-socket implant.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Minimally Invasive Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"A smaller surgical incision is used which may reduce tissue damage and promote faster recovery.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Posterior Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"A commonly used surgical approach where the hip joint is accessed from the back of the hip.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Anterior Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"A modern surgical approach where the hip joint is accessed from the front, often allowing quicker recovery.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid bending the hip beyond recommended limits\", \"Take prescribed medications and pain relievers\", \"Keep the surgical site clean and dry\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Blood clots\", \"Dislocation of the implant\", \"Nerve damage (rare)\"]','<p>Hip replacement surgery provides long-lasting relief from chronic hip pain and stiffness. Most patients experience significant improvement in mobility and overall quality of life. With proper rehabilitation and healthy lifestyle habits, artificial hip joints can last many years. Regular follow-ups help monitor implant function. Patients can return to normal daily activities with improved comfort and movement.</p>','<p>Total Hip Replacement is one of the most effective treatments for severe hip joint damage. With modern surgical techniques and proper rehabilitation, patients can regain mobility and enjoy an active, pain-free life.</p>','Total Hip Replacement Surgery: Procedure & Recovery | Nano H','Regain your mobility with Total Hip Replacement at Nano Hospital. Learn about advanced surgical techniques, recovery timelines.','total hip replacement, hip arthroplasty, hip surgery, chronic hip pain treatment, anterior hip replacement, Nano Hospital orthopedics',1,'2026-03-17 07:35:11','2026-04-13 11:28:03',NULL),(41,'Hip Resurfacing','procedures/banners/e741bd05-985b-479e-a582-652406ac2691.webp',NULL,'hip-resurfacing','<p>Hip resurfacing is a bone-preserving surgical procedure used to treat hip joint damage. Instead of replacing the entire joint, the damaged surfaces are reshaped and covered with a metal implant.</p>','<p>Hip resurfacing is an orthopedic surgical procedure where the damaged surfaces of the hip joint are reshaped and covered with a metal prosthetic cap. Unlike total hip replacement, this procedure preserves more of the patient’s natural bone and is often recommended for younger or active individuals with hip joint damage.</p>','[\"Hip pain\", \"Stiffness in hip movement\", \"Difficulty walking\", \"Reduced mobility\"]','[\"Hip arthritis\", \"Joint degeneration\", \"Hip injury\"]','[\"Osteoarthritis of the hip\", \"Degenerative joint disease\", \"Hip cartilage damage\", \"Bone deterioration around the hip joint\"]','[\"Maintain a healthy body weight\", \"Regular exercise to strengthen hip muscles\", \"Avoid repetitive stress on hip joints\", \"Early treatment of hip injuries\"]','[\"Physical examination of hip movement\", \"X-ray imaging of the hip joint\", \"MRI scan to evaluate cartilage damage\", \"CT scan for detailed bone structure analysis\"]','<p>Hip resurfacing surgery involves reshaping the damaged ball of the hip joint and covering it with a smooth metal cap. The socket portion of the hip joint may also receive a metal lining. This procedure preserves more bone compared to total hip replacement while relieving pain and improving joint function.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Birmingham Hip Resurfacing\", \"description\": \"A widely used hip resurfacing technique that uses a metal-on-metal implant designed to preserve more natural bone.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Minimally Invasive Hip Resurfacing\", \"description\": \"A surgical approach using smaller incisions to reduce tissue damage and promote faster recovery.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow prescribed physiotherapy exercises\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during early recovery\", \"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Take medications as prescribed by the doctor\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up visits\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Implant wear\", \"Bone fracture around implant\", \"Nerve damage (rare)\"]','<p>Hip resurfacing helps preserve more natural bone compared to full hip replacement. Many patients regain improved mobility and reduced pain after recovery. This procedure is often recommended for younger and active patients. With proper care and rehabilitation, the implant can function effectively for many years. Regular monitoring ensures long-term joint health.</p>','<p>Hip resurfacing is an effective treatment option for selected patients with hip joint damage. By preserving natural bone and restoring joint function, the procedure can significantly improve mobility and quality of life.</p>','Hip Resurfacing Surgery | Nano Hospitals','Learn about Hip Resurfacing surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, surgery types, recovery timeline and risks.','hip resurfacing surgery, hip joint resurfacing, hip arthritis treatment, bone preserving hip surgery',1,'2026-03-17 07:38:15','2026-03-17 10:16:28',NULL),(42,'Arthroscopic Knee Surgery','procedures/banners/5b62c97c-e6d9-45f5-bba8-61201076c9dc.webp',NULL,'arthroscopic-knee-surgery','<p>Arthroscopic knee surgery is a minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose and treat knee joint problems using a small camera and specialized surgical instruments.</p>','<p>Arthroscopic knee surgery is a modern orthopedic procedure in which a small camera called an arthroscope is inserted into the knee joint through tiny incisions. The camera allows the surgeon to view the inside of the joint on a screen and perform surgical repairs using specialized instruments without making large incisions.</p>','[\"Knee pain\", \"Swelling around the knee joint\", \"Joint locking\", \"Limited knee movement\"]','[\"Meniscus injury\", \"Ligament damage\", \"Cartilage problems\", \"Sports injuries\"]','[\"Athletes and sports-related knee injuries\", \"Degenerative knee conditions\", \"Previous knee trauma\", \"Cartilage deterioration\"]','[\"Regular strengthening exercises for knee muscles\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Avoid excessive strain on knee joints\", \"Use protective gear during sports\"]','[\"Physical examination of knee movement\", \"X-ray imaging to check bone structure\", \"MRI scan to detect ligament or cartilage injuries\", \"Diagnostic arthroscopy in complex cases\"]','<p>During arthroscopic knee surgery, small surgical instruments are inserted through tiny incisions around the knee. The surgeon uses a miniature camera to view the inside of the joint and repair or remove damaged tissues such as torn cartilage, ligaments, or loose fragments. The procedure is minimally invasive and usually results in faster recovery compared to traditional open surgery.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Meniscus Repair Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive procedure used to repair or remove torn meniscus cartilage in the knee.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Ligament Reconstruction Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"Arthroscopic surgery used to repair or reconstruct damaged ligaments such as the ACL.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Cartilage Repair Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A procedure used to treat damaged cartilage in the knee joint.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Diagnostic Knee Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive procedure used to examine the knee joint and diagnose internal joint problems.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow prescribed physiotherapy exercises\", \"Apply ice to reduce swelling\", \"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Attend follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Swelling\", \"Temporary stiffness\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>Arthroscopic knee surgery helps restore joint function and relieve pain caused by internal knee injuries. Because the procedure uses small incisions, healing is usually quicker and less painful. Physiotherapy helps strengthen the knee and improve mobility after surgery. Most patients can return to sports and daily activities after recovery. Proper exercise and joint care help maintain long-term knee health.</p>','<p>Arthroscopic knee surgery is an effective minimally invasive treatment for many knee joint conditions. With proper rehabilitation and medical guidance, patients can regain mobility and return to an active lifestyle.</p>','Arthroscopic Knee Surgery | Nano Hospitals','Learn about Arthroscopic Knee Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment methods, surgery types, recovery timeline and risks.','arthroscopic knee surgery, knee arthroscopy, meniscus repair surgery, ACL arthroscopy, minimally invasive knee surgery',1,'2026-03-17 07:40:30','2026-03-17 10:15:49',NULL),(43,'Arthroscopic Shoulder Surgery','procedures/banners/26fa3f1c-2183-4724-8d68-0229bf01c86b.webp',NULL,'arthroscopic-shoulder-surgery','<p>Arthroscopic shoulder surgery is a minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose and treat problems inside the shoulder joint using a small camera and surgical instruments.</p>','<p>Arthroscopic shoulder surgery is a minimally invasive orthopedic procedure where a small camera called an arthroscope is inserted into the shoulder joint through tiny incisions. This allows surgeons to examine the joint and repair damaged tissues using specialized instruments without making large surgical cuts.</p>','[\"Shoulder pain\", \"Limited arm movement\", \"Weakness in the shoulder\", \"Clicking or instability\"]','[\"Rotator cuff injuries\", \"Shoulder impingement\", \"Joint inflammation\", \"Sports injuries\"]','[\"Repetitive overhead arm movements\", \"Sports-related injuries\", \"Degenerative shoulder joint conditions\", \"Previous shoulder trauma\"]','[\"Strengthening shoulder muscles through exercise\", \"Proper warm-up before physical activities\", \"Avoid excessive strain on shoulder joints\", \"Maintain good posture during activities\"]','[\"Physical examination of shoulder movement\", \"X-ray imaging of the shoulder joint\", \"MRI scan to detect soft tissue injuries\", \"Ultrasound to assess tendon damage\"]','<p>Arthroscopic shoulder surgery uses small surgical instruments inserted through tiny incisions around the shoulder. The surgeon uses a miniature camera to view the joint and repair damaged tissues such as torn tendons, ligaments, or cartilage. This minimally invasive technique reduces tissue damage and often leads to faster recovery compared to traditional open surgery.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Rotator Cuff Repair\", \"description\": \"Arthroscopic surgery used to repair torn rotator cuff tendons in the shoulder.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Shoulder Impingement Surgery\", \"description\": \"A procedure used to relieve pressure on shoulder tendons by removing inflamed tissue or bone spurs.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Labral Repair\", \"description\": \"Arthroscopic repair of the labrum, the cartilage ring that stabilizes the shoulder joint.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Shoulder Stabilization Surgery\", \"description\": \"A procedure used to repair ligaments and stabilize the shoulder joint after repeated dislocations.\"}]','[]','[\"Wear a shoulder sling as advised by the surgeon\", \"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid heavy lifting during recovery\", \"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Attend follow-up medical appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Shoulder stiffness\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Nerve injury (rare)\"]','<p>Arthroscopic shoulder surgery provides effective treatment for many shoulder injuries while minimizing surgical trauma. Most patients experience reduced pain and improved shoulder mobility after recovery. Rehabilitation exercises help restore strength and flexibility. Early treatment can prevent further joint damage. With proper care, patients can return to normal activities and sports.</p>','<p>Arthroscopic shoulder surgery is a safe and effective minimally invasive procedure for treating a variety of shoulder joint conditions. With proper rehabilitation and care, most patients regain strength, mobility, and improved quality of life.</p>','Arthroscopic Shoulder Surgery | Minimally Invasive ','Learn about Arthroscopic Shoulder Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, surgery types, recovery timeline and risks.','arthroscopic shoulder surgery, shoulder arthroscopy, rotator cuff repair surgery, minimally invasive shoulder surgery',1,'2026-03-17 07:41:52','2026-04-14 10:51:44',NULL),(44,'ACL Reconstruction','procedures/banners/e1d2a12b-f74e-4a75-aa79-8af8e493e42b.webp',NULL,'acl-reconstruction','<p>ACL reconstruction is a surgical procedure used to repair a torn anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) in the knee, which is commonly injured during sports activities.</p>','<p>ACL reconstruction is an orthopedic surgery performed to replace a damaged or torn anterior cruciate ligament in the knee. The ACL plays a critical role in stabilizing the knee joint during movement. When this ligament is torn due to injury or sports activity, surgical reconstruction using a tendon graft helps restore knee stability and function.</p>','[\"Sudden knee pain\", \"Knee instability\", \"Swelling around the knee\", \"Difficulty bearing weight\"]','[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden twisting of the knee\", \"Direct impact to the knee\"]','[\"High-impact sports such as football or basketball\", \"Sudden changes in direction while running\", \"Weak knee muscles\", \"Previous knee injuries\"]','[\"Strength training for leg and knee muscles\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Use of correct sports techniques\", \"Avoid excessive stress on the knee joint\"]','[\"Physical knee stability examination\", \"MRI scan to evaluate ligament damage\", \"X-ray imaging to rule out bone injury\", \"Arthroscopic diagnostic evaluation\"]','<p>ACL reconstruction surgery involves replacing the torn ligament with a graft taken from another tendon in the patient’s body or from a donor. The graft acts as a new ligament and is secured inside the knee joint to restore stability and normal movement. Arthroscopic techniques are commonly used to perform the surgery with minimal incisions.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Autograft ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"The torn ligament is replaced using a tendon taken from the patient’s own body, usually from the hamstring or patellar tendon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Allograft ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A donor tendon graft is used to replace the damaged ACL ligament.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Arthroscopic ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive surgical approach using a small camera and specialized instruments to reconstruct the ACL.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Use knee braces if recommended by the surgeon\", \"Apply ice to reduce swelling\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Attend regular follow-up visits\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Knee stiffness\", \"Re-injury of the ligament\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>ACL reconstruction helps restore stability and function of the knee joint. Most patients can return to sports and physical activities after proper rehabilitation. Strength training and physiotherapy are important for long-term recovery. Maintaining muscle strength around the knee helps protect the joint. With proper care, patients can achieve excellent long-term outcomes.</p>','<p>ACL reconstruction is a highly effective treatment for torn anterior cruciate ligaments. With modern surgical techniques and structured rehabilitation programs, patients can regain knee stability and return to an active lifestyle.</p>','ACL Reconstruction Surgery | Nano Hospitals','Learn about ACL Reconstruction surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','ACL reconstruction, anterior cruciate ligament surgery, ACL repair surgery, knee ligament reconstruction',1,'2026-03-17 07:42:48','2026-03-17 10:14:35',NULL),(45,'Meniscus Repair / Resection','procedures/banners/735eb4f3-5a0b-40bf-af3a-ccfe7172fa1a.webp',NULL,'meniscus-repair-resection','<p>Meniscus surgery is performed to repair or remove a torn meniscus, which is the cartilage that cushions the knee joint.</p>','<p>Meniscus repair or resection is a surgical procedure used to treat tears in the meniscus cartilage of the knee. The meniscus acts as a shock absorber between the thigh bone and shin bone. When the cartilage is torn due to injury or degeneration, arthroscopic surgery can be performed to repair the tear or remove the damaged portion to restore knee function.</p>','[\"Knee pain\", \"Swelling in the knee joint\", \"Joint locking\", \"Difficulty bending the knee\"]','[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden twisting of the knee\", \"Age-related cartilage wear\"]','[\"High-impact sports activities\", \"Degenerative knee conditions\", \"Previous knee injuries\", \"Weak knee muscles\"]','[\"Strengthening exercises for leg and knee muscles\", \"Proper warm-up before sports\", \"Avoid sudden twisting movements\", \"Maintain healthy body weight\"]','[\"Physical knee examination\", \"MRI scan to detect meniscus tear\", \"X-ray to rule out bone injury\", \"Diagnostic arthroscopy in complex cases\"]','<p>Meniscus surgery is typically performed using arthroscopic techniques. Small instruments and a camera are inserted through tiny incisions to repair the torn cartilage or remove the damaged portion. The goal of the procedure is to relieve pain, restore joint movement, and prevent further knee damage.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Meniscus Repair\", \"description\": \"The torn meniscus cartilage is stitched back together to preserve the natural structure of the knee.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Partial Meniscectomy\", \"description\": \"Only the damaged portion of the meniscus is removed to relieve symptoms while preserving as much cartilage as possible.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Arthroscopic Meniscus Surgery\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive surgical procedure using a camera and specialized instruments to repair or remove damaged cartilage.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Apply ice packs to reduce swelling\", \"Avoid excessive knee strain during recovery\", \"Take prescribed medications\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up visits\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Recurrent tear\", \"Swelling around the knee\"]','<p>Meniscus surgery helps relieve pain and restore normal knee function. Early treatment prevents further joint damage and arthritis. Rehabilitation exercises strengthen the muscles around the knee. Patients usually return to daily activities and sports after recovery. Proper joint care helps maintain long-term knee health.</p>','<p>Meniscus repair or resection surgery is an effective treatment for torn knee cartilage. With early diagnosis, proper surgical treatment, and structured rehabilitation, most patients regain full knee function and return to an active lifestyle.</p>','Meniscus Repair Surgery | Nano Hospitals','Learn about Meniscus Repair and Resection surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','meniscus repair surgery, meniscus tear treatment, arthroscopic meniscus surgery, knee cartilage repair',1,'2026-03-17 07:44:01','2026-03-17 10:20:31',NULL),(46,'Rotator Cuff Repair','procedures/banners/885a18c3-0347-4f9f-80cf-b7699e2f73fb.webp',NULL,'rotator-cuff-repair','<p>Rotator cuff repair is a surgical procedure used to repair torn tendons in the shoulder that help stabilize and move the arm.</p>','<p>Rotator cuff repair is an orthopedic surgical procedure performed to repair torn tendons of the rotator cuff in the shoulder joint. The rotator cuff is a group of muscles and tendons that stabilize the shoulder and allow arm movement. When these tendons are torn due to injury or degeneration, surgery may be required to reattach them to the bone and restore shoulder function.</p>','[\"Shoulder pain\", \"Weakness in the arm\", \"Difficulty lifting the arm\", \"Pain during sleep\"]','[\"Repetitive shoulder movement\", \"Sports injuries\", \"Age-related tendon degeneration\"]','[\"Athletes involved in overhead sports\", \"Degenerative shoulder conditions\", \"Heavy lifting activities\", \"Previous shoulder injuries\"]','[\"Regular shoulder strengthening exercises\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Avoid excessive strain on shoulder joints\", \"Maintain correct posture during physical activity\"]','[\"Physical shoulder examination\", \"MRI scan to detect tendon tears\", \"Ultrasound imaging of shoulder tendons\", \"X-ray imaging to evaluate bone structure\"]','<p>Rotator cuff repair surgery involves reattaching the torn tendon to the shoulder bone. This is usually performed using minimally invasive arthroscopic techniques where small instruments and a camera are inserted through tiny incisions. The goal of surgery is to relieve pain, restore shoulder strength, and improve arm movement.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Arthroscopic Rotator Cuff Repair\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive technique where small instruments and a camera are used to repair torn tendons.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Mini-Open Rotator Cuff Repair\", \"description\": \"A combination of arthroscopic and small open surgical techniques used to repair tendon damage.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Open Rotator Cuff Repair\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical approach used for large or complex tendon tears.\"}]','[]','[\"Wear a shoulder sling as advised by the surgeon\", \"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid heavy lifting during recovery\", \"Apply ice to reduce swelling\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up visits\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Shoulder stiffness\", \"Re-tear of tendon\", \"Nerve injury (rare)\"]','<p>Rotator cuff repair helps restore strength and movement of the shoulder. With proper rehabilitation, most patients regain full arm function. Early treatment prevents worsening of tendon damage. Physiotherapy plays a crucial role in recovery. Long-term results are generally excellent when patients follow rehabilitation programs.</p>','<p>Rotator cuff repair surgery is an effective treatment for torn shoulder tendons. With modern surgical techniques and proper rehabilitation, most patients regain shoulder strength, mobility, and the ability to return to normal daily activities.</p>','Rotator Cuff Repair Surgery | Nano Hospitals','Learn about Rotator Cuff Repair surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','rotator cuff repair, shoulder tendon repair surgery, rotator cuff tear treatment, arthroscopic rotator cuff surgery',1,'2026-03-17 07:44:55','2026-03-17 10:21:21',NULL),(48,'Laminectomy','procedures/banners/e69e1da7-10bb-47d3-a6aa-d6c8ff71b0e1.webp',NULL,'laminectomy','Laminectomy is a spinal decompression surgery in which part of the vertebral bone called the lamina is removed to relieve pressure on the spinal cord or nerves. The procedure is commonly performed for spinal stenosis and severe nerve compression. It helps improve mobility and reduce neurological symptoms.','The surgery may include: Removal of lamina bone Enlargement of spinal canal space Nerve decompression Removal of thickened ligaments or bone spurs Conditions treated include: Spinal stenosis Degenerative spinal disease Nerve compression Spinal tumors The procedure may be combined with spinal stabilization if necessary.','[{\"value\":\"Chronic back pain\"},{\"value\":\"Leg weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Numbness in limbs\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty standing or walking\"},{\"value\":\"Balance problems\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Laminectomy is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Spinal instability\"},{\"value\":\"Nerve damage\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent symptoms\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Laminectomy is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>The surgery may include: Removal of lamina bone Enlargement of spinal canal space Nerve decompression Removal of thickened ligaments or bone spurs Conditions treated include: Spinal stenosis Degenerative spinal disease N...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Follow spinal rehabilitation programs\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid heavy activities during recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain correct posture\"},{\"value\":\"Continue prescribed medications\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up spine evaluations\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Spinal instability\"},{\"value\":\"Nerve damage\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent symptoms\"}]','Laminectomy improves nerve decompression and mobility in many spinal disorders. Long-term success depends on rehabilitation and spinal health maintenance.','','Laminectomy','Laminectomy is a spinal decompression surgery in which part of the vertebral bone called the lamina is removed to relieve pressure on the spinal cord or nerves. The procedure is commonly performed for spinal stenosis and severe nerve compression. It helps improve mobility and reduce neurological symptoms.','',1,'2026-03-17 07:50:27','2026-07-29 00:28:07',NULL),(49,'Discectomy (Cervical / Lumbar)','procedures/banners/8860d37c-96e5-4119-bd90-d8c12438dbc8.webp',NULL,'discectomy-cervical-lumbar','<p>Discectomy is a surgical procedure performed to remove the damaged portion of a herniated disc that is pressing on spinal nerves. It helps relieve pain, numbness, and weakness caused by nerve compression.</p>','<p>Discectomy is a spinal surgery used to remove the portion of a damaged or herniated disc that is compressing nearby nerves. By relieving pressure on the spinal nerves, the procedure helps reduce pain, restore nerve function, and improve mobility. It is commonly performed in the cervical (neck) or lumbar (lower back) regions of the spine.</p>','[\"Severe back or neck pain\", \"Numbness or tingling in arms or legs\", \"Muscle weakness\", \"Difficulty walking or standing\"]','[\"Herniated disc\", \"Degenerative disc disease\", \"Spinal injury\"]','[\"Age-related spinal degeneration\", \"Repetitive heavy lifting\", \"Poor posture and spinal strain\", \"Previous spinal injuries\"]','[\"Maintain proper posture while sitting and standing\", \"Exercise regularly to strengthen core and back muscles\", \"Avoid lifting heavy objects improperly\", \"Maintain a healthy body weight\"]','[\"Physical neurological examination\", \"MRI scan to detect herniated discs\", \"CT scan to evaluate spinal structures\", \"X-ray imaging to rule out bone abnormalities\"]','<p>During discectomy surgery, the surgeon removes the damaged portion of the intervertebral disc that is pressing on the spinal nerve. This relieves nerve compression and reduces pain, numbness, and weakness. The procedure can be performed using minimally invasive techniques in many cases.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Cervical Discectomy\", \"description\": \"A procedure performed in the neck region to remove herniated disc material compressing spinal nerves.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Lumbar Discectomy\", \"description\": \"A surgery performed in the lower back to remove part of a herniated disc causing nerve compression.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Microdiscectomy\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive discectomy performed using small surgical instruments and a microscope.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy and rehabilitation exercises\", \"Avoid heavy lifting during recovery\", \"Maintain good posture to protect the spine\", \"Take medications as prescribed by the doctor\", \"Attend regular follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Nerve damage\", \"Recurrence of disc herniation\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>Discectomy helps relieve nerve pressure and reduce chronic pain. Most patients experience improved mobility and better quality of life after surgery. Rehabilitation exercises help strengthen the spine and prevent future injuries. Maintaining proper posture and avoiding heavy lifting can help protect spinal health. With proper care, patients can return to normal daily activities.</p>','<p>Discectomy is an effective surgical treatment for herniated discs causing nerve compression. With modern surgical techniques and proper rehabilitation, patients can regain mobility and return to normal daily activities.</p>','Discectomy Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Discectomy surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','discectomy surgery, cervical discectomy, lumbar discectomy, microdiscectomy, herniated disc surgery',1,'2026-03-17 07:54:18','2026-03-19 10:12:52',NULL),(50,'Fracture Fixation (ORIF)','procedures/banners/0f4e6db1-2a65-44a5-a554-26a010a8d7bc.webp',NULL,'fracture-fixation-orif','<p>Open Reduction Internal Fixation (ORIF) is a surgical procedure used to repair severely broken bones by realigning them and securing them with metal plates, screws, or rods.</p>','<p>Open Reduction Internal Fixation (ORIF) is an orthopedic surgical procedure used to treat complex bone fractures. During the procedure, the surgeon first repositions the broken bone fragments into their normal alignment (open reduction) and then stabilizes them using metal implants such as plates, screws, or rods (internal fixation).</p>','[\"Severe pain at injury site\", \"Swelling and bruising\", \"Inability to move the limb\", \"Visible bone deformity\"]','[\"Accidents\", \"Sports injuries\", \"Falls\"]','[\"High-impact trauma\", \"Severe bone fractures\", \"Road traffic accidents\", \"Falls from height\"]','[\"Use protective gear during sports activities\", \"Follow workplace safety precautions\", \"Maintain strong bones through proper nutrition and exercise\", \"Take precautions to prevent falls\"]','[\"Physical examination of the injured limb\", \"X-ray imaging to identify bone fractures\", \"CT scan to evaluate complex fractures\", \"MRI scan to assess surrounding soft tissue damage\"]','<p>During ORIF surgery, the surgeon makes an incision to access the broken bone and carefully repositions the fragments into their correct alignment. Metal implants such as plates, screws, or rods are then used to hold the bone pieces together while they heal. This procedure restores bone stability and supports proper healing.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Plate and Screw Fixation\", \"description\": \"Metal plates and screws are used to stabilize the fractured bone.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Intramedullary Rod Fixation\", \"description\": \"A metal rod is inserted into the bone marrow cavity to stabilize long bone fractures.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Screw Fixation\", \"description\": \"Special surgical screws are used to hold bone fragments together.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises to restore mobility\", \"Avoid placing weight on the injured limb until advised\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain and inflammation\", \"Keep the surgical site clean and monitored for infection\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Delayed bone healing\", \"Implant irritation\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>ORIF helps restore normal bone alignment and function after serious fractures. With proper healing and physiotherapy, most patients regain full mobility. Following medical advice and rehabilitation programs supports faster recovery. Implants may remain in place permanently or be removed later if required. Long-term results are usually excellent.</p>','<p>Fracture fixation using ORIF is an effective surgical treatment for severe bone fractures. With modern surgical techniques and proper rehabilitation, patients can regain strength, mobility, and normal function of the affected limb.</p>','Fracture Fixation (ORIF) Surgery | Open Reduction ','Learn about Fracture Fixation (ORIF) surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','ORIF surgery, fracture fixation surgery, open reduction internal fixation, bone fracture repair',1,'2026-03-17 07:56:54','2026-04-14 10:54:03',NULL),(51,'External Fixation','procedures/banners/0ec9b5ef-3a0e-4971-b6b7-a6d330088bb2.webp',NULL,'external-fixation','<p>External fixation is a surgical technique used to stabilize broken bones using metal rods and pins placed outside the body.</p>','<p>External fixation is an orthopedic procedure used to stabilize fractured bones using metal pins or screws inserted into the bone and connected to a rigid frame outside the body. This method keeps the bone fragments aligned while they heal, especially in complex or open fractures where internal fixation may not be suitable.</p>','[\"Severe bone fracture\", \"Swelling and pain\", \"Open or complex fractures\"]','[\"High-impact injuries\", \"Road accidents\", \"Severe trauma\"]','[\"Multiple bone fractures\", \"Severe soft tissue damage\", \"Open fractures with infection risk\", \"Complex orthopedic trauma\"]','[\"Follow road safety guidelines\", \"Use protective gear during sports\", \"Maintain strong bones through proper nutrition and exercise\", \"Take precautions to avoid falls and injuries\"]','[\"Physical examination of the injured area\", \"X-ray imaging to assess fracture alignment\", \"CT scan for complex fracture evaluation\", \"MRI scan to assess soft tissue injuries\"]','<p>During external fixation surgery, metal pins or screws are inserted into the bone above and below the fracture site. These pins are connected to an external metal frame that stabilizes the bone fragments in the correct position during healing. This technique is commonly used for severe fractures, open fractures, or when immediate stabilization is required.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Temporary External Fixation\", \"description\": \"Used as an initial stabilization method for severe fractures before definitive surgery.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Circular External Fixation\", \"description\": \"A ring-shaped frame used to stabilize complex fractures and deformities.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Hybrid External Fixation\", \"description\": \"A combination of different external fixation systems used for complex fractures.\"}]','[]','[\"Clean pin sites regularly to prevent infection\", \"Follow physiotherapy exercises to restore mobility\", \"Avoid placing excessive weight on the affected limb\", \"Attend regular medical checkups to monitor bone healing\", \"Take prescribed medications as directed\"]','[\"Infection at pin sites\", \"Bone healing delay\", \"Discomfort from external frame\", \"Nerve or soft tissue irritation\"]','<p>External fixation helps stabilize complex fractures that cannot be treated with traditional methods. Once the bone heals properly, the external device is removed. Rehabilitation exercises help restore mobility and strength. Proper care of pin sites reduces the risk of infection. Most patients recover well with appropriate treatment.</p>','<p>External fixation is an effective orthopedic technique for stabilizing complex fractures and severe injuries. With proper surgical care, monitoring, and rehabilitation, patients can achieve successful bone healing and regain normal limb function.</p>','External Fixation Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about External Fixation surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','external fixation surgery, fracture stabilization, orthopedic external fixator, bone fracture treatment',1,'2026-03-17 07:57:46','2026-03-19 10:18:39',NULL),(52,'Intramedullary Nailing','procedures/banners/58d6c9bf-2186-47ad-a8bd-1f0ebdcfff82.webp',NULL,'intramedullary-nailing','<p>Intramedullary nailing is a surgical procedure used to treat fractures of long bones such as the femur or tibia by inserting a metal rod inside the bone canal.</p>','<p>Intramedullary nailing is an orthopedic surgical technique used to stabilize fractures of long bones. During the procedure, a metal rod called an intramedullary nail is inserted into the hollow center of the bone to keep the fractured pieces aligned while healing occurs.</p>','[\"Severe limb pain\", \"Swelling around the injured area\", \"Inability to bear weight\", \"Bone deformity\"]','[\"Road accidents\", \"Falls\", \"Sports injuries\"]','[\"High-impact trauma\", \"Severe long bone fractures\", \"Accidents involving high force\", \"Osteoporosis-related fractures\"]','[\"Follow road safety measures\", \"Use protective equipment during sports\", \"Maintain strong bones with proper nutrition and exercise\", \"Take precautions to avoid falls\"]','[\"Physical examination of the injured limb\", \"X-ray imaging to confirm bone fracture\", \"CT scan for complex fractures\", \"MRI scan to assess surrounding soft tissue damage\"]','<p>During intramedullary nailing surgery, a metal rod is inserted into the center canal of the fractured bone to stabilize it. Screws are often placed at both ends of the rod to keep the bone fragments aligned while healing occurs. This technique allows strong internal support and promotes faster recovery.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Femoral Intramedullary Nailing\", \"description\": \"Used to treat fractures of the femur (thigh bone) by inserting a rod through the bone canal.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Tibial Intramedullary Nailing\", \"description\": \"Performed to stabilize fractures of the tibia (shin bone).\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Humeral Intramedullary Nailing\", \"description\": \"Used to treat fractures of the upper arm bone (humerus).\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid excessive weight bearing until advised by the doctor\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain and inflammation\", \"Attend follow-up appointments to monitor bone healing\", \"Maintain proper nutrition for bone recovery\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Implant irritation\", \"Delayed healing\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>Intramedullary nailing provides strong support for fractured bones and allows early movement. Most patients regain normal function after recovery. Physiotherapy helps restore muscle strength and flexibility. Following rehabilitation programs ensures better outcomes. Long-term recovery is usually successful.</p>','<p>Intramedullary nailing is a reliable and widely used orthopedic procedure for stabilizing long bone fractures. With proper treatment and rehabilitation, patients can regain full mobility and return to normal daily activities.</p>','Intramedullary Nailing Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Intramedullary Nailing surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','intramedullary nailing, femur fracture surgery, tibia fracture treatment, orthopedic bone rod surgery',1,'2026-03-17 08:01:34','2026-03-19 10:21:30',NULL),(53,'Joint Arthroscopy','procedures/banners/1540b93b-151e-44cc-ad7f-ad1e191d5cf0.webp',NULL,'joint-arthroscopy','<p>Joint arthroscopy is a minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose and treat problems inside joints such as the knee, shoulder, hip, or ankle.</p>','<p>Joint arthroscopy is a minimally invasive surgical technique that allows doctors to examine and treat joint problems using a small camera called an arthroscope. The arthroscope is inserted into the joint through small incisions, allowing the surgeon to visualize the joint on a monitor and perform repairs with specialized instruments.</p>','[\"Joint pain\", \"Swelling around the joint\", \"Stiffness\", \"Limited range of motion\"]','[\"Ligament injuries\", \"Cartilage damage\", \"Joint inflammation\"]','[\"Sports-related joint injuries\", \"Degenerative joint conditions\", \"Repeated stress on joints\", \"Previous joint trauma\"]','[\"Regular strengthening exercises for joints\", \"Proper warm-up before physical activities\", \"Avoid excessive strain on joints\", \"Maintain a healthy body weight\"]','[\"Physical examination of joint movement\", \"X-ray imaging to evaluate bone structure\", \"MRI scan to assess ligament and cartilage damage\", \"Diagnostic arthroscopy if required\"]','<p>During joint arthroscopy, a small camera is inserted into the joint through a tiny incision. The surgeon uses specialized instruments inserted through additional small incisions to repair damaged ligaments, cartilage, or other joint structures. This minimally invasive approach reduces tissue damage and promotes faster recovery.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Knee Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose and treat knee joint problems.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Shoulder Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"Used to repair shoulder joint injuries such as rotator cuff tears.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Hip Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"Performed to treat hip joint conditions such as labral tears.\"}, {\"name\": \"4. Ankle Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A procedure used to diagnose and treat ankle joint injuries.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Apply ice to reduce swelling\", \"Avoid strenuous activities during recovery\", \"Take medications as prescribed\", \"Attend follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>Joint arthroscopy helps treat joint injuries with minimal tissue damage. Patients usually experience faster recovery and improved joint function. Rehabilitation exercises help restore mobility and strength. Early treatment prevents further joint damage. Long-term outcomes are generally very good.</p>','<p>Joint arthroscopy is a safe and effective minimally invasive procedure for diagnosing and treating a variety of joint conditions. With proper rehabilitation and care, patients can regain mobility and return to normal activities quickly.</p>','Joint Arthroscopy Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Joint Arthroscopy including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','joint arthroscopy surgery, knee arthroscopy, shoulder arthroscopy, minimally invasive joint surgery',1,'2026-03-17 08:03:07','2026-03-19 10:26:14',NULL),(54,'Tendon Repair Surgery','procedures/banners/4fa3e81c-f776-494c-9540-341c699a275c.webp',NULL,'tendon-repair-surgery','<p>Tendon repair surgery is performed to repair torn or damaged tendons that connect muscles to bones.</p>','<p>Tendon repair surgery is an orthopedic procedure used to repair torn or damaged tendons. Tendons connect muscles to bones and enable joint movement. When a tendon is injured due to trauma, sports activity, or repetitive strain, surgical repair may be required to restore normal function and mobility.</p>','[\"Pain during movement\", \"Weakness in affected area\", \"Swelling\", \"Difficulty moving the joint\"]','[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden trauma\", \"Repetitive strain\"]','[\"Athletes performing repetitive movements\", \"Heavy physical activities\", \"Age-related tendon degeneration\", \"Previous tendon injuries\"]','[\"Proper warm-up before exercise or sports\", \"Avoid repetitive strain on joints and tendons\", \"Strengthen muscles through regular exercise\", \"Maintain good posture and body mechanics\"]','[\"Physical examination of the affected joint\", \"Ultrasound imaging to evaluate tendon damage\", \"MRI scan to assess tendon tears\", \"X-ray imaging to rule out bone injuries\"]','<p>During tendon repair surgery, the surgeon stitches the torn tendon back together or reattaches it to the bone using special surgical techniques. In some cases, grafts may be used to strengthen the repaired tendon. The goal of the procedure is to restore strength, stability, and normal movement of the affected joint.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Open Tendon Repair\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical approach used for repairing severely damaged tendons.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Arthroscopic Tendon Repair\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive technique using a small camera and specialized instruments.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Tendon Graft Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A procedure where a tendon graft is used to reconstruct severely damaged tendons.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid excessive movement or strain on the repaired tendon\", \"Take medications as prescribed by the doctor\", \"Attend follow-up appointments for monitoring recovery\", \"Gradually return to physical activities as advised\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Tendon stiffness\", \"Re-tear\", \"Nerve irritation (rare)\"]','<p>Tendon repair surgery helps restore normal movement and strength. Proper rehabilitation is essential for successful recovery. Physiotherapy strengthens the muscles and improves flexibility. Early treatment prevents long-term functional problems. Most patients regain good joint function after recovery.</p>','<p>Tendon repair surgery is an effective treatment for damaged or torn tendons. With modern surgical techniques and structured rehabilitation programs, patients can regain strength, flexibility, and normal joint movement.</p>','Tendon Repair Surgery: Procedure, Recovery & Care | Nano Hos','Restore your mobility with expert tendon repair surgery at Nano Hospital. Our specialists treat tears in the hand, shoulder, knee, and ankle using advanced mini','tendon repair surgery, torn tendon treatment, tendon reconstruction, orthopedic surgery, tendon injury recovery, Nano Hospital orthopedics',1,'2026-03-17 08:04:14','2026-04-13 11:26:28',NULL),(55,'Carpal Tunnel Release','procedures/banners/9cc451cb-b76c-4afd-a208-f07574343534.webp',NULL,'carpal-tunnel-release','<p>Carpal tunnel release surgery is performed to relieve pressure on the median nerve in the wrist, which causes pain, numbness, and tingling in the hand.</p>','<p>Carpal tunnel release is a surgical procedure used to treat carpal tunnel syndrome, a condition caused by compression of the median nerve in the wrist. The surgery involves cutting the ligament that presses on the nerve, thereby relieving pressure and improving hand function.</p>','[\"Numbness in fingers\", \"Tingling in hand\", \"Weak grip strength\", \"Wrist pain\"]','[\"Repetitive hand movements\", \"Wrist injuries\", \"Nerve compression\"]','[\"Frequent repetitive hand motions\", \"Prolonged computer or typing work\", \"Wrist injuries or fractures\", \"Medical conditions such as diabetes or arthritis\"]','[\"Take regular breaks during repetitive hand activities\", \"Maintain proper wrist posture while working\", \"Perform wrist stretching and strengthening exercises\", \"Use ergonomic tools and equipment\"]','[\"Physical examination of the wrist and hand\", \"Nerve conduction studies\", \"Electromyography (EMG)\", \"Ultrasound imaging of the median nerve\"]','<p>Carpal tunnel release surgery involves cutting the transverse carpal ligament to reduce pressure on the median nerve. This procedure helps relieve symptoms such as pain, numbness, and tingling, and allows the nerve to function normally again.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Open Carpal Tunnel Release\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical technique where a small incision is made in the wrist to cut the ligament.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Endoscopic Carpal Tunnel Release\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive procedure using a small camera to guide the release of the ligament.\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Perform recommended hand and wrist exercises\", \"Avoid heavy lifting during recovery\", \"Take prescribed medications as directed\", \"Attend follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Temporary weakness\", \"Nerve irritation\", \"Scar tenderness\"]','<p>Carpal tunnel surgery provides effective relief from nerve compression symptoms. Many patients regain normal hand strength and sensation after recovery. Physiotherapy exercises help improve wrist mobility. Avoiding repetitive strain protects the wrist in the future. Long-term results are usually very successful.</p>','<p>Carpal tunnel release surgery is a safe and effective treatment for relieving pressure on the median nerve. With proper recovery and rehabilitation, most patients regain normal hand function and return to daily activities comfortably.</p>','Carpal Tunnel Release Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Carpal Tunnel Release surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','carpal tunnel release surgery, carpal tunnel syndrome treatment, wrist nerve compression surgery, median nerve decompression',1,'2026-03-17 08:05:13','2026-03-19 10:33:04',NULL),(56,'Trigger Finger Release','procedures/banners/7f42f6de-d869-4c14-beda-18acdf0ebb4f.webp',NULL,'trigger-finger-release','<p>Trigger finger release surgery is performed to treat a condition where a finger becomes stuck in a bent position due to tendon inflammation.</p>','<p>Trigger finger release is a minor surgical procedure used to treat stenosing tenosynovitis, commonly known as trigger finger. The condition occurs when the tendon sheath in the finger becomes inflamed and tight, causing the finger to lock or catch during movement. Surgery releases the tight sheath to restore smooth tendon movement.</p>','[\"Finger stiffness\", \"Clicking or locking of finger\", \"Pain in the palm\", \"Difficulty straightening the finger\"]','[\"Repetitive hand use\", \"Tendon inflammation\", \"Diabetes or arthritis\"]','[\"Frequent gripping or repetitive hand movements\", \"Underlying medical conditions such as diabetes\", \"Inflammatory conditions like rheumatoid arthritis\", \"Previous hand injuries\"]','[\"Avoid repetitive strain on fingers\", \"Take breaks during repetitive hand activities\", \"Perform hand stretching exercises\", \"Maintain good hand ergonomics while working\"]','[\"Physical examination of the affected finger\", \"Assessment of finger movement and locking\", \"Ultrasound imaging of the tendon\", \"Medical evaluation to rule out underlying conditions\"]','<p>During trigger finger release surgery, the surgeon makes a small incision near the base of the affected finger and releases the tight tendon sheath. This allows the tendon to move freely and restores normal finger movement.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Open Trigger Finger Release\", \"description\": \"A small incision is made in the palm to release the tight tendon sheath.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Percutaneous Trigger Finger Release\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive technique using a needle to release the tight sheath without a surgical incision.\"}]','[]','[\"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Perform recommended finger exercises\", \"Avoid heavy gripping during recovery\", \"Take medications as prescribed\", \"Attend follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Finger stiffness\", \"Scar tenderness\"]','<p>Trigger finger surgery usually provides immediate improvement in finger movement. Most patients regain full hand function after recovery. Simple hand exercises help restore strength and flexibility. Early treatment prevents permanent finger stiffness. Long-term outcomes are excellent.</p>','<p>Trigger finger release surgery is a simple and effective procedure for restoring normal finger movement. With proper recovery and rehabilitation, patients can quickly return to daily activities with improved hand function.</p>','Trigger Finger Release Surgery | Finger Locking Treatment','Learn about Trigger Finger Release surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','trigger finger release surgery, trigger finger treatment, stenosing tenosynovitis surgery, finger tendon release',1,'2026-03-17 08:07:55','2026-03-19 10:35:35',NULL),(57,'Bunionectomy (Hallux Valgus Correction)','procedures/banners/f634bc75-fa7a-4517-b67a-039e473d2cd2.webp',NULL,'bunionectomy-hallux-valgus-correction','<p>Bunionectomy is a surgical procedure used to correct a bunion, which is a bony bump that forms at the base of the big toe.</p>','<p>Bunionectomy, also known as hallux valgus correction surgery, is performed to remove the bony bump that forms at the base of the big toe and realign the toe joint. The surgery helps relieve pain and restore proper foot alignment.</p>','[\"Pain at the base of the big toe\", \"Swelling and redness\", \"Difficulty wearing shoes\", \"Toe deformity\"]','[\"Genetic foot structure\", \"Tight footwear\", \"Arthritis\"]','[\"Family history of bunions\", \"Foot deformities\", \"Prolonged use of tight or narrow footwear\", \"Inflammatory joint diseases\"]','[\"Wear properly fitting footwear\", \"Avoid high heels and tight shoes\", \"Use orthotic support if needed\", \"Maintain good foot hygiene and care\"]','[\"Physical examination of the foot\", \"X-ray imaging to evaluate toe alignment\", \"Assessment of joint flexibility\", \"Medical evaluation for underlying arthritis\"]','<p>During bunionectomy surgery, the surgeon removes the enlarged bone and corrects the alignment of the big toe joint. In some cases, the bones may be repositioned and secured with screws or plates to maintain proper alignment.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Osteotomy Bunionectomy\", \"description\": \"The bone is cut and repositioned to correct the alignment of the toe.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Exostectomy\", \"description\": \"Removal of the bony bump from the joint without major bone realignment.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Arthrodesis\", \"description\": \"Fusion of the affected joint to correct severe bunion deformity.\"}]','[]','[\"Wear supportive footwear during recovery\", \"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Follow recommended physiotherapy exercises\", \"Avoid excessive pressure on the foot\", \"Attend follow-up medical appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Toe stiffness\", \"Recurrence of bunion\", \"Delayed bone healing\"]','<p>Bunionectomy helps relieve pain and correct foot alignment. Most patients experience improved comfort while walking and wearing shoes. Proper footwear and foot care help prevent recurrence. Rehabilitation exercises improve foot strength and mobility. Long-term outcomes are generally very positive.</p>','<p>Bunionectomy surgery is an effective treatment for correcting bunion deformities and relieving foot pain. With proper recovery and foot care, patients can regain normal walking ability and improved foot function.</p>','Bunionectomy Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Bunionectomy surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','bunionectomy surgery, hallux valgus correction, bunion treatment, foot bunion surgery',1,'2026-03-17 08:08:48','2026-03-19 10:37:09',NULL),(58,'Achilles Tendon Repair','procedures/banners/c87010c4-485d-4fef-8ff2-38eb8b97fb2e.webp',NULL,'achilles-tendon-repair','<p>Achilles tendon repair is a surgical procedure used to treat a torn or ruptured Achilles tendon, which connects the calf muscles to the heel bone and helps in walking and running.</p>','<p>Achilles tendon repair is a surgical procedure performed to repair a torn or ruptured Achilles tendon. The Achilles tendon is the largest tendon in the body and plays an essential role in walking, running, and jumping. Surgery restores tendon continuity and strength so the ankle can function normally again.</p>','[\"Sudden pain in the back of the ankle\", \"Difficulty walking\", \"Swelling near the heel\", \"Weakness while pushing the foot\"]','[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden increase in physical activity\", \"Direct trauma to the tendon\"]','[\"High-impact sports activities\", \"Sudden strain on calf muscles\", \"Previous Achilles tendon injuries\", \"Poor warm-up before exercise\"]','[\"Warm up properly before physical activity\", \"Gradually increase intensity of exercise\", \"Perform calf strengthening and stretching exercises\", \"Use proper footwear during sports\"]','[\"Physical examination of the ankle\", \"Ultrasound imaging of the tendon\", \"MRI scan to assess tendon rupture\", \"Functional assessment of ankle movement\"]','<p>During Achilles tendon repair surgery, the torn ends of the tendon are stitched together using strong sutures. In some cases, tendon grafts may be used if the rupture is severe. The goal of the surgery is to restore tendon strength, stability, and ankle function.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Open Achilles Tendon Repair\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical approach using an incision to repair the torn tendon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Minimally Invasive Achilles Repair\", \"description\": \"A modern technique using small incisions and specialized instruments to repair the tendon.\"}]','[]','[\"Wear protective braces or casts as advised\", \"Follow physiotherapy and rehabilitation exercises\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain and inflammation\", \"Attend regular follow-up visits\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Tendon stiffness\", \"Re-rupture of the tendon\", \"Nerve irritation\"]','<p>Achilles tendon repair helps restore strength and flexibility in the ankle. With proper rehabilitation, most patients regain normal walking and athletic ability. Physiotherapy exercises improve muscle strength and balance. Avoiding excessive strain during recovery is important. Long-term results are usually very successful.</p>','<p>Achilles tendon repair surgery is an effective treatment for ruptured tendons and helps restore ankle stability and movement. With proper rehabilitation and care, patients can return to normal daily activities and sports.</p>','Achilles Tendon Repair Surgery & Recovery | Nano Hospital','Expert Achilles tendon rupture treatment at Nano Hospital. Learn about our advanced surgery options, diagnosis, recovery timelines, and expert care to get you b','achilles tendon repair surgery, achilles tendon rupture treatment, ankle tendon repair, achilles surgery, Nano Hospital orthopedics, torn achilles recovery',1,'2026-03-17 08:09:48','2026-04-13 11:25:20',NULL),(59,'Shoulder Stabilization Surgery','procedures/banners/e2d92dc7-f381-4a5e-879c-c7e358fc5d17.webp',NULL,'shoulder-stabilization-surgery','<p>Shoulder stabilization surgery is performed to correct repeated shoulder dislocations and restore stability to the shoulder joint.</p>','<p>Shoulder stabilization surgery is an orthopedic procedure designed to repair damaged ligaments and tissues that support the shoulder joint. The surgery helps restore normal joint alignment and prevent repeated shoulder dislocations.</p>','[\"Shoulder instability\", \"Repeated dislocations\", \"Pain during movement\", \"Weakness in the shoulder\"]','[\"Sports injuries\", \"Ligament damage\", \"Trauma to the shoulder joint\"]','[\"High-impact sports such as football or basketball\", \"Previous shoulder dislocations\", \"Weak shoulder ligaments\", \"Traumatic shoulder injuries\"]','[\"Strengthening shoulder muscles through exercise\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Avoid excessive strain on the shoulder joint\", \"Use protective gear during sports\"]','[\"Physical examination of shoulder stability\", \"X-ray imaging of the shoulder joint\", \"MRI scan to assess ligament damage\", \"Arthroscopic evaluation of the shoulder\"]','<p>During shoulder stabilization surgery, the surgeon repairs or tightens the ligaments and soft tissues that support the shoulder joint. This helps restore joint stability and prevent future dislocations.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Arthroscopic Shoulder Stabilization\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive procedure using a small camera and instruments to repair damaged shoulder ligaments.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Open Shoulder Stabilization\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical approach used to repair severe ligament damage.\"}]','[]','[\"Wear a shoulder sling as advised by the surgeon\", \"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid heavy lifting during recovery\", \"Take medications as prescribed\", \"Attend follow-up medical appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Shoulder stiffness\", \"Recurrent instability\", \"Nerve irritation\"]','<p>Shoulder stabilization surgery helps restore joint strength and prevent repeated dislocations. Most patients regain normal shoulder function after rehabilitation. Physiotherapy is essential to rebuild muscle strength and flexibility. Early treatment prevents further joint damage. Long-term outcomes are generally excellent.</p>','<p>Shoulder stabilization surgery is an effective treatment for recurrent shoulder dislocations. With proper surgical care and rehabilitation, patients can regain stable shoulder movement and return to daily activities.</p>','Shoulder Stabilization Surgery | Shoulder Dislocation ','Learn about Shoulder Stabilization Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','shoulder stabilization surgery, shoulder dislocation treatment, shoulder ligament repair, recurrent shoulder instability',1,'2026-03-17 08:10:57','2026-04-14 10:57:51',NULL),(60,'Hip Arthroscopy','procedures/banners/a3e7a773-1e6b-4a2a-8e55-ce7b8cb1dcdc.webp',NULL,'hip-arthroscopy','<p>Hip arthroscopy is a minimally invasive surgical procedure used to diagnose and treat problems inside the hip joint using a small camera and specialized instruments.</p>','<p>Hip arthroscopy is a minimally invasive orthopedic procedure in which a small camera called an arthroscope is inserted into the hip joint through tiny incisions. This allows surgeons to diagnose and treat conditions such as labral tears, cartilage damage, and hip impingement with minimal disruption to surrounding tissues.</p>','[\"Hip pain\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Clicking sensation in the hip\", \"Reduced range of motion\"]','[\"Labral tears\", \"Hip impingement\", \"Cartilage damage\"]','[\"Sports-related hip injuries\", \"Repetitive hip movements\", \"Degenerative joint conditions\", \"Previous hip trauma\"]','[\"Regular strengthening exercises for hip muscles\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Avoid excessive strain on the hip joint\", \"Maintain a healthy body weight\"]','[\"Physical examination of hip movement\", \"X-ray imaging to assess bone structure\", \"MRI scan to detect labral or cartilage damage\", \"Diagnostic hip arthroscopy when required\"]','<p>During hip arthroscopy, the surgeon inserts a small camera and surgical instruments through tiny incisions around the hip joint. Damaged cartilage, labral tears, or bone abnormalities can be repaired using specialized tools while preserving healthy tissue.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Labral Repair Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A procedure used to repair tears in the hip labrum.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Hip Impingement Correction\", \"description\": \"Removal or reshaping of bone causing impingement in the hip joint.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Cartilage Repair Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive technique used to treat cartilage damage in the hip joint.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Avoid strenuous physical activity during recovery\", \"Use assistive devices such as crutches if recommended\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain relief\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Nerve irritation (rare)\"]','<p>Hip arthroscopy helps relieve pain and restore hip mobility with minimal surgical trauma. Most patients experience quicker recovery compared to traditional surgery. Rehabilitation exercises strengthen surrounding muscles and improve joint stability. Early treatment helps prevent further joint damage. Long-term results are usually very good.</p>','<p>Hip arthroscopy is a safe and effective minimally invasive procedure for diagnosing and treating various hip joint conditions. With proper rehabilitation and care, patients can regain mobility and return to normal daily activities.</p>','Hip Arthroscopy Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Hip Arthroscopy surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','hip arthroscopy surgery, hip joint arthroscopy, labral tear treatment, minimally invasive hip surgery',1,'2026-03-17 08:13:21','2026-03-19 10:51:05',NULL),(61,'Ankle Arthroscopy','procedures/banners/a670c873-7d43-4bcb-9aee-208c4b4d670a.webp',NULL,'ankle-arthroscopy','<p>Ankle arthroscopy is a minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose and treat problems inside the ankle joint.</p>','<p>Ankle arthroscopy is a minimally invasive surgical procedure in which a small camera called an arthroscope is inserted into the ankle joint through tiny incisions. The camera allows the surgeon to visualize the joint and treat various conditions such as ligament injuries, cartilage damage, and chronic ankle instability.</p>','[\"Ankle pain\", \"Swelling\", \"Limited movement\", \"Instability in ankle\"]','[\"Ligament injuries\", \"Cartilage damage\", \"Repeated ankle sprains\"]','[\"Sports-related ankle injuries\", \"Previous ankle sprains\", \"Chronic ankle instability\", \"Degenerative joint conditions\"]','[\"Perform ankle strengthening exercises\", \"Use proper footwear during sports\", \"Warm up before physical activities\", \"Avoid repeated ankle strain\"]','[\"Physical examination of ankle mobility\", \"X-ray imaging to evaluate bone structures\", \"MRI scan to detect ligament or cartilage damage\", \"Diagnostic arthroscopy if needed\"]','<p>During ankle arthroscopy, the surgeon inserts a small camera and specialized instruments into the ankle joint through tiny incisions. Damaged cartilage, ligaments, or loose bone fragments can be repaired or removed to restore normal joint function.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Ligament Repair Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive procedure used to repair damaged ankle ligaments.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Cartilage Repair Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"Treatment of cartilage damage inside the ankle joint using specialized surgical tools.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Debridement Arthroscopy\", \"description\": \"Removal of damaged tissue or loose fragments from the ankle joint.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Keep the surgical area clean and dry\", \"Avoid excessive strain on the ankle\", \"Take medications as prescribed by the doctor\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Temporary swelling\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Nerve irritation (rare)\"]','<p>Ankle arthroscopy allows doctors to treat joint problems with minimal incisions. Patients usually experience faster healing and reduced pain after surgery. Physiotherapy helps restore ankle strength and flexibility. Early treatment prevents chronic ankle problems. Long-term outcomes are generally positive.</p>','<p>Ankle arthroscopy is an effective minimally invasive procedure for diagnosing and treating ankle joint problems. With proper rehabilitation and medical care, patients can regain mobility and return to daily activities.</p>','Ankle Arthroscopy Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Ankle Arthroscopy including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','ankle arthroscopy surgery, ankle joint arthroscopy, ligament repair ankle surgery, minimally invasive ankle surgery',1,'2026-03-17 08:14:16','2026-03-19 10:53:20',NULL),(62,'Bone Grafting','procedures/banners/c5adeeca-2b45-49fb-9684-beb98bdf4af5.webp',NULL,'bone-grafting','<p>Bone grafting is a surgical procedure used to repair or rebuild damaged bones by transplanting bone tissue from another part of the body or using synthetic material.</p>','<p>Bone grafting is a surgical technique used to repair bone defects or promote bone healing. The procedure involves placing healthy bone tissue or synthetic bone material into an area where bone is missing or damaged. This graft stimulates new bone growth and helps restore bone structure and strength.</p>','[\"Bone defects\", \"Delayed fracture healing\", \"Bone loss after injury\"]','[\"Severe fractures\", \"Bone infections\", \"Bone tumors\"]','[\"Severe bone injuries\", \"Chronic bone infections\", \"Bone loss due to trauma or surgery\", \"Degenerative bone conditions\"]','[\"Maintain good bone health with proper nutrition\", \"Ensure adequate calcium and vitamin D intake\", \"Protect bones from injuries during sports or activities\", \"Seek early medical treatment for bone infections\"]','[\"Physical examination of the affected area\", \"X-ray imaging to assess bone damage\", \"CT scan to evaluate bone structure\", \"MRI scan to detect bone or soft tissue abnormalities\"]','<p>During bone grafting surgery, healthy bone tissue is placed into the damaged or missing bone area. The graft acts as a scaffold that stimulates new bone growth and helps the body repair the damaged bone naturally over time.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Autograft Bone Grafting\", \"description\": \"Bone tissue is taken from another part of the patient’s body, usually the pelvis.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Allograft Bone Grafting\", \"description\": \"Bone tissue from a donor is used to repair damaged bone.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Synthetic Bone Grafting\", \"description\": \"Artificial bone substitutes are used to stimulate new bone growth.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow the surgeon’s instructions carefully\", \"Avoid excessive stress on the affected bone\", \"Maintain a healthy diet rich in calcium and protein\", \"Take prescribed medications as directed\", \"Attend regular follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Graft rejection\", \"Delayed healing\", \"Pain at the donor site (for autografts)\"]','<p>Bone grafting helps restore bone strength and structure. Over time, the graft integrates with the existing bone and promotes natural healing. Patients usually regain normal bone function after recovery. Proper nutrition and rehabilitation support healing. Long-term outcomes are typically successful.</p>','<p>Bone grafting is an effective surgical procedure used to rebuild and strengthen damaged bones. With proper medical care, nutrition, and rehabilitation, patients can achieve successful bone healing and long-term recovery.</p>','Bone Grafting Surgery | Nano Hospital','Learn about Bone Grafting surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','bone grafting surgery, bone reconstruction surgery, bone repair treatment, orthopedic bone graft',1,'2026-03-17 08:15:40','2026-03-19 10:55:46',NULL),(63,'Limb Lengthening Surgery','procedures/banners/bef6e0b7-844a-4b77-89c1-178ef2102df3.webp',NULL,'limb-lengthening-surgery','<p>Limb lengthening surgery is performed to increase the length of bones in the arms or legs using specialized surgical techniques and devices.</p>','<p>Limb lengthening surgery is an orthopedic procedure that gradually increases the length of bones in the arms or legs. The bone is surgically divided and a special device is used to slowly separate the bone segments, allowing new bone tissue to form in the gap as it heals.</p>','[\"Limb length difference\", \"Difficulty walking\", \"Uneven posture\"]','[\"Congenital conditions\", \"Growth disorders\", \"Injury affecting bone growth\"]','[\"Congenital limb length discrepancies\", \"Bone growth abnormalities\", \"Previous bone injuries\", \"Developmental skeletal conditions\"]','[\"Early medical evaluation for growth abnormalities\", \"Regular monitoring of children with limb length differences\", \"Proper treatment of bone injuries\", \"Maintaining overall bone health\"]','[\"Physical examination and limb measurement\", \"X-ray imaging of the bones\", \"CT scan to evaluate bone structure\", \"Gait analysis to assess walking pattern\"]','<p>During limb lengthening surgery, the bone is carefully divided and a specialized device such as an external fixator or internal rod is attached. The device gradually lengthens the bone over time, allowing new bone tissue to form in the gap.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. External Fixator Limb Lengthening\", \"description\": \"An external device is attached to the bone to gradually increase its length.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Internal Lengthening Nail\", \"description\": \"A telescopic rod placed inside the bone gradually lengthens it from within.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Ilizarov Technique\", \"description\": \"A specialized circular external fixation system used for complex limb lengthening and deformity correction.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend regular follow-up visits for monitoring bone growth\", \"Perform physiotherapy exercises to maintain mobility\", \"Keep surgical areas clean to prevent infection\", \"Avoid excessive strain on the affected limb\", \"Maintain a balanced diet to support bone healing\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Delayed bone healing\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Nerve or muscle irritation\"]','<p>Limb lengthening surgery helps correct limb differences and improve balance and mobility. The bone gradually grows and strengthens during the healing process. Physiotherapy is essential to maintain joint flexibility and muscle strength. With proper care, patients achieve improved physical function. Long-term results are generally positive.</p>','<p>Limb lengthening surgery is an advanced orthopedic procedure that can effectively correct limb discrepancies and improve mobility. With proper surgical care and rehabilitation, patients can achieve better balance and functional outcomes.</p>','Limb Lengthening Surgery | Bone Lengthening Treatment','Learn about Limb Lengthening Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','limb lengthening surgery, bone lengthening procedure, limb discrepancy correction, orthopedic limb lengthening',1,'2026-03-17 08:16:42','2026-04-14 10:55:42',NULL),(64,'Scoliosis Correction Surgery','procedures/banners/77015064-7ae6-4f9e-8b68-ae6d413db39a.webp',NULL,'scoliosis-correction-surgery','<p>Scoliosis correction surgery is performed to treat abnormal curvature of the spine and restore proper spinal alignment.</p>','<p>Scoliosis correction surgery is an orthopedic procedure used to straighten and stabilize a curved spine. The surgery typically involves placing metal rods, screws, or other implants along the spine to correct alignment and prevent the curvature from worsening.</p>','[\"Uneven shoulders\", \"Curved spine\", \"Back pain\", \"Difficulty standing straight\"]','[\"Congenital spine abnormalities\", \"Neuromuscular disorders\", \"Idiopathic scoliosis\"]','[\"Genetic predisposition\", \"Abnormal spinal development\", \"Neuromuscular diseases such as cerebral palsy\", \"Rapid growth during adolescence\"]','[\"Regular spinal checkups during growth years\", \"Early detection and monitoring of spinal curvature\", \"Use of braces when recommended by doctors\", \"Maintaining good posture\"]','[\"Physical examination of spine alignment\", \"X-ray imaging to measure spinal curvature\", \"MRI scan to evaluate spinal cord and nerves\", \"CT scan for detailed spinal structure analysis\"]','<p>During scoliosis correction surgery, the surgeon uses metal rods, screws, and other implants to straighten the spine and stabilize it in the corrected position. Bone grafts may also be used to fuse parts of the spine and prevent further curvature.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Spinal Fusion for Scoliosis\", \"description\": \"A procedure where vertebrae are fused together to maintain proper spinal alignment.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Posterior Spinal Fusion\", \"description\": \"The spine is corrected and stabilized through an incision in the back.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Anterior Spinal Fusion\", \"description\": \"A surgical approach through the front of the body to correct spinal curvature.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy and rehabilitation exercises\", \"Avoid heavy lifting during recovery\", \"Maintain proper posture and spinal support\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up visits with the surgeon\", \"Take medications as prescribed\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Nerve injury\", \"Implant complications\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]','<p>Scoliosis surgery helps improve spinal alignment and posture. Many patients experience better balance and reduced back pain after recovery. Physiotherapy helps strengthen spinal muscles and maintain flexibility. Early treatment prevents progression of spinal curvature. Long-term outcomes are usually very good.</p>','<p>Scoliosis correction surgery is an effective treatment for severe spinal curvature. With proper surgical care and rehabilitation, patients can achieve improved posture, spinal stability, and quality of life.</p>','Scoliosis Correction Surgery | Spine Curvature Treatment','Learn about Scoliosis Correction Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','scoliosis surgery, scoliosis correction surgery, spinal curvature treatment, spinal fusion scoliosis',1,'2026-03-17 08:17:49','2026-04-14 12:28:51',NULL),(65,'Clubfoot Correction Surgery','procedures/banners/90eb518a-4620-4ef0-b9bc-b9526b62c988.webp',NULL,'clubfoot-correction-surgery','<p>Clubfoot correction surgery is performed to treat a congenital condition where a baby&#039;s foot is twisted out of its normal position.</p>','<p>Clubfoot correction surgery is an orthopedic procedure used to treat congenital clubfoot (talipes equinovarus), a condition where a baby’s foot is twisted inward and downward. The surgery helps realign the bones, tendons, and ligaments of the foot so that the child can walk normally as they grow.</p>','[\"Twisted or inward-turned foot\", \"Difficulty placing foot flat on the ground\", \"Abnormal foot shape\"]','[\"Congenital deformity\", \"Genetic factors\"]','[\"Family history of clubfoot\", \"Genetic disorders affecting bone development\", \"Abnormal fetal positioning during pregnancy\", \"Neuromuscular conditions\"]','[\"Early screening of newborns for foot deformities\", \"Regular pediatric orthopedic checkups\", \"Prompt treatment using casting or braces\", \"Parental awareness of congenital conditions\"]','[\"Physical examination of the infant’s foot\", \"Assessment of foot alignment and flexibility\", \"X-ray imaging if required\", \"Evaluation by a pediatric orthopedic specialist\"]','<p>Clubfoot correction surgery involves carefully adjusting the bones, tendons, and ligaments of the foot to restore proper alignment. In some cases, surgical release of tight tendons or repositioning of bones may be necessary to correct the deformity.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Soft Tissue Release Surgery\", \"description\": \"Tight tendons and ligaments around the foot are released to correct the deformity.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Tendon Transfer Surgery\", \"description\": \"A tendon is repositioned to help balance the muscles of the foot.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Osteotomy for Clubfoot\", \"description\": \"Bone reshaping surgery used in severe or recurrent cases.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow doctor instructions for casting and bracing\", \"Ensure proper use of corrective footwear\", \"Perform physiotherapy exercises if recommended\", \"Attend scheduled pediatric orthopedic follow-ups\", \"Monitor foot growth and development\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Recurrence of deformity\", \"Joint stiffness\", \"Scar formation\"]','<p>Clubfoot surgery helps children achieve normal foot alignment and improved mobility. Early treatment allows better growth and development of the foot. Physiotherapy and supportive footwear help maintain correction. Most children are able to walk and participate in activities normally. Long-term results are very encouraging.</p>','<p>Clubfoot correction surgery is an effective treatment for congenital foot deformities. With early medical intervention and proper follow-up care, children can achieve normal foot function and lead active lives.</p>','Clubfoot Correction Surgery | Congenital Clubfoot Treatment','Learn about Clubfoot Correction Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','clubfoot correction surgery, congenital clubfoot treatment, talipes equinovarus surgery, pediatric orthopedic foot surgery',1,'2026-03-17 08:19:13','2026-04-14 10:52:21',NULL),(66,'Joint Replacement Revision Surgery','procedures/banners/f9b0e5ae-5ad4-4026-b728-a4ad8784b39b.webp',NULL,'joint-replacement-revision-surgery','<p>Joint replacement revision surgery is performed when a previously implanted artificial joint becomes worn, loose, or infected and needs replacement.</p>','<p>Joint replacement revision surgery is an orthopedic procedure performed to replace or repair an existing artificial joint implant that has worn out, loosened, or become infected. The surgeon removes the old implant and replaces it with a new prosthetic joint to restore stability and function.</p>','[\"Persistent joint pain\", \"Swelling\", \"Difficulty moving the joint\", \"Instability of the implant\"]','[\"Implant wear over time\", \"Infection\", \"Implant loosening\"]','[\"Long-term use of artificial joints\", \"Joint infections\", \"Mechanical stress on the implant\", \"Previous joint replacement complications\"]','[\"Regular follow-up visits after joint replacement surgery\", \"Maintaining a healthy body weight\", \"Avoiding excessive stress on artificial joints\", \"Following recommended physiotherapy exercises\"]','[\"Physical examination of joint stability\", \"X-ray imaging to evaluate implant position\", \"MRI or CT scan for detailed joint assessment\", \"Blood tests to detect infection\"]','<p>During revision surgery, the surgeon removes the worn or damaged implant and replaces it with a new prosthetic joint. Additional procedures such as bone grafting or reinforcement of surrounding tissues may also be required to ensure stability.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Knee Replacement Revision\", \"description\": \"Replacement of a failed or worn-out artificial knee joint.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Hip Replacement Revision\", \"description\": \"Replacement of a failed artificial hip joint with a new implant.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Partial Revision Surgery\", \"description\": \"Only the damaged component of the artificial joint is replaced.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow physiotherapy and rehabilitation programs\", \"Take prescribed medications as directed\", \"Avoid excessive stress on the new implant\", \"Maintain proper joint care and hygiene\", \"Attend scheduled follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Blood clots\", \"Implant complications\", \"Nerve damage (rare)\"]','<p>Revision surgery helps restore joint function when the original implant fails. Modern surgical techniques improve implant durability and performance. Physiotherapy helps regain strength and mobility. Patients often experience improved comfort and movement after recovery. Long-term outcomes depend on overall health and rehabilitation.</p>','<p>Joint replacement revision surgery is an effective treatment for failed or worn artificial joints. With proper surgical care and rehabilitation, patients can regain joint stability and improve their quality of life.</p>','Joint Replacement Revision Surgery | Implant Replacement ','Learn about Joint Replacement Revision Surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','joint replacement revision surgery, hip revision surgery, knee revision surgery, artificial joint replacement revision',1,'2026-03-17 08:20:34','2026-04-14 10:54:51',NULL),(67,'Amputation (Upper / Lower Limb)','procedures/banners/f754dcc7-28b1-444f-9e25-cc390dd62fbe.webp',NULL,'amputation-upper-lower-limb','<p>Amputation is a surgical procedure in which a damaged or diseased limb is removed to prevent further complications and improve overall health.</p>','<p>Amputation surgery involves the removal of a severely damaged, infected, or diseased limb to protect the patient’s overall health. The procedure may involve removing part of an arm or leg and is often followed by rehabilitation and prosthetic support to restore mobility and independence.</p>','[\"Severe limb injury\", \"Non-healing infections\", \"Advanced vascular disease\", \"Bone tumors\"]','[\"Severe trauma\", \"Diabetes complications\", \"Infections\", \"Cancer\"]','[\"Severe limb trauma\", \"Peripheral vascular disease\", \"Diabetes-related complications\", \"Malignant bone tumors\"]','[\"Proper management of diabetes and vascular diseases\", \"Early treatment of severe infections\", \"Safety precautions to prevent traumatic injuries\", \"Regular medical monitoring for chronic conditions\"]','[\"Physical examination of the affected limb\", \"Imaging tests such as X-rays or MRI\", \"Blood tests to evaluate infection or disease\", \"Vascular studies to assess blood flow\"]','<p>During amputation surgery, the surgeon removes the damaged portion of the limb while preserving as much healthy tissue as possible. After surgery, rehabilitation programs help patients adapt to prosthetic limbs and regain mobility.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Upper Limb Amputation\", \"description\": \"Removal of part of the arm due to severe injury, infection, or disease.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Lower Limb Amputation\", \"description\": \"Removal of part of the leg due to trauma, vascular disease, or complications from diabetes.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Partial Limb Amputation\", \"description\": \"Removal of a portion of the limb such as fingers, toes, or part of the foot.\"}]','[]','[\"Proper wound care to prevent infection\", \"Regular physiotherapy sessions\", \"Use of prosthetic limbs when recommended\", \"Psychological counseling and emotional support\", \"Follow-up medical appointments for monitoring recovery\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Phantom limb pain\", \"Emotional adjustment challenges\", \"Delayed wound healing\"]','<p>Amputation can help save lives and prevent serious complications from severe injuries or infections. Rehabilitation programs and prosthetic limbs allow many patients to regain independence. Physiotherapy helps improve strength, balance, and mobility. Emotional and psychological support also plays an important role in recovery. With proper rehabilitation, patients can lead active and productive lives.</p>','<p>Amputation surgery is sometimes necessary to protect a patient’s overall health when severe injury or disease affects a limb. With modern prosthetic technology and comprehensive rehabilitation programs, many patients can achieve independence and maintain a high quality of life.</p>','Amputation Surgery | Upper and Lower Limb Removal Treatment','Learn about Amputation surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','amputation surgery, limb amputation, upper limb amputation, lower limb amputation, prosthetic rehabilitation',1,'2026-03-17 08:21:38','2026-04-14 10:50:50',NULL),(68,'Vertebroplasty / Kyphoplasty','procedures/banners/edab19b6-e144-4c8a-9e4e-65b865b2425d.webp',NULL,'vertebroplasty-kyphoplasty','<p>Vertebroplasty and kyphoplasty are minimally invasive procedures used to treat spinal compression fractures, often caused by osteoporosis or trauma.</p>','<p>Vertebroplasty and kyphoplasty are specialized spinal procedures used to stabilize fractured vertebrae. In vertebroplasty, medical-grade bone cement is injected directly into the fractured bone. In kyphoplasty, a balloon is first inserted to restore vertebral height before injecting cement to stabilize the bone.</p>','[\"Severe back pain\", \"Limited spinal movement\", \"Difficulty standing or walking\"]','[\"Osteoporosis\", \"Spinal fractures\", \"Trauma or injury\"]','[\"Severe osteoporosis\", \"Weak or fragile vertebral bones\", \"Spinal trauma or injury\", \"Age-related bone degeneration\"]','[\"Maintain bone health with calcium and vitamin D\", \"Regular exercise to strengthen bones\", \"Early treatment of osteoporosis\", \"Prevent falls and spinal injuries\"]','[\"Physical examination of spinal movement\", \"X-ray imaging to detect vertebral fractures\", \"MRI scan to assess spinal damage\", \"CT scan for detailed bone evaluation\"]','<p>During vertebroplasty or kyphoplasty, a needle is inserted into the fractured vertebra under imaging guidance. Medical bone cement is injected to stabilize the bone and relieve pain. In kyphoplasty, a balloon may be used to restore the vertebral height before cement injection.</p>','[{\"name\": \"1. Vertebroplasty\", \"description\": \"Bone cement is injected directly into the fractured vertebra to stabilize the spine.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Kyphoplasty\", \"description\": \"A balloon is inserted to create space and restore vertebral height before cement injection.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow medical advice regarding activity levels\", \"Maintain proper posture to protect the spine\", \"Take medications for osteoporosis if prescribed\", \"Attend follow-up appointments\", \"Perform recommended physiotherapy exercises\"]','[\"Infection\", \"Cement leakage\", \"Rare nerve injury\"]','<p>These procedures help stabilize spinal fractures and provide rapid pain relief. Patients can regain mobility and return to daily activities quickly. Managing osteoporosis through medication and lifestyle changes helps prevent future fractures. Regular medical checkups help monitor bone health. Long-term outcomes are generally very positive.</p>','<p>Vertebroplasty and kyphoplasty are effective minimally invasive treatments for spinal compression fractures. With proper treatment and bone health management, patients can experience significant pain relief and improved mobility.</p>','Vertebroplasty & Kyphoplasty | Nano Hospital','Learn about Vertebroplasty and Kyphoplasty procedures including symptoms, causes, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.','vertebroplasty, kyphoplasty, spinal compression fracture treatment, vertebral fracture surgery',1,'2026-03-17 11:28:55','2026-03-19 10:16:30',NULL),(69,'Cystoscopy','procedures/banners/179d1d3f-8a77-44dd-a04f-55532492e8c8.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/e67770ed-8c31-4e40-9a0f-bd186ff6c6a4.webp','cystoscopy','<p>Cystoscopy is a diagnostic and therapeutic procedure used to examine the inside of the urinary bladder and urethra. It is performed using a cystoscope, a thin tube with a camera and light at the end, which allows the doctor to directly visualize the urinary tract. This procedure is essential for identifying conditions such as bladder infections, stones, tumors, strictures, and causes of unexplained urinary symptoms. It also helps in performing minor treatments like biopsy or removal of small growths.</p>','<p>Cystoscopy is commonly recommended when patients present with symptoms like blood in urine, recurrent urinary infections, or difficulty in urination. The procedure involves inserting the cystoscope through the urethra into the bladder under local or spinal anesthesia. It provides a clear, real-time view of the bladder lining and helps in accurate diagnosis. It is usually completed within a short duration and does not require a long hospital stay, making it a safe and effective diagnostic tool.</p>','[\"Blood in urine (hematuria)\",\"Frequent urinary infections\",\"Painful urination\",\"Difficulty passing urine\",\"Urinary urgency\",\"Lower abdominal discomfort\"]','[\"Bladder infections\",\"Urinary tract abnormalities\",\"Bladder stones\",\"Tumors in the urinary tract\",\"Urethral strictures\"]','[\"Recurrent urinary tract infections\",\"Smoking\",\"Bladder inflammation\",\"History of urinary stones\",\"Advanced age\"]','[\"Maintain proper hydration\",\"Practice good personal hygiene\",\"Avoid smoking\",\"Treat urinary infections early\",\"Attend regular medical checkups\"]','[\"Urine analysis\",\"Urine culture\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT scan of urinary tract\",\"Cystoscopy examination\"]','<p>Cystoscopy is performed by inserting a cystoscope through the urethra into the bladder. The procedure allows direct visualization of the urinary tract and may also be used to perform biopsies, remove small stones, or treat minor abnormalities. It is generally performed under local or spinal anesthesia and usually takes a short time to complete.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Flexible Cystoscopy\",\"description\":\"A flexible cystoscope is used for diagnostic examination with minimal discomfort.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Rigid Cystoscopy\",\"description\":\"A rigid cystoscope is used for both diagnosis and minor surgical procedures.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Operative Cystoscopy\",\"description\":\"Used for performing procedures such as biopsy, stone removal, or treatment of bladder abnormalities.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink plenty of water\",\"Take prescribed medications\",\"Avoid holding urine\",\"Maintain hygiene\",\"Report fever or severe pain\"]','[\"Mild burning sensation\",\"Bleeding in urine\",\"Urinary tract infection\",\"Temporary discomfort\",\"Rare injury to urethra\"]','<p>Cystoscopy is a safe and reliable procedure with minimal long-term complications. It plays a crucial role in early detection of serious urological conditions, including bladder cancer. Regular monitoring through cystoscopy may be required in certain patients, ensuring timely treatment and better health outcomes.</p>','<p>Cystoscopy is an important diagnostic and therapeutic procedure for evaluating urinary tract conditions. Early diagnosis and proper management through cystoscopy help improve patient outcomes and support long-term urinary health.</p>','Cystoscopy Procedure | Bladder and Urinary Tract Examination','Learn about Cystoscopy procedure including symptoms, risks, diagnosis, treatment overview, post-operative care, and long-term outlook.','cystoscopy procedure, bladder examination, urinary tract diagnosis, flexible cystoscopy, rigid cystoscopy, bladder health',1,'2026-05-06 07:09:44','2026-05-07 10:47:23',NULL),(70,'Ureteric Stenting (DJ Stent)','procedures/banners/00daf268-a39b-44c8-b5bf-dd7c6a8b268c.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/fc4c426f-8370-4d8d-8a10-3d5d1afd4b0c.webp','ureteric-stenting-dj-stent','<p>Ureteric stenting involves placing a thin, flexible tube called a Double J (DJ) stent between the kidney and bladder to ensure proper urine flow. It is commonly used when there is blockage due to stones, swelling, or after surgical procedures. The stent prevents pressure buildup in the kidney and protects it from damage caused by urine obstruction.</p>','<p>When the ureter is blocked, urine cannot pass normally, leading to pain and kidney damage. A DJ stent is inserted using an endoscopic procedure through the urinary tract without any external incision. It helps restore normal urine flow and is usually kept temporarily until the underlying condition is treated. The procedure is quick, effective, and widely used in urology.</p>','[\"Flank pain\",\"Difficulty in urination\",\"Reduced urine flow\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Recurrent infections\",\"Kidney swelling\"]','[\"Kidney stones\",\"Ureteral blockage\",\"Post-surgical swelling\",\"Urinary tract narrowing\",\"Tumors causing obstruction\"]','[\"Untreated kidney stones\",\"Urinary tract infections\",\"Previous urinary surgeries\",\"Inflammation of ureter\",\"Urinary obstruction\"]','[\"Stay hydrated regularly\",\"Treat urinary infections early\",\"Attend routine medical checkups\",\"Follow treatment for kidney stones\",\"Maintain urinary tract health\"]','[\"Urine examination\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT KUB scan\",\"X-ray imaging\",\"Cystoscopy evaluation\"]','<p>A DJ stent is inserted through an endoscopic procedure to maintain urine flow from the kidney to the bladder. The procedure is usually performed under anesthesia without external cuts. The stent relieves obstruction and protects kidney function until the underlying problem is resolved.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Temporary DJ Stenting\",\"description\":\"A short-term stent placement used to relieve temporary urinary obstruction.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Post-Surgical DJ Stenting\",\"description\":\"Placed after urological surgeries to support healing and urine drainage.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Emergency Ureteric Stenting\",\"description\":\"Performed urgently in severe urinary blockage or infection cases.\"}]','[]','[\"Stay well hydrated\",\"Avoid heavy physical activity\",\"Take medications regularly\",\"Attend follow-up for removal\",\"Monitor for fever or pain\"]','[\"Frequent urination\",\"Discomfort or pain\",\"Infection\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Stent displacement (rare)\"]','<p>DJ stents are highly effective in relieving urinary obstruction. Once removed on time, patients usually recover completely without complications. Delayed removal may lead to infection or stone formation, so regular follow-up is essential.</p>','<p>Ureteric stenting with a DJ stent is a safe and effective procedure for relieving urinary obstruction and protecting kidney function. Timely treatment and proper follow-up ensure successful recovery and prevention of complications.</p>','Ureteric Stenting (DJ Stent) | Urinary Obstruction Treatment','Learn about Ureteric Stenting (DJ Stent) procedure including symptoms, risks, diagnosis, treatment overview, recovery, and post-operative care.','DJ stent procedure, ureteric stenting, urinary obstruction treatment, kidney stent, ureter blockage treatment',1,'2026-05-06 07:11:21','2026-05-07 11:07:03',NULL),(71,'ESWL (Extracorporeal Shock Wave Lithotripsy)','procedures/banners/bef3751a-fb68-4faf-9537-01fa58253e59.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/d300b12d-81c3-4c70-ae3f-f988678982ee.webp','eswl-extracorporeal-shock-wave-lithotripsy','<p>ESWL is a non-invasive procedure used to treat kidney stones by breaking them into smaller fragments using high-energy shock waves. These fragments are then naturally passed through urine. It is one of the most preferred treatments for small to medium-sized stones as it avoids surgery and promotes faster recovery.</p>','<p>Kidney stones can cause severe pain and urinary blockage. ESWL uses external shock waves focused on the stone to fragment it without making any incision. The procedure is usually done on an outpatient basis and requires minimal anesthesia. It is safe, effective, and allows patients to return to normal activities quickly.</p>','[\"Severe flank pain\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Nausea or vomiting\",\"Pain during urination\",\"Frequent urge to urinate\",\"Lower abdominal pain\"]','[\"Kidney stone formation\",\"Dehydration\",\"High mineral concentration in urine\",\"Dietary factors\",\"Urinary tract abnormalities\"]','[\"Low water intake\",\"Family history of kidney stones\",\"Obesity\",\"High salt diet\",\"Recurrent urinary infections\"]','[\"Drink plenty of water daily\",\"Reduce salt intake\",\"Maintain a healthy diet\",\"Avoid dehydration\",\"Follow medical advice for stone prevention\"]','[\"Urine analysis\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT KUB scan\",\"X-ray imaging\",\"Blood tests\"]','<p>ESWL uses externally generated shock waves to break kidney stones into smaller fragments. These fragments are then naturally passed through urine over time. The procedure does not involve surgical cuts and is usually completed within a short duration under minimal anesthesia.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Standard ESWL\",\"description\":\"Used for small to medium-sized kidney stones using focused shock waves.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Ultrasound-Guided ESWL\",\"description\":\"Shock waves are guided using ultrasound imaging for accurate targeting.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Fluoroscopy-Guided ESWL\",\"description\":\"X-ray guidance is used during the procedure to locate and fragment stones.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink plenty of water\",\"Take pain relief medications\",\"Filter urine if advised\",\"Avoid heavy work\",\"Follow-up scans\"]','[\"Incomplete stone removal\",\"Pain during passage of fragments\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Temporary kidney injury\",\"Rare obstruction\"]','<p>ESWL is highly effective for selected patients. With proper hydration and dietary modifications, recurrence of stones can be reduced significantly, ensuring long-term kidney health.</p>','<p>ESWL is a safe and effective non-invasive treatment for kidney stones. Early treatment, proper hydration, and lifestyle modifications help ensure successful recovery and reduce the chances of future stone formation.</p>','ESWL Treatment for Kidney Stones | Shock Wave Lithotripsy','Learn about ESWL treatment including symptoms, kidney stone diagnosis, risks, recovery, and post-operative care for shock wave lithotripsy.','ESWL treatment, extracorporeal shock wave lithotripsy, kidney stone treatment, non surgical kidney stone removal, lithotripsy procedure',1,'2026-05-06 07:12:13','2026-05-07 11:08:03',NULL),(73,'URSL (Ureteroscopy with Laser Lithotripsy)','procedures/banners/c1ede0bb-b619-443c-8e80-fb48f96b1602.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/56f7e99b-f4c9-452a-9495-5cb8770e6b73.webp','ursl-ureteroscopy-with-laser-lithotripsy','<p>URSL is a minimally invasive procedure used to remove stones from the ureter using a thin scope and laser technology. The scope is passed through the natural urinary pathway, and the stone is broken into smaller pieces for removal or natural passage.</p>','<p>Ureteric stones can block urine flow and cause severe pain. URSL allows direct visualization and treatment of stones without any incision. A laser is used to break the stone into fine particles. It is a highly effective and commonly performed procedure with quick recovery.</p>','[\"Severe flank pain\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Difficulty urinating\",\"Burning sensation\",\"Nausea\",\"Urinary urgency\"]','[\"Ureteric stones\",\"Dehydration\",\"High mineral concentration in urine\",\"Poor dietary habits\",\"Recurrent urinary tract infections\"]','[\"History of kidney stones\",\"Low fluid intake\",\"Obesity\",\"High salt diet\",\"Family history of stones\"]','[\"Drink adequate water daily\",\"Maintain a balanced diet\",\"Reduce salt intake\",\"Treat urinary infections early\",\"Follow medical advice for stone prevention\"]','[\"Urine examination\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT KUB scan\",\"X-ray imaging\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>URSL involves inserting a thin ureteroscope through the urinary tract to directly visualize the stone. A laser is then used to break the stone into smaller fragments, which are either removed or allowed to pass naturally through urine. The procedure is minimally invasive and usually performed under anesthesia.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Semi-Rigid URSL\",\"description\":\"Used for stones located in the lower and middle ureter using a semi-rigid ureteroscope.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Flexible URSL\",\"description\":\"A flexible scope is used to access stones in the upper ureter or kidney.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Laser Lithotripsy URSL\",\"description\":\"Laser energy is used to fragment stones into fine particles for easier removal.\"}]','[]','[\"Maintain hydration\",\"Take antibiotics\",\"Avoid strenuous activity\",\"Monitor urine output\",\"Follow-up visits\"]','[\"Infection\",\"Ureter injury\",\"Bleeding\",\"Stricture formation\",\"Residual stones\"]','<p>URSL provides excellent outcomes with high success rates. Preventive care and lifestyle changes help reduce the chances of stone recurrence.</p>','<p>URSL is a safe and effective minimally invasive treatment for ureteric stones. Proper follow-up, hydration, and lifestyle modifications support faster recovery and help prevent future stone formation.</p>','URSL Procedure | Ureteroscopy with Laser Lithotripsy ','Learn about URSL procedure including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and treatment for ureteric stones using laser lithotripsy.','URSL procedure, ureteroscopy with laser lithotripsy, ureter stone treatment, laser stone removal, minimally invasive stone surgery',1,'2026-05-06 07:12:50','2026-05-07 11:09:14',NULL),(74,'RIRS (Retrograde Intrarenal Surgery)','procedures/banners/c473986a-6a5e-4484-858a-a275dcdc1a15.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/b55b2938-e2e3-405d-bcf6-1a0a1fed9814.webp','rirs-retrograde-intrarenal-surgery','<p>RIRS is an advanced procedure used to treat kidney stones without any incision. A flexible scope is passed through the urinary tract into the kidney, where a laser is used to break the stones into fine particles.</p>','<p>RIRS is ideal for treating stones located inside the kidney that are difficult to reach by other methods. It offers high precision and minimal discomfort. The procedure is safe, effective, and allows faster recovery compared to traditional surgery.</p>','[\"Kidney pain\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Recurrent infections\",\"Nausea\",\"Urinary discomfort\",\"Reduced urine flow\"]','[\"Kidney stone formation\",\"Dehydration\",\"High mineral content in urine\",\"Poor dietary habits\",\"Recurrent urinary tract infections\"]','[\"Family history of kidney stones\",\"Low fluid intake\",\"Obesity\",\"High salt consumption\",\"Metabolic disorders\"]','[\"Drink sufficient water daily\",\"Maintain a healthy diet\",\"Reduce salt intake\",\"Treat urinary infections early\",\"Follow preventive medical advice\"]','[\"Urine examination\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT KUB scan\",\"X-ray imaging\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>RIRS involves inserting a flexible ureteroscope through the natural urinary passage into the kidney. A laser is used to fragment kidney stones into tiny particles, which are later passed naturally through urine. The procedure avoids external cuts and supports quicker recovery.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Flexible RIRS\",\"description\":\"A flexible ureteroscope is used to access and treat stones within the kidney.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Laser RIRS\",\"description\":\"Laser technology is used to break kidney stones into fine fragments.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Dusting Technique RIRS\",\"description\":\"Stones are converted into fine dust-like particles for natural passage through urine.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink adequate fluids\",\"Take prescribed medicines\",\"Rest for few days\",\"Avoid heavy lifting\",\"Follow-up imaging\"]','[\"Infection\",\"Bleeding\",\"Incomplete stone removal\",\"Rare ureter injury\"]','<p>RIRS is highly successful with minimal complications. Patients can return to normal activities quickly, and proper preventive measures reduce recurrence risk.</p>','<p>RIRS is a safe and effective minimally invasive procedure for treating kidney stones. Early treatment, proper hydration, and lifestyle changes help achieve successful recovery and reduce future stone recurrence.</p>','RIRS Procedure | Retrograde Intrarenal Surgery for Kidney ','Learn about RIRS procedure including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and minimally invasive treatment for kidney stones.','RIRS procedure, retrograde intrarenal surgery, kidney stone laser treatment, minimally invasive kidney stone surgery, flexible ureteroscopy',1,'2026-05-06 07:13:35','2026-05-07 11:10:58',NULL),(75,'PCNL (Percutaneous Nephrolithotomy)','procedures/banners/d662212a-e9a8-4b8e-a147-7656384b07f9.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/68cbbb96-1d9d-4a47-a8b4-5dfcefd9dd24.webp','pcnl-percutaneous-nephrolithotomy','<p>PCNL is a surgical procedure used to remove large or complex kidney stones that cannot be treated effectively with non-invasive methods. It involves creating a small incision in the back to access the kidney directly. A special instrument is used to break the stone and remove the fragments. This procedure is considered the gold standard for treating large kidney stones and ensures maximum stone clearance in a single session.</p>','<p>When kidney stones grow large, they can block urine flow and damage kidney function. PCNL allows direct access to the kidney through a small tract created in the skin. A nephroscope is inserted to visualize and remove stones. The procedure is performed under anesthesia and requires short hospitalization. It is highly effective for complete stone removal.</p>','[\"Severe back or flank pain\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Recurrent urinary infections\",\"Nausea and vomiting\",\"Difficulty passing urine\",\"Kidney swelling\"]','[\"Large kidney stones\",\"Dehydration\",\"High mineral concentration in urine\",\"Recurrent urinary tract infections\",\"Metabolic disorders\"]','[\"Family history of kidney stones\",\"Low fluid intake\",\"Obesity\",\"High salt diet\",\"Untreated urinary infections\"]','[\"Drink adequate water daily\",\"Maintain a balanced diet\",\"Reduce salt intake\",\"Treat urinary infections promptly\",\"Follow medical advice for stone prevention\"]','[\"Urine examination\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT KUB scan\",\"X-ray imaging\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>PCNL involves creating a small incision in the back to access the kidney directly. A nephroscope is inserted through the tract to visualize the stones, which are then broken into smaller fragments and removed. The procedure is performed under anesthesia and provides effective clearance of large or complex kidney stones.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Standard PCNL\",\"description\":\"A conventional procedure used for removing large kidney stones through a small incision.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Mini PCNL\",\"description\":\"Uses smaller instruments and access tracts to reduce recovery time and discomfort.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Ultra-Mini PCNL\",\"description\":\"A minimally invasive variation using very small instruments for selected stone cases.\"}]','[]','[\"Monitor urine output\",\"Maintain hydration\",\"Take prescribed medications\",\"Avoid heavy lifting\",\"Follow-up imaging\"]','[\"Bleeding\",\"Infection\",\"Injury to kidney\",\"Need for blood transfusion (rare)\",\"Adjacent organ injury (rare)\"]','<p>PCNL offers excellent outcomes with high success rates in removing large stones. With proper dietary changes and medical management, recurrence can be minimized, ensuring long-term kidney health.</p>','<p>PCNL is a highly effective surgical treatment for large and complex kidney stones. Proper follow-up, hydration, and preventive care help ensure successful recovery and reduce the risk of future stone formation.</p>','PCNL Procedure | Percutaneous Nephrolithotomy for Kidney ','Learn about PCNL procedure including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and treatment for large kidney stones.','PCNL procedure, percutaneous nephrolithotomy, large kidney stone treatment, kidney stone surgery, minimally invasive kidney stone removal',1,'2026-05-06 07:14:18','2026-05-07 11:12:33',NULL),(76,'Mini / Ultra-mini PCNL','procedures/banners/086158a6-9c36-44ec-9371-fa111be4db50.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/896369fc-7382-4be6-ae54-1c3f2c14f837.webp','mini-ultra-mini-pcnl','<p>Mini and ultra-mini PCNL are advanced versions of standard PCNL that use smaller instruments and smaller access tracts to remove kidney stones. These techniques reduce tissue damage, bleeding, and recovery time while maintaining effective stone clearance.</p>','<p>These procedures are ideal for moderate-sized stones and patients who require less invasive options. By using smaller instruments, surgeons can achieve precise stone removal with minimal trauma. Hospital stay and recovery time are shorter compared to conventional PCNL.</p>','[\"Kidney or flank pain\",\"Blood in urine\",\"Urinary infection\",\"Nausea\",\"Urinary discomfort\",\"Reduced urine flow\"]','[\"Moderate-sized kidney stones\",\"Dehydration\",\"High mineral concentration in urine\",\"Urinary tract infections\",\"Metabolic abnormalities\"]','[\"Family history of kidney stones\",\"Low water intake\",\"High salt diet\",\"Obesity\",\"Recurrent urinary infections\"]','[\"Maintain proper hydration\",\"Follow a balanced diet\",\"Reduce excessive salt intake\",\"Treat urinary infections promptly\",\"Attend regular medical checkups\"]','[\"Urine analysis\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT KUB scan\",\"X-ray imaging\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>Mini and ultra-mini PCNL procedures involve creating a small tract through the skin into the kidney using smaller instruments compared to standard PCNL. Stones are visualized, fragmented, and removed with minimal trauma, resulting in reduced pain, bleeding, and faster recovery.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Mini PCNL\",\"description\":\"Uses smaller access tracts and instruments for effective removal of moderate-sized kidney stones.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Ultra-mini PCNL\",\"description\":\"A more minimally invasive variation using ultra-small instruments for selected stone cases.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Super-mini PCNL\",\"description\":\"An advanced technique designed to reduce bleeding and hospital stay while ensuring stone clearance.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink plenty of fluids\",\"Take medications as prescribed\",\"Avoid strenuous activity\",\"Monitor urine\",\"Attend follow-up visits\"]','[\"Mild bleeding\",\"Infection\",\"Residual stones\",\"Temporary pain\"]','<p>Mini PCNL provides effective stone removal with faster recovery. Patients experience less pain and complications, making it a preferred option in suitable cases.</p>','<p>Mini and ultra-mini PCNL are safe and effective minimally invasive procedures for kidney stone removal. Proper hydration, follow-up care, and lifestyle modifications help ensure successful recovery and prevent stone recurrence.</p>','Mini PCNL Procedure | Ultra-mini PCNL for Kidney Stones','Learn about Mini and Ultra-mini PCNL procedures including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and minimally invasive kidney stone treatment.','mini PCNL, ultra mini PCNL, kidney stone removal, minimally invasive kidney stone surgery, advanced PCNL procedure',1,'2026-05-06 07:15:13','2026-05-07 11:13:33',NULL),(77,'TURP (Transurethral Resection of Prostate)','procedures/banners/5dcb38ed-9b96-4008-96fb-b77c3539c992.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/d1edd5fc-dff6-4f4d-8a81-7d32c2f3228a.webp','turp-transurethral-resection-of-prostate','<p>TURP is a surgical procedure used to treat an enlarged prostate (benign prostatic hyperplasia). It involves removing excess prostate tissue through the urethra using a special instrument. This helps relieve urinary obstruction and improves urine flow.</p>','<p>An enlarged prostate can block urine flow and cause symptoms like difficulty urinating and frequent urination. TURP is performed without any external incision and is considered the standard treatment for moderate to severe prostate enlargement. The procedure significantly improves quality of life.</p>','[\"Difficulty starting urination\",\"Weak urine stream\",\"Frequent urination\",\"Night-time urination\",\"Incomplete bladder emptying\",\"Urgency\"]','[\"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)\",\"Age-related prostate enlargement\",\"Hormonal changes\",\"Family history of prostate problems\",\"Urinary obstruction\"]','[\"Increasing age\",\"Family history of prostate enlargement\",\"Obesity\",\"Diabetes\",\"Sedentary lifestyle\"]','[\"Maintain a healthy lifestyle\",\"Exercise regularly\",\"Limit caffeine and alcohol intake\",\"Attend regular health checkups\",\"Seek early treatment for urinary symptoms\"]','[\"Digital rectal examination\",\"Urine analysis\",\"PSA blood test\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"Uroflowmetry test\"]','<p>TURP involves inserting a resectoscope through the urethra to remove excess prostate tissue causing urinary obstruction. The procedure improves urine flow and relieves urinary symptoms without requiring external incisions. It is performed under anesthesia and usually requires short hospitalization.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Monopolar TURP\",\"description\":\"Traditional TURP procedure using monopolar electrical energy to remove prostate tissue.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Bipolar TURP\",\"description\":\"An advanced TURP technique using bipolar energy with reduced risk of complications.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Laser-Assisted TURP\",\"description\":\"Laser technology is used along with TURP techniques for precise tissue removal.\"}]','[]','[\"Maintain fluid intake\",\"Avoid heavy lifting\",\"Monitor urine color\",\"Follow catheter care instructions\",\"Attend follow-up\"]','[\"Bleeding\",\"Infection\",\"Retrograde ejaculation\",\"Temporary urinary incontinence\",\"Rare erectile dysfunction\"]','<p>TURP provides long-lasting relief from urinary symptoms. Most patients experience significant improvement in urine flow and overall comfort.</p>','<p>TURP is a highly effective surgical treatment for enlarged prostate causing urinary obstruction. Proper post-operative care and follow-up help ensure smooth recovery and long-term symptom relief.</p>','TURP Procedure | Enlarged Prostate Treatment Surgery','Learn about TURP procedure including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and treatment for enlarged prostate (BPH).','TURP procedure, enlarged prostate surgery, BPH treatment, transurethral resection of prostate, prostate enlargement treatment',1,'2026-05-06 07:15:54','2026-05-07 11:16:40',NULL),(78,'Laser Prostate Surgery (HoLEP / ThuLEP)','procedures/banners/acf2e8ed-281b-4ada-bfcd-aa5c3cf87923.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/7836fc27-22be-4368-9065-58d3768bbadb.webp','laser-prostate-surgery-holep-thulep','Laser prostate surgery is a minimally invasive treatment used to remove enlarged prostate tissue using laser energy.','Procedures such as HoLEP and ThuLEP precisely remove obstructing prostate tissue while minimizing bleeding.','[{\"value\":\"Poor urine flow\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty emptying the bladder\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary urgency\"},{\"value\":\"Night-time urination\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Laser Prostate Surgery (HoLEP \\/ ThuLEP) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary burning during urination\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding or blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary tract infection\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary urinary leakage\"},{\"value\":\"Retrograde ejaculation\"}]','[]','[]','Laser prostate surgery removes enlarged tissue while reducing bleeding risk.','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Increase water intake after surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid strenuous activities temporarily\"},{\"value\":\"Take antibiotics if prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor urinary symptoms carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Attend scheduled follow-up appointments\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary burning during urination\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding or blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary tract infection\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary urinary leakage\"},{\"value\":\"Retrograde ejaculation\"}]','Laser prostate surgery provides effective long-term relief with faster recovery.','Laser prostate surgery is a minimally invasive option for enlarged prostate treatment.','Laser Prostate Surgery','Learn about HoLEP and ThuLEP laser prostate surgery.','HoLEP, ThuLEP, laser prostate surgery',1,'2026-05-06 07:16:35','2026-07-29 00:28:07',NULL),(79,'TUIP (Transurethral Incision of Prostate)','procedures/banners/348bf79f-cbb6-4653-9dca-c7048f40991a.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/04b39136-30cd-4dea-8700-0f8d2e9b37eb.webp','tuip-transurethral-incision-of-prostate','<p>TUIP is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat mild to moderate prostate enlargement. Instead of removing tissue, small cuts are made in the prostate to relieve pressure on the urethra.</p>','<p>TUIP is typically recommended for younger patients or those with smaller prostates. It improves urine flow with less risk of complications compared to TURP. The procedure is quick and requires minimal recovery time.</p>','[\"Difficulty urinating\",\"Weak urine stream\",\"Frequent urination\",\"Urgency\",\"Night urination\",\"Incomplete emptying\"]','[\"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)\",\"Age-related prostate enlargement\",\"Hormonal imbalance\",\"Urinary obstruction\",\"Family history of prostate problems\"]','[\"Increasing age\",\"Obesity\",\"Diabetes\",\"Sedentary lifestyle\",\"Family history of enlarged prostate\"]','[\"Maintain a healthy lifestyle\",\"Exercise regularly\",\"Limit caffeine and alcohol intake\",\"Attend regular prostate screenings\",\"Seek early treatment for urinary symptoms\"]','[\"Digital rectal examination\",\"PSA blood test\",\"Urine analysis\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"Uroflowmetry test\"]','<p>TUIP involves inserting a specialized instrument through the urethra and making small incisions in the prostate tissue to reduce pressure on the urethra. This improves urine flow without removing prostate tissue and helps relieve urinary symptoms effectively.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Standard TUIP\",\"description\":\"Small incisions are made in the prostate to relieve urinary obstruction.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Electrosurgical TUIP\",\"description\":\"Electrical energy is used to perform precise incisions in the prostate tissue.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Laser-Assisted TUIP\",\"description\":\"Laser technology is used to create prostate incisions with minimal bleeding.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink fluids\",\"Avoid heavy lifting\",\"Take medications\",\"Monitor symptoms\",\"Follow-up\"]','[\"Bleeding\",\"Infection\",\"Retrograde ejaculation\",\"Temporary discomfort\"]','<p>TUIP provides good symptom relief in selected patients. It has fewer complications and faster recovery compared to more invasive procedures.</p>','<p>TUIP is a safe and effective minimally invasive procedure for treating mild to moderate prostate enlargement. Proper follow-up and lifestyle management help ensure long-term urinary symptom relief and improved quality of life.</p>','TUIP Procedure | Minimally Invasive Enlarged Prostate ','Learn about TUIP procedure including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and treatment for enlarged prostate (BPH).','TUIP procedure, transurethral incision of prostate, enlarged prostate treatment, BPH surgery, minimally invasive prostate procedure',1,'2026-05-06 07:17:31','2026-05-07 11:20:51',NULL),(80,'Cystolitholapaxy','procedures/banners/45cdcf3f-b1a0-427a-b421-d9d13966a64b.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/881ba8be-38f7-4fe7-85f2-b39de4ebe439.webp','cystolitholapaxy','Cystolitholapaxy is a procedure used to break and remove bladder stones.','A cystoscope is inserted through the urethra and stones are broken into fragments before removal.','[{\"value\":\"Painful urination\"},{\"value\":\"Blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"},{\"value\":\"Lower abdominal discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Interrupted urine flow\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Cystolitholapaxy is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bladder injury\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary tract infection\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete stone removal\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrence of bladder stones\"}]','[]','[]','Cystolitholapaxy removes bladder stones and restores urine flow.','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Drink extra fluids to flush the bladder\"},{\"value\":\"Take antibiotics if prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for fever or severe pain\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid strenuous activities briefly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up imaging if advised\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bladder injury\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary tract infection\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete stone removal\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrence of bladder stones\"}]','Most patients experience complete symptom relief after bladder stone removal.','Cystolitholapaxy effectively removes bladder stones and improves urinary symptoms.','Cystolitholapaxy','Learn about bladder stone removal through cystolitholapaxy.','cystolitholapaxy, bladder stone removal',1,'2026-05-06 07:18:07','2026-07-29 00:28:07',NULL),(81,'TURBT (Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor)','procedures/banners/67271022-67a8-450c-a9bf-dcc811b87529.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/f76b8522-d768-4581-ba19-c7affe350637.webp','turbt-transurethral-resection-of-bladder-tumor','<p>TURBT is a procedure used to diagnose and treat bladder tumors. The tumor is removed through the urethra using a special instrument, and tissue is sent for biopsy.</p>','<p>This procedure is crucial for early detection and management of bladder cancer. It allows both removal and staging of tumors. It is minimally invasive and does not require external incision.</p>','[\"Blood in urine\",\"Frequent urination\",\"Painful urination\",\"Urgency\",\"Pelvic discomfort\",\"Recurrent infections\"]','[\"Bladder tumors\",\"Smoking\",\"Exposure to industrial chemicals\",\"Chronic bladder irritation\",\"Recurrent urinary infections\"]','[\"Smoking history\",\"Advanced age\",\"Exposure to harmful chemicals\",\"Family history of bladder cancer\",\"Chronic urinary tract irritation\"]','[\"Avoid smoking\",\"Maintain proper hydration\",\"Limit exposure to harmful chemicals\",\"Treat urinary infections promptly\",\"Attend regular medical checkups\"]','[\"Urine analysis\",\"Urine cytology\",\"Ultrasound scan\",\"CT scan\",\"Cystoscopy examination\"]','<p>TURBT involves inserting a resectoscope through the urethra to visualize and remove bladder tumors. The removed tissue is sent for biopsy to determine the tumor type and stage. The procedure is minimally invasive and plays an important role in diagnosis, treatment, and staging of bladder cancer.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Diagnostic TURBT\",\"description\":\"Performed to obtain tissue samples for biopsy and confirm bladder tumor diagnosis.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Therapeutic TURBT\",\"description\":\"Used to completely remove visible bladder tumors and improve treatment outcomes.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Repeat TURBT\",\"description\":\"A follow-up procedure performed to evaluate residual or recurrent tumors.\"}]','[]','[\"Monitor urine\",\"Drink fluids\",\"Avoid heavy work\",\"Follow-up cystoscopy\",\"Take medications\"]','[\"Bleeding\",\"Infection\",\"Bladder perforation (rare)\",\"Tumor recurrence\"]','<p>Outcome depends on tumor type and stage. Regular follow-up is essential to detect recurrence early and ensure effective treatment.</p>','<p>TURBT is a highly effective minimally invasive procedure for diagnosing and treating bladder tumors. Early detection, proper treatment, and regular follow-up significantly improve long-term outcomes and help manage bladder cancer effectively.</p>','TURBT Procedure | Bladder Tumor Removal and Diagnosis','Learn about TURBT procedure including symptoms, diagnosis, risks, recovery, and bladder tumor treatment.','TURBT procedure, bladder tumor removal, bladder cancer treatment, transurethral resection bladder tumor, cystoscopy bladder tumor surgery',1,'2026-05-06 07:19:17','2026-05-07 11:51:53',NULL),(82,'Nephrectomy (Partial or Radical)','procedures/banners/499612d2-c82c-4f8c-91e9-04be62863e82.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/3ac24d35-3d8e-4ba9-9899-6a80b3c24e0a.webp','nephrectomy-partial-or-radical','Nephrectomy is a surgical procedure involving removal of part or all of a kidney.','Partial nephrectomy removes only diseased tissue while radical nephrectomy removes the entire kidney.','[{\"value\":\"Kidney tumors\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent flank pain\"},{\"value\":\"Blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent kidney infections\"},{\"value\":\