tectomy, prostate cancer surgery',1,'2026-05-06 07:23:37','2026-07-29 00:28:08',NULL),(87,'Radical Cystectomy with Urinary Diversion','procedures/banners/dec0b4f4-7000-44e7-819d-fbc0f0536f0a.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/b2b3096e-129d-4499-b751-75d915dfbd12.webp','radical-cystectomy-with-urinary-diversion','Radical cystectomy is the surgical removal of the bladder for invasive bladder cancer.','Urinary diversion is created using part of the intestine after bladder removal.','[{\"value\":\"Muscle-invasive bladder cancer\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Severe urinary symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic pain\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent bladder tumors\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Radical Cystectomy with Urinary Diversion is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Major bleeding during surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary leakage complications\"},{\"value\":\"Bowel-related complications\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clot formation\"}]','[]','[]','Radical cystectomy removes the bladder and creates urinary diversion.','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Learn proper stoma or pouch care\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Follow dietary recommendations\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular cancer follow-ups\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for infection or leakage\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Major bleeding during surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary leakage complications\"},{\"value\":\"Bowel-related complications\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clot formation\"}]','Radical cystectomy can improve survival in invasive bladder cancer.','Radical cystectomy is a major surgical treatment for bladder cancer.','Radical Cystectomy','Learn about radical cystectomy with urinary diversion.','radical cystectomy, bladder cancer surgery',1,'2026-05-06 07:24:20','2026-07-29 00:28:08',NULL),(88,'Psychological Counseling','procedures/banners/523f5fba-e176-45dd-bc4c-8f01b0ec946b.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/a62514b8-1790-4ccb-83ee-b1696e0e15e7.webp','psychological-counseling','<p>Psychological counseling is a professional mental health service that helps individuals understand emotional difficulties, stress, behavioral problems, relationship conflicts, and life challenges. It focuses on improving emotional well-being, coping skills, and mental resilience through guided conversations and therapeutic techniques.</p>','<p>Counseling provides a safe and confidential environment where individuals can openly discuss their thoughts, feelings, and concerns. Mental health professionals help patients identify unhealthy patterns, improve communication skills, manage stress, and develop practical solutions for personal and emotional challenges. Counseling may be short-term or long-term depending on the condition and goals.</p>','[\"Persistent sadness or emotional distress\",\"Anxiety, fear, or excessive worrying\",\"Difficulty coping with stress or life changes\",\"Relationship or family conflicts\",\"Loss of motivation or emotional balance\"]','[\"Chronic stress\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Relationship difficulties\",\"Work or academic pressure\",\"Major life changes\"]','[\"Untreated emotional stress\",\"Social isolation\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"Family or relationship conflicts\",\"History of mental health challenges\"]','[\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Maintain healthy social relationships\",\"Seek help early for emotional difficulties\",\"Maintain work-life balance\",\"Engage in regular physical activity and self-care\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Mental health screening questionnaires\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional and cognitive assessment\"]','<p>Psychological counseling involves structured discussions and therapeutic techniques guided by trained mental health professionals. Counseling sessions help individuals understand emotions, manage stress, improve behavior patterns, strengthen relationships, and develop effective coping skills for emotional well-being.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Individual Counseling\",\"description\":\"One-on-one counseling sessions focused on personal emotional and psychological concerns.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Family Counseling\",\"description\":\"Therapy sessions involving family members to improve communication and resolve conflicts.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)\",\"description\":\"A structured therapy approach focused on identifying and changing negative thought patterns and behaviors.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend counseling sessions regularly\",\"Practice recommended coping strategies\",\"Maintain open communication with the therapist\",\"Follow stress management techniques at home\",\"Monitor emotional progress consistently\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during difficult discussions\",\"Temporary increase in emotional sensitivity\",\"Resistance to behavioral changes\",\"Dependency on frequent counseling sessions\",\"Delayed improvement in severe psychiatric conditions\"]','<p>With proper counseling and consistent participation, many individuals experience improved emotional stability, healthier relationships, better coping skills, and enhanced self-confidence. Long-term counseling can significantly improve quality of life and mental wellness.</p>','<p>Psychological counseling is an important mental health service that supports emotional well-being and personal growth. Early intervention, active participation, and consistent therapeutic support help individuals achieve better mental health and improved quality of life.</p>','Psychological Counseling | Mental Health and Emotional ','Learn about Psychological Counseling including symptoms, emotional challenges, therapy approaches, benefits, and long-term mental wellness support.','psychological counseling, mental health counseling, emotional therapy, stress management therapy, counseling services',1,'2026-05-09 07:03:33','2026-05-09 09:57:20',NULL),(89,'Psychotherapy',NULL,NULL,'psychotherapy','Psychotherapy is a structured mental health treatment that helps individuals understand emotions, thoughts, and behaviors affecting their mental well-being. It involves evidence-based therapeutic methods guided by trained professionals.','Psychotherapy is used for depression, anxiety disorders, trauma, personality disorders, addiction, and behavioral issues. Treatment may involve individual, family, or group sessions. Therapists help patients recognize unhealthy thought patterns and develop healthier coping mechanisms.','[\"Persistent emotional distress\",\"Mood swings or emotional instability\",\"Behavioral changes affecting daily life\",\"Difficulty managing trauma or stress\",\"Social withdrawal or isolation\"]','[\"Chronic stress\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Mental health disorders\",\"Relationship conflicts\",\"Substance abuse or addiction\"]','[\"Untreated psychological disorders\",\"Social isolation\",\"Poor emotional coping skills\",\"Family history of mental illness\",\"Long-term emotional stress\"]','[\"Seek early mental health support\",\"Maintain healthy social relationships\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Maintain regular sleep and exercise routines\",\"Avoid substance abuse\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Clinical mental health evaluation\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Cognitive evaluation\",\"Emotional health screening\"]','Psychotherapy involves structured therapeutic sessions conducted by trained mental health professionals. Evidence-based techniques are used to help individuals understand emotions, improve behaviors, manage stress, and develop healthier coping mechanisms for long-term mental wellness.','[{\"name\":\"1. Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)\",\"description\":\"Focuses on identifying and changing unhealthy thought patterns and behaviors.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Psychodynamic Therapy\",\"description\":\"Explores unconscious emotions and past experiences affecting current behavior.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Group Psychotherapy\",\"description\":\"Therapy sessions conducted with multiple individuals facing similar emotional or psychological challenges.\"}]','[\"Emotional improvement develops gradually over sessions\",\"Coping skills strengthen with consistent participation\",\"Behavioral and emotional stability improves over time\",\"Long-term therapy may be required depending on the condition\"]','[\"Continue scheduled therapy sessions\",\"Apply coping techniques in daily life\",\"Maintain healthy routines and sleep patterns\",\"Practice emotional self-awareness\",\"Follow therapist recommendations consistently\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during therapy\",\"Temporary worsening of symptoms initially\",\"Frustration with slow progress\",\"Difficulty discussing traumatic experiences\",\"Inconsistent participation reducing effectiveness\"]','Psychotherapy often improves emotional control, communication, self-esteem, and coping skills. Long-term benefits include reduced psychiatric symptoms, improved relationships, and better psychological resilience.','Psychotherapy is an effective mental health treatment that supports emotional healing, behavioral improvement, and psychological resilience. Consistent participation and professional guidance help individuals achieve long-term mental wellness and improved quality of life.','Psychotherapy Treatment | Mental Health Therapy and Emotional Wellness','Learn about Psychotherapy including symptoms, mental health conditions, therapy approaches, emotional healing, and long-term psychological wellness.','psychotherapy, mental health therapy, cognitive behavioral therapy, emotional wellness treatment, psychological therapy',1,'2026-05-09 07:04:10','2026-05-09 07:04:10',NULL),(90,'Cognitive Behavioral Therapy','procedures/banners/06fc8592-38de-41c7-9071-74db06e54376.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/6ef07c7a-a343-4c6e-b10e-beebe81a0aa9.webp','cognitive-behavioral-therapy','<p>Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) is a structured psychotherapy technique focused on identifying and changing negative thoughts and unhealthy behavioral patterns.</p>','<p>CBT is widely used for anxiety, depression, OCD, phobias, PTSD, and stress-related disorders. The therapy helps individuals understand the relationship between thoughts, emotions, and behaviors. Sessions are goal-oriented and practical.</p>','[\"Negative thinking patterns\",\"Excessive anxiety or fear\",\"Depression and hopelessness\",\"Compulsive behaviors or obsessions\",\"Difficulty managing stress\"]','[\"Chronic stress\",\"Anxiety disorders\",\"Depression\",\"Traumatic experiences\",\"Behavioral and emotional difficulties\"]','[\"Untreated mental health conditions\",\"Poor stress management\",\"Social isolation\",\"Low emotional resilience\",\"Family history of psychiatric disorders\"]','[\"Practice stress management regularly\",\"Seek early mental health support\",\"Maintain healthy social interactions\",\"Follow healthy sleep and exercise routines\",\"Avoid unhealthy coping habits\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Mental health evaluation\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Emotional health screening\",\"Clinical interview\"]','<p>Cognitive Behavioral Therapy involves structured therapy sessions that help individuals recognize negative thought patterns and replace them with healthier behaviors and coping strategies. The therapy is goal-oriented and focuses on practical solutions to improve emotional well-being and daily functioning.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Individual CBT\",\"description\":\"One-on-one therapy sessions focused on personal emotional and behavioral challenges.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Group CBT\",\"description\":\"Therapy sessions conducted in groups for individuals with similar mental health concerns.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Exposure-Based CBT\",\"description\":\"A CBT technique involving gradual exposure to fears or anxiety triggers to reduce emotional distress.\"}]','[]','[\"Practice CBT exercises regularly\",\"Maintain thought journals if advised\",\"Continue behavioral exposure activities\",\"Attend follow-up sessions consistently\",\"Monitor emotional triggers carefully\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort while confronting fears\",\"Resistance to behavioral exercises\",\"Temporary anxiety during exposure techniques\",\"Incomplete results with inconsistent participation\",\"Frustration if progress is gradual\"]','<p>CBT provides long-lasting coping skills that help individuals manage stress, anxiety, depression, and behavioral issues effectively. Many patients experience improved emotional regulation and better daily functioning.</p>','<p>Cognitive Behavioral Therapy is an effective evidence-based treatment for emotional and behavioral challenges. Consistent participation and application of coping strategies help individuals achieve long-term emotional stability and improved mental wellness.</p>','Cognitive Behavioral Therapy | CBT for Mental Health ','Learn about Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) including symptoms, therapy techniques, emotional wellness, coping strategies, and mental health treatment.','cognitive behavioral therapy, CBT therapy, anxiety treatment, depression therapy, mental health counseling',1,'2026-05-09 07:04:43','2026-05-09 10:00:48',NULL),(91,'Dialectical Behavior Therapy','procedures/banners/8f757bc2-69e6-4735-a594-e70290989ed0.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/626af2ff-768f-4f2f-85dd-682fad9aeea0.webp','dialectical-behavior-therapy','<p>Dialectical Behavior Therapy (DBT) is a specialized psychotherapy designed to help individuals regulate emotions, tolerate distress, and improve interpersonal relationships.</p>','<p>DBT is commonly used for borderline personality disorder, self-harm behavior, emotional instability, and severe mood disorders. It combines mindfulness, emotional regulation, distress tolerance, and communication skills training.</p>','[\"Intense emotional reactions\",\"Self-harm tendencies\",\"Relationship instability\",\"Difficulty controlling anger\",\"Impulsive behavior\"]','[\"Emotional trauma\",\"Personality disorders\",\"Chronic stress\",\"Mood disorders\",\"Difficulty coping with emotions\"]','[\"Untreated emotional instability\",\"Social isolation\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"History of self-harm behavior\",\"Severe mood disturbances\"]','[\"Seek early mental health support\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Maintain healthy relationships\",\"Develop positive coping strategies\",\"Attend regular therapy sessions\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Mental health screening\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional regulation assessment\"]','<p>Dialectical Behavior Therapy involves structured psychotherapy sessions focused on mindfulness, emotional regulation, distress tolerance, and interpersonal effectiveness. The therapy helps individuals develop healthier emotional responses, improve coping skills, and reduce harmful behaviors.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Individual DBT\",\"description\":\"One-on-one therapy sessions focused on emotional regulation and behavioral management.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Group Skills Training DBT\",\"description\":\"Group-based sessions teaching mindfulness, distress tolerance, and interpersonal skills.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Comprehensive DBT Program\",\"description\":\"A structured therapy program combining individual sessions, group training, and crisis support.\"}]','[]','[\"Practice mindfulness techniques daily\",\"Follow emotional regulation exercises\",\"Maintain therapy attendance regularly\",\"Use coping strategies during crises\",\"Build healthy support systems\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during sessions\",\"Resistance to behavioral change\",\"Temporary emotional distress\",\"Difficulty maintaining therapy routines\",\"Slow improvement in severe cases\"]','<p>DBT can significantly improve emotional control, reduce self-destructive behaviors, and enhance relationships and social functioning over time.</p>','<p>Dialectical Behavior Therapy is an effective treatment for emotional instability and behavioral challenges. Consistent participation and application of coping strategies help individuals improve emotional well-being, relationships, and overall quality of life.</p>','Dialectical Behavior Therapy | DBT for Emotional Regulation','Learn about Dialectical Behavior Therapy (DBT) including symptoms, emotional regulation techniques, coping skills, and mental health treatment.','dialectical behavior therapy, DBT therapy, emotional regulation treatment, borderline personality disorder therapy, mental health counseling',1,'2026-05-09 07:05:25','2026-05-09 10:02:24',NULL),(92,'Supportive Therapy','procedures/banners/d525342b-313b-465f-9f58-6b16f36b2c66.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/637e5cb3-8bcf-47bd-83a5-4cff7dc87dd2.webp','supportive-therapy','<p>Supportive therapy focuses on providing emotional support, reassurance, encouragement, and practical coping strategies to individuals facing mental health challenges.</p>','<p>This therapy strengthens emotional resilience and helps patients manage stress, illness, grief, and life crises. It is often used alongside other psychiatric treatments.</p>','[\"Emotional stress or sadness\",\"Anxiety related to life events\",\"Difficulty coping with illness\",\"Low self-confidence\",\"Feelings of helplessness\"]','[\"Stressful life events\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Chronic illness\",\"Relationship difficulties\",\"Mental health disorders\"]','[\"Untreated emotional distress\",\"Social isolation\",\"Poor coping skills\",\"Chronic stress exposure\",\"Lack of emotional support\"]','[\"Maintain healthy social relationships\",\"Seek emotional support early\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Follow healthy lifestyle habits\",\"Attend regular mental health checkups\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Mental health screening\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional wellness assessment\"]','<p>Supportive therapy involves guided discussions and emotional support provided by mental health professionals. The therapy focuses on improving coping skills, strengthening emotional resilience, reducing stress, and helping individuals manage daily life challenges more effectively.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Individual Supportive Therapy\",\"description\":\"One-on-one sessions focused on emotional support and coping strategies.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Family Supportive Therapy\",\"description\":\"Therapy sessions involving family members to improve emotional support and communication.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Crisis Supportive Therapy\",\"description\":\"Short-term supportive counseling provided during emotional crises or stressful situations.\"}]','[]','[\"Continue counseling sessions regularly\",\"Practice stress reduction techniques\",\"Engage in social support systems\",\"Follow healthy lifestyle habits\",\"Maintain open communication with therapists\"]','[\"Limited improvement in severe psychiatric disorders\",\"Emotional dependency on therapy\",\"Slow progress in behavioral changes\",\"Reduced effectiveness without patient participation\",\"Temporary emotional discomfort\"]','<p>Supportive therapy improves emotional stability, confidence, coping abilities, and overall psychological well-being.</p>','<p>Supportive therapy is an important mental health treatment that strengthens emotional resilience and coping skills. Consistent participation and professional guidance help individuals achieve better emotional well-being and improved quality of life.</p>','Supportive Therapy | Emotional Support and Mental Wellness','Learn about Supportive Therapy including emotional support techniques, coping strategies, mental wellness benefits, and psychological care.','supportive therapy, emotional support counseling, mental wellness therapy, stress coping therapy, psychological support',1,'2026-05-09 07:06:03','2026-05-09 10:03:59',NULL),(93,'Family Therapy','procedures/banners/3461a043-eee1-4e5e-9f12-8a32dda5e94a.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/b450d9b7-c9b5-4925-b00f-8ac144863dee.webp','family-therapy','<p>Family therapy is a counseling approach that involves family members in the treatment process to improve communication, relationships, and emotional support.</p>','<p>It helps address family conflicts, parenting issues, mental illness impacts, addiction, and communication problems. Therapists guide families toward healthier interactions and conflict resolution.</p>','[\"Frequent family conflicts\",\"Communication breakdown\",\"Emotional stress within the household\",\"Behavioral problems in children\",\"Family tension related to illness or addiction\"]','[\"Relationship conflicts\",\"Mental health disorders\",\"Substance abuse or addiction\",\"Parenting difficulties\",\"Stressful life changes\"]','[\"Poor family communication\",\"Chronic emotional stress\",\"Unresolved family conflicts\",\"Lack of emotional support\",\"Mental health challenges within the family\"]','[\"Maintain open communication within the family\",\"Address conflicts early\",\"Practice healthy coping strategies\",\"Encourage emotional support among family members\",\"Seek professional counseling when needed\"]','[\"Family relationship assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Mental health screening\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Communication pattern assessment\"]','<p>Family therapy involves structured counseling sessions where family members work together with a therapist to improve communication, resolve conflicts, strengthen relationships, and create healthier emotional interactions within the household.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Structural Family Therapy\",\"description\":\"Focuses on improving family structure, boundaries, and interaction patterns.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Strategic Family Therapy\",\"description\":\"Uses practical strategies to address specific family conflicts and behavioral problems.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Systemic Family Therapy\",\"description\":\"Examines family relationships and emotional dynamics to improve overall functioning.\"}]','[]','[\"Practice healthy communication skills\",\"Attend therapy sessions together consistently\",\"Encourage emotional support within the family\",\"Follow conflict-resolution strategies\",\"Maintain positive family routines\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during discussions\",\"Resistance from family members\",\"Temporary increase in conflicts\",\"Incomplete participation reducing effectiveness\",\"Difficulty accepting behavioral changes\"]','<p>Family therapy often strengthens relationships, improves communication, and creates healthier emotional environments for long-term mental wellness.</p>','<p>Family therapy is an effective counseling approach that improves communication, emotional support, and conflict resolution within families. Consistent participation helps create stronger relationships and a healthier emotional environment.</p>','Family Therapy | Counseling for Healthy Family Relationships','Learn about Family Therapy including communication improvement, conflict resolution, emotional support, and mental wellness counseling.','family therapy, family counseling, relationship therapy, conflict resolution counseling, emotional support therapy',1,'2026-05-09 08:14:20','2026-05-09 10:04:50',NULL),(94,'Couples Therapy','procedures/banners/895e4a00-069c-4848-bd19-5a0156d662db.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/6ce4be0b-8c22-4364-bcc0-0b73e0173613.webp','couples-therapy','<p>Couples therapy helps partners resolve conflicts, improve communication, and strengthen emotional and relationship health.</p>','<p>It addresses trust issues, communication problems, emotional distance, relationship stress, and mental health-related relationship challenges.</p>','[\"Frequent arguments\",\"Emotional disconnection\",\"Trust or intimacy problems\",\"Communication difficulties\",\"Stress affecting the relationship\"]','[\"Poor communication\",\"Relationship conflicts\",\"Emotional stress\",\"Trust issues\",\"Mental health challenges\"]','[\"Unresolved relationship conflicts\",\"Emotional disconnection\",\"Chronic stress\",\"Lack of mutual support\",\"Poor coping strategies\"]','[\"Maintain open communication\",\"Address conflicts early\",\"Practice mutual respect and empathy\",\"Spend quality time together\",\"Seek professional help when needed\"]','[\"Relationship assessment\",\"Communication evaluation\",\"Emotional health assessment\",\"Behavioral analysis\",\"Clinical counseling interview\"]','<p>Couples therapy involves structured counseling sessions guided by a trained therapist to improve communication, resolve conflicts, rebuild trust, and strengthen emotional connection between partners. The therapy focuses on healthy relationship patterns and long-term emotional well-being.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Emotionally Focused Couples Therapy\",\"description\":\"Focuses on improving emotional bonding and strengthening relationship attachment.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Behavioral Couples Therapy\",\"description\":\"Uses behavioral techniques to improve communication and conflict resolution.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Cognitive Couples Therapy\",\"description\":\"Helps partners identify and change unhealthy thought patterns affecting the relationship.\"}]','[]','[\"Practice communication techniques daily\",\"Attend sessions consistently\",\"Build mutual emotional support\",\"Follow therapist-guided exercises\",\"Maintain healthy relationship boundaries\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during sessions\",\"Resistance to relationship changes\",\"Temporary emotional tension\",\"Unequal participation by partners\",\"Emotional distress if conflicts intensify initially\"]','<p>Couples therapy can improve relationship satisfaction, emotional bonding, trust, and long-term communication.</p>','<p>Couples therapy is an effective approach for improving communication, emotional connection, and relationship stability. Consistent participation and healthy coping strategies help strengthen long-term relationship health and emotional well-being.</p>','Couples Therapy | Relationship Counseling and Support','Learn about Couples Therapy including communication improvement, relationship counseling, emotional bonding, and conflict resolution support.','couples therapy, relationship counseling, marriage counseling, communication therapy, emotional relationship support',1,'2026-05-09 08:15:26','2026-05-09 10:06:07',NULL),(95,'Group Therapy',NULL,NULL,'group-therapy','Group therapy involves multiple individuals participating in guided therapy sessions led by a mental health professional.','It allows individuals to share experiences, learn coping strategies, and receive emotional support from others facing similar challenges.','[\"Social isolation\",\"Anxiety or depression\",\"Difficulty coping with stress\",\"Emotional distress\",\"Addiction or behavioral challenges\"]','[\"Mental health disorders\",\"Chronic stress\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Substance abuse\",\"Social or relationship difficulties\"]','[\"Lack of social support\",\"Untreated emotional distress\",\"Poor coping skills\",\"Social withdrawal\",\"Behavioral or addiction-related challenges\"]','[\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain healthy social relationships\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Participate in healthy group activities\",\"Follow positive lifestyle habits\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Mental health screening\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional wellness assessment\"]','Group therapy involves structured sessions where individuals with similar emotional or psychological challenges participate together under the guidance of a trained therapist. The therapy promotes emotional support, shared learning, improved coping strategies, and better interpersonal skills.','[{\"name\":\"1. Support Group Therapy\",\"description\":\"Focuses on emotional support and shared experiences among group members.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Cognitive Behavioral Group Therapy\",\"description\":\"Uses CBT techniques within a group setting to improve coping and behavior patterns.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Addiction Recovery Group Therapy\",\"description\":\"Provides structured support and coping strategies for individuals recovering from addiction.\"}]','[\"Emotional support improves gradually over sessions\",\"Social confidence develops with participation\",\"Coping skills strengthen over time\",\"Long-term group participation may improve emotional resilience\"]','[\"Attend sessions regularly\",\"Respect group confidentiality\",\"Participate actively in discussions\",\"Practice learned coping skills\",\"Build healthy peer support systems\"]','[\"Discomfort sharing personal experiences\",\"Fear of judgment from others\",\"Emotional triggering during discussions\",\"Confidentiality concerns\",\"Unequal participation among members\"]','Group therapy enhances social support, emotional understanding, confidence, and coping abilities over time.','Group therapy is an effective mental health treatment that promotes emotional support, social connection, and healthier coping strategies. Consistent participation helps improve emotional well-being and interpersonal functioning.','Group Therapy | Mental Health Support and Counseling','Learn about Group Therapy including emotional support, coping strategies, social connection, and mental health counseling benefits.','group therapy, mental health group counseling, emotional support therapy, addiction group therapy, psychological support groups',1,'2026-05-09 08:16:11','2026-05-09 08:16:11',NULL),(97,'Support Groups','procedures/banners/54891d44-0d3e-402d-a600-7b8e15042c2b.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/ed939e42-eb25-4357-a0de-92a33fd7ac65.webp','support-groups','<p>Support groups are organized gatherings where individuals with similar mental health challenges share experiences, encouragement, and coping strategies.</p>','<p>Support groups help reduce feelings of isolation and provide emotional encouragement for individuals dealing with mental illness, addiction, grief, or trauma.</p>','[\"Loneliness or isolation\",\"Emotional stress\",\"Difficulty coping with illness\",\"Anxiety or depression\",\"Lack of emotional support\"]','[\"Mental health disorders\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Grief or loss\",\"Addiction-related challenges\",\"Chronic stress\"]','[\"Social isolation\",\"Poor emotional coping skills\",\"Lack of support systems\",\"Untreated mental health conditions\",\"Chronic emotional stress\"]','[\"Maintain healthy social relationships\",\"Seek emotional support early\",\"Participate in healthy community activities\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Follow mental health treatment plans consistently\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Mental health evaluation\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional wellness screening\"]','<p>Support groups involve structured meetings where individuals with shared emotional or psychological challenges come together to discuss experiences, receive encouragement, and learn coping strategies. Sessions may be professionally guided or peer-led to promote emotional resilience and social support.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Mental Health Support Groups\",\"description\":\"Support sessions focused on anxiety, depression, and emotional wellness challenges.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Addiction Recovery Support Groups\",\"description\":\"Groups designed to support individuals recovering from substance abuse or addiction.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Grief and Trauma Support Groups\",\"description\":\"Provides emotional support for individuals coping with grief, loss, or traumatic experiences.\"}]','[]','[\"Participate actively in meetings\",\"Build healthy peer connections\",\"Practice emotional coping strategies\",\"Maintain treatment compliance\",\"Seek professional help when needed\"]','[\"Exposure to emotionally triggering discussions\",\"Dependence on peer validation\",\"Misinformation if not professionally guided\",\"Discomfort sharing personal experiences\",\"Inconsistent participation reducing benefits\"]','<p>Support groups improve emotional resilience, confidence, social connection, and long-term coping abilities.</p>','<p>Support groups provide valuable emotional support and shared understanding for individuals facing mental health or life challenges. Consistent participation helps improve coping skills, social connection, and overall emotional well-being.</p>','Support Groups | Emotional and Mental Health Support','Learn about Support Groups including emotional support, coping strategies, peer connection, and mental health wellness benefits.','support groups, emotional support groups, mental health support, addiction recovery groups, peer counseling support',1,'2026-05-09 08:20:24','2026-05-09 10:07:55',NULL),(98,'Psychiatric Evaluation','procedures/banners/76c6f712-1aed-4cdf-81ca-a8ee8bc8e1f6.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/503e69a0-1ead-4f3a-96f7-729bfc339bb0.webp','psychiatric-evaluation','<p>Psychiatric evaluation is a comprehensive mental health assessment performed by a psychiatrist or mental health professional.</p>','<p>The evaluation includes medical history, emotional assessment, behavioral analysis, mental status examination, and diagnosis planning.</p>','[\"Persistent emotional distress\",\"Behavioral changes\",\"Mood instability\",\"Anxiety or depression\",\"Difficulty functioning in daily life\"]','[\"Mental health disorders\",\"Chronic stress\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Substance abuse\",\"Neurological or psychological conditions\"]','[\"Untreated psychiatric conditions\",\"Social isolation\",\"Family history of mental illness\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"Chronic emotional stress\"]','[\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain healthy lifestyle habits\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Maintain social and emotional support systems\",\"Attend regular mental health checkups\"]','[\"Mental status examination\",\"Psychological assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Mood and emotional screening tests\"]','<p>Psychiatric evaluation involves a detailed assessment of emotional, behavioral, and psychological health performed by a mental health professional. The process helps identify mental health conditions, assess severity, and develop individualized treatment plans for effective long-term care.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Initial Psychiatric Evaluation\",\"description\":\"A comprehensive first-time mental health assessment used for diagnosis and treatment planning.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Follow-Up Psychiatric Evaluation\",\"description\":\"Regular reassessment sessions to monitor treatment progress and symptom changes.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Emergency Psychiatric Assessment\",\"description\":\"Urgent psychiatric evaluation for severe emotional distress, behavioral crisis, or safety concerns.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow treatment recommendations carefully\",\"Attend follow-up appointments\",\"Monitor symptoms consistently\",\"Maintain medication compliance if prescribed\",\"Communicate openly with healthcare providers\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during assessment\",\"Anxiety discussing personal issues\",\"Misinterpretation if history is incomplete\",\"Temporary emotional stress\",\"Delayed diagnosis in complex cases\"]','<p>Accurate psychiatric evaluation helps guide effective treatment plans, improving mental health outcomes and long-term recovery.</p>','<p>Psychiatric evaluation is an essential step in diagnosing and managing mental health conditions. Early assessment, proper treatment planning, and regular follow-up help improve emotional well-being and long-term mental health outcomes.</p>','Psychiatric Evaluation | Mental Health Assessment ','Learn about Psychiatric Evaluation including mental health assessment, emotional evaluation, diagnosis planning, and psychiatric care.','psychiatric evaluation, mental health assessment, psychiatric diagnosis, emotional health evaluation, psychological assessment',1,'2026-05-09 08:21:06','2026-05-09 10:10:40',NULL),(99,'Risk Assessment',NULL,NULL,'risk-assessment','Risk assessment evaluates the possibility of self-harm, suicide, violence, or severe psychiatric complications.','Mental health professionals assess emotional stability, behavioral patterns, psychiatric history, and environmental factors to ensure patient safety.','[\"Suicidal thoughts\",\"Aggressive behavior\",\"Severe emotional distress\",\"Self-harm tendencies\",\"Psychotic symptoms\"]','[\"Severe mental health disorders\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Substance abuse\",\"Chronic stress\",\"Psychiatric crises\"]','[\"History of self-harm or suicide attempts\",\"Untreated psychiatric illness\",\"Social isolation\",\"Substance dependence\",\"Lack of emotional support\"]','[\"Seek mental health care early\",\"Maintain regular psychiatric follow-up\",\"Build strong emotional support systems\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Avoid substance abuse\"]','[\"Psychiatric evaluation\",\"Mental status examination\",\"Behavioral risk assessment\",\"Suicide risk screening\",\"Clinical interview\"]','Risk assessment involves a structured evaluation performed by mental health professionals to identify the likelihood of self-harm, suicide, aggression, or psychiatric emergencies. The process helps determine safety concerns, intervention needs, and appropriate treatment planning.','[{\"name\":\"1. Suicide Risk Assessment\",\"description\":\"Evaluates suicidal thoughts, intentions, and behaviors to ensure patient safety.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Violence Risk Assessment\",\"description\":\"Assesses aggressive behaviors and the risk of harm toward others.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Psychiatric Crisis Assessment\",\"description\":\"Emergency evaluation performed during severe emotional or psychiatric crises.\"}]','[\"Assessment is completed during psychiatric evaluation sessions\",\"Safety planning may begin immediately if required\",\"Regular follow-up monitoring supports long-term safety\",\"Ongoing psychiatric care may be necessary for high-risk conditions\"]','[\"Follow crisis management plans\",\"Maintain regular psychiatric follow-up\",\"Build strong support systems\",\"Remove potential self-harm risks at home\",\"Seek immediate help during emergencies\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during questioning\",\"Anxiety about hospitalization or interventions\",\"Fear of stigma\",\"Miscommunication affecting assessment accuracy\",\"Delayed intervention in rapidly changing conditions\"]','Risk assessments improve patient safety and support timely interventions that reduce psychiatric emergencies and improve recovery.','Risk assessment is a critical part of mental health care that helps identify safety concerns and guide timely intervention. Proper evaluation, support systems, and psychiatric follow-up improve long-term emotional stability and patient safety.','Psychiatric Risk Assessment | Mental Health Safety Evaluation','Learn about Psychiatric Risk Assessment including suicide risk evaluation, behavioral assessment, crisis intervention, and mental health safety planning.','psychiatric risk assessment, suicide risk evaluation, mental health safety assessment, behavioral risk screening, psychiatric crisis assessment',1,'2026-05-09 08:22:34','2026-05-09 08:22:34',NULL),(100,'Monitoring & Management of Medication Side Effects','procedures/banners/749599f8-d3ce-4b16-b77e-dd84bee0e028.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/81c77c9c-06c6-47dc-b5b8-c6d76053ef45.webp','monitoring-management-of-medication-side-effects','<p>This process involves regular monitoring of psychiatric medication effects and side effects to ensure patient safety and treatment effectiveness.</p>','<p>Psychiatrists evaluate physical, emotional, and behavioral responses to medications and adjust doses when necessary.</p>','[\"Drowsiness or fatigue\",\"Weight changes\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Mood changes\",\"Digestive discomfort\"]','[\"Psychiatric medications\",\"Medication dose adjustments\",\"Drug interactions\",\"Long-term medication use\",\"Individual sensitivity to medications\"]','[\"Medication non-compliance\",\"Polypharmacy or multiple medications\",\"Underlying medical conditions\",\"Improper dosage management\",\"Lack of regular psychiatric follow-up\"]','[\"Attend regular psychiatric reviews\",\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\",\"Avoid self-medication\",\"Inform doctors about all medications being used\",\"Maintain healthy lifestyle habits\"]','[\"Physical examination\",\"Medication review assessment\",\"Blood investigations\",\"Metabolic monitoring tests\",\"Psychiatric evaluation\"]','<p>Monitoring and management of medication side effects involves regular psychiatric consultations to evaluate the effectiveness and safety of psychiatric medications. Treatment plans may include dosage adjustments, medication changes, supportive therapies, and monitoring of physical and emotional health indicators.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Routine Medication Monitoring\",\"description\":\"Regular assessment of medication effectiveness and side effects during psychiatric treatment.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Metabolic Side Effect Monitoring\",\"description\":\"Monitoring weight, blood sugar, cholesterol, and metabolic health during long-term psychiatric medication use.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Medication Adjustment Management\",\"description\":\"Careful modification of psychiatric medication doses or combinations to reduce side effects and improve treatment response.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend regular medical reviews\",\"Report side effects promptly\",\"Avoid abrupt medication discontinuation\",\"Maintain proper medication schedules\",\"Follow lifestyle recommendations\"]','[\"Medication dependency\",\"Allergic reactions\",\"Hormonal or metabolic side effects\",\"Sedation or dizziness\",\"Medication interactions\"]','<p>Proper monitoring improves treatment safety, reduces complications, and helps maintain stable mental health.</p>','<p>Monitoring and management of psychiatric medication side effects are essential for safe and effective mental health treatment. Regular follow-up, early reporting of symptoms, and proper medication adjustments help improve long-term treatment outcomes and patient well-being.</p>','Psychiatric Medication Side Effect Monitoring','Learn about monitoring and management of psychiatric medication side effects including safety evaluations, medication reviews.','psychiatric medication monitoring, medication side effect management, mental health medication safety, psychiatric treatment follow-up, medication review psychiatry',1,'2026-05-09 08:23:08','2026-05-09 10:14:05',NULL),(103,'Electroconvulsive Therapy','procedures/banners/dd94089b-da4e-4749-a4df-e2b574c9a878.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/ed8b6899-e87b-434f-9617-ae783f2452e7.webp','electroconvulsive-therapy','<p>Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT) is a medical treatment that uses controlled electrical stimulation of the brain to treat severe psychiatric disorders.</p>','<p>ECT is commonly used for severe depression, treatment-resistant mental illness, catatonia, and severe bipolar disorder. The procedure is performed under anesthesia with careful monitoring.</p>','[\"Severe depression\",\"Suicidal thoughts\",\"Catatonia\",\"Severe bipolar symptoms\",\"Treatment-resistant psychiatric illness\"]','[\"Severe depressive disorder\",\"Bipolar disorder\",\"Treatment-resistant mental illness\",\"Psychotic disorders\",\"Catatonic psychiatric conditions\"]','[\"Untreated severe psychiatric illness\",\"High suicide risk\",\"Poor response to medications\",\"Severe emotional distress\",\"Chronic psychiatric instability\"]','[\"Seek psychiatric treatment early\",\"Maintain regular mental health follow-up\",\"Follow prescribed medications consistently\",\"Build strong emotional support systems\",\"Practice healthy stress management techniques\"]','[\"Psychiatric evaluation\",\"Mental status examination\",\"Physical examination\",\"Blood investigations\",\"Anesthesia fitness assessment\"]','<p>Electroconvulsive Therapy involves controlled electrical stimulation of the brain under general anesthesia to produce a brief therapeutic seizure. The procedure is carefully monitored by psychiatrists and anesthesiologists and is used to rapidly improve severe psychiatric symptoms when other treatments are ineffective.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Bilateral ECT\",\"description\":\"Electrical stimulation is applied to both sides of the brain for severe psychiatric conditions.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Unilateral ECT\",\"description\":\"Electrical stimulation is applied to one side of the brain to reduce cognitive side effects.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Maintenance ECT\",\"description\":\"Periodic ECT sessions are continued to prevent relapse in severe psychiatric illness.\"}]','[]','[\"Rest after each session\",\"Attend follow-up psychiatric appointments\",\"Monitor memory and cognitive function\",\"Continue prescribed medications if advised\",\"Maintain emotional support systems\"]','[\"Temporary memory loss\",\"Confusion after treatment\",\"Headache or muscle soreness\",\"Anesthesia-related complications\",\"Emotional distress regarding treatment\"]','<p>ECT can provide rapid improvement in severe psychiatric symptoms and significantly improve functioning in individuals not responding to other treatments.</p>','<p>Electroconvulsive Therapy is an effective treatment for severe and treatment-resistant psychiatric disorders. Careful monitoring, psychiatric follow-up, and supportive care help improve long-term emotional stability and quality of life.</p>','Electroconvulsive Therapy | ECT for Severe Psychiatric ','Learn about Electroconvulsive Therapy (ECT) including symptoms, treatment process, risks, recovery, and psychiatric care benefits.','electroconvulsive therapy, ECT treatment, severe depression treatment, psychiatric therapy, bipolar disorder treatment',1,'2026-05-09 08:25:28','2026-05-09 10:16:29',NULL),(104,'Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation','procedures/banners/dd987f45-7f6d-4b9b-9faf-89c064ab1823.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/4835c262-688b-4586-b5cb-6a97905edfd9.webp','transcranial-magnetic-stimulation','<p>Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (TMS) is a non-invasive brain stimulation therapy used to treat depression and other psychiatric conditions.</p>','<p>TMS uses magnetic pulses to stimulate specific brain regions involved in mood regulation.</p>','[\"Treatment-resistant depression\",\"Persistent sadness\",\"Anxiety symptoms\",\"Low motivation\",\"Emotional instability\"]','[\"Major depressive disorder\",\"Treatment-resistant psychiatric illness\",\"Anxiety disorders\",\"Mood regulation disturbances\",\"Chronic emotional stress\"]','[\"Untreated severe depression\",\"Poor response to antidepressant medications\",\"Chronic psychiatric symptoms\",\"Emotional instability\",\"Long-term stress-related mental health conditions\"]','[\"Seek psychiatric care early\",\"Maintain regular mental health follow-up\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Follow prescribed treatment plans\",\"Maintain healthy sleep and lifestyle habits\"]','[\"Psychiatric evaluation\",\"Mental status examination\",\"Depression screening assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Clinical interview\"]','<p>Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation involves the use of magnetic pulses delivered through a specialized device placed near the scalp. The treatment stimulates brain regions associated with mood regulation and emotional control. TMS is non-invasive, performed without anesthesia, and commonly used for treatment-resistant depression and related psychiatric conditions.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Repetitive TMS (rTMS)\",\"description\":\"Repeated magnetic stimulation sessions used to improve depressive and anxiety symptoms.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Deep TMS\",\"description\":\"Advanced TMS technique targeting deeper brain regions involved in mood regulation.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Maintenance TMS Therapy\",\"description\":\"Periodic TMS sessions continued to maintain long-term symptom improvement and prevent relapse.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend all scheduled sessions\",\"Monitor mood improvements regularly\",\"Report unusual symptoms promptly\",\"Continue psychiatric follow-up care\",\"Maintain healthy routines and sleep\"]','[\"Mild headache\",\"Scalp discomfort\",\"Dizziness\",\"Rare seizure risk\",\"Temporary fatigue\"]','<p>TMS can improve mood, reduce depressive symptoms, and enhance daily functioning with minimal recovery time.</p>','<p>Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation is a safe and effective non-invasive treatment for depression and related psychiatric disorders. Consistent therapy sessions and psychiatric follow-up help improve long-term emotional well-being and daily functioning.</p>','Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation | TMS Therapy ','Learn about Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (TMS) including depression treatment, brain stimulation therapy, risks, recovery, and psychiatric care.','transcranial magnetic stimulation, TMS therapy, depression treatment, non-invasive brain stimulation, psychiatric therapy',1,'2026-05-09 08:26:10','2026-05-09 10:17:42',NULL),(105,'Biofeedback Therapy','procedures/banners/bc37848a-19b2-45e1-8306-1935c2f357c7.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/203a60f8-16f8-44e6-9991-dda7b0a39e4c.webp','biofeedback-therapy','<p>Biofeedback therapy teaches individuals to control physical stress responses using monitoring devices and relaxation techniques.</p>','<p>It helps manage anxiety, stress, headaches, and emotional regulation by improving awareness of body responses.</p>','[\"Stress-related tension\",\"Anxiety symptoms\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Chronic headaches\",\"Emotional dysregulation\"]','[\"Chronic stress\",\"Anxiety disorders\",\"Poor emotional regulation\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Stress-related physical symptoms\"]','[\"High stress levels\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"Untreated anxiety disorders\",\"Chronic emotional strain\",\"Lack of relaxation practices\"]','[\"Practice regular stress management techniques\",\"Maintain healthy sleep habits\",\"Engage in relaxation exercises\",\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain a healthy work-life balance\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Stress evaluation\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Physiological monitoring tests\",\"Clinical mental health evaluation\"]','<p>Biofeedback therapy uses specialized monitoring devices to help individuals become aware of physical stress responses such as heart rate, muscle tension, breathing patterns, and skin temperature. Through guided relaxation and coping techniques, patients learn to regulate these responses and improve emotional and physical well-being.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Electromyography (EMG) Biofeedback\",\"description\":\"Monitors muscle tension to help individuals reduce stress-related physical symptoms.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Heart Rate Variability Biofeedback\",\"description\":\"Focuses on regulating heart rate patterns to improve stress and emotional control.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Neurofeedback Therapy\",\"description\":\"Uses brainwave monitoring to improve emotional regulation and mental performance.\"}]','[]','[\"Practice relaxation techniques regularly\",\"Attend follow-up therapy sessions\",\"Monitor stress levels consistently\",\"Maintain healthy sleep patterns\",\"Use coping strategies during stressful situations\"]','[\"Mild frustration during training\",\"Temporary emotional discomfort\",\"Limited benefit with irregular practice\",\"Dependence on equipment guidance\",\"Slow progress in severe cases\"]','<p>Biofeedback therapy improves stress management, emotional control, relaxation, and overall mental wellness.</p>','<p>Biofeedback therapy is an effective non-invasive treatment that helps individuals improve stress management and emotional regulation. Consistent practice and regular therapy sessions support long-term mental and physical well-being.</p>','Biofeedback Therapy | Stress and Emotional Regulation ','Learn about Biofeedback Therapy including stress management, emotional regulation, relaxation techniques, and mental wellness support.','biofeedback therapy, stress management therapy, emotional regulation treatment, relaxation therapy, neurofeedback treatment',1,'2026-05-09 08:26:56','2026-05-12 05:47:43',NULL),(106,'Crisis Intervention','procedures/banners/1c6f7915-aa40-41e3-b227-79988dda69c1.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/e87a87d0-867d-499c-807f-89d06e1c6210.webp','crisis-intervention','<p>Crisis intervention provides immediate mental health support during psychiatric emergencies or severe emotional distress.</p>','<p>It focuses on stabilizing emotional crises, preventing harm, and connecting individuals to ongoing mental health care.</p>','[\"Severe anxiety or panic\",\"Suicidal thoughts\",\"Emotional breakdowns\",\"Aggressive behavior\",\"Acute psychiatric distress\"]','[\"Severe emotional stress\",\"Psychiatric emergencies\",\"Traumatic life events\",\"Untreated mental health disorders\",\"Substance abuse or withdrawal\"]','[\"History of psychiatric illness\",\"Social isolation\",\"Lack of emotional support\",\"High suicide risk\",\"Chronic stress exposure\"]','[\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain regular psychiatric follow-up\",\"Build healthy emotional support systems\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Avoid substance abuse\"]','[\"Psychiatric evaluation\",\"Mental status examination\",\"Behavioral risk assessment\",\"Suicide risk screening\",\"Emergency psychological assessment\"]','<p>Crisis intervention involves immediate psychiatric assessment and emotional stabilization during severe mental health emergencies. Mental health professionals provide supportive counseling, safety planning, crisis management, and coordination of ongoing psychiatric treatment to reduce harm and restore emotional stability.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Emergency Psychiatric Crisis Intervention\",\"description\":\"Immediate mental health support provided during severe psychiatric emergencies.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Suicide Prevention Crisis Intervention\",\"description\":\"Focused intervention aimed at reducing suicide risk and ensuring patient safety.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Trauma Crisis Counseling\",\"description\":\"Supportive counseling provided during acute emotional trauma or psychological distress.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend psychiatric follow-up appointments\",\"Continue prescribed treatment plans\",\"Build strong emotional support systems\",\"Avoid stress triggers when possible\",\"Seek immediate help during recurring crises\"]','[\"Emotional instability during crisis\",\"Risk of self-harm\",\"Sudden behavioral changes\",\"Need for emergency hospitalization\",\"Relapse without proper follow-up care\"]','<p>Early crisis intervention improves safety, emotional recovery, and long-term mental health stability.</p>','<p>Crisis intervention is a critical mental health service that provides immediate support during psychiatric emergencies. Early intervention, ongoing psychiatric care, and strong emotional support systems help improve recovery and long-term emotional well-being.</p>','Crisis Intervention | Emergency Mental Health Support','Learn about Crisis Intervention including psychiatric emergency care, emotional stabilization, suicide prevention, and mental health recovery support.','crisis intervention, psychiatric emergency care, suicide prevention support, emotional crisis counseling, mental health crisis management',1,'2026-05-09 08:28:48','2026-05-09 10:18:44',NULL),(108,'Telepsychiatry Services','procedures/banners/193dd180-3c88-49d7-8b55-84f33e219dea.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/fe098907-a2ba-4574-9685-d8994e5b1b20.webp','telepsychiatry-services','<p>Telepsychiatry provides psychiatric consultations and mental health treatment through secure online communication platforms.</p>','<p>It allows patients to access mental health services remotely, improving convenience and continuity of care.</p>','[\"Anxiety or depression requiring follow-up\",\"Stress-related disorders\",\"Difficulty accessing in-person care\",\"Emotional distress needing counseling\",\"Ongoing psychiatric conditions\"]','[\"Mental health disorders\",\"Limited access to psychiatric care\",\"Chronic stress\",\"Emotional or behavioral challenges\",\"Need for long-term psychiatric follow-up\"]','[\"Lack of mental health support\",\"Social isolation\",\"Untreated psychiatric conditions\",\"Difficulty accessing healthcare facilities\",\"Chronic emotional stress\"]','[\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain regular psychiatric follow-up\",\"Use secure communication platforms\",\"Practice healthy stress management techniques\",\"Maintain healthy routines and sleep habits\"]','[\"Psychiatric evaluation\",\"Mental health screening\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional wellness evaluation\"]','<p>Telepsychiatry involves psychiatric consultations, counseling, medication management, and mental health follow-up conducted through secure video or online communication platforms. The service improves access to psychiatric care while supporting continuity of treatment and emotional well-being.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Online Psychiatric Consultation\",\"description\":\"Remote psychiatric assessments and treatment planning conducted through video consultations.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Teletherapy Sessions\",\"description\":\"Online counseling and psychotherapy sessions provided through secure digital platforms.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Remote Medication Management\",\"description\":\"Virtual psychiatric follow-up for monitoring medications and treatment response.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend scheduled online appointments regularly\",\"Ensure private and quiet consultation spaces\",\"Follow prescribed medications consistently\",\"Monitor symptoms and emotional changes\",\"Maintain emergency contact information\"]','[\"Technical connectivity issues\",\"Limited physical observation during sessions\",\"Privacy concerns if systems are insecure\",\"Reduced emergency intervention capability\",\"Communication difficulties in severe psychiatric cases\"]','<p>Telepsychiatry improves accessibility, treatment continuity, and mental health support, especially for individuals in remote areas.</p>','<p>Telepsychiatry services provide convenient and effective access to mental health care through secure digital platforms. Regular participation and proper follow-up help improve emotional well-being and long-term psychiatric outcomes.</p>','Telepsychiatry Services | Online Mental Health','Learn about Telepsychiatry Services including online psychiatric consultations, virtual therapy, medication management, and remote mental health support.','telepsychiatry services, online psychiatric consultation, virtual mental health care, teletherapy, remote psychiatric treatment',1,'2026-05-09 08:30:17','2026-05-09 10:19:52',NULL),(109,'Electroencephalogram','procedures/banners/821346e7-fc18-4cf3-8e55-24ce2fe547fd.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/94aa70d1-45c7-4f17-95c8-bc6e81f4dfe6.webp','electroencephalogram','<p>An Electroencephalogram (EEG) is a diagnostic test used to measure the electrical activity of the brain.</p>','<p>EEG helps diagnose epilepsy, seizures, sleep disorders, brain dysfunction, and neurological conditions by recording brain wave patterns using electrodes placed on the scalp.</p>','[\"Seizures or convulsions\",\"Episodes of unconsciousness\",\"Memory disturbances\",\"Sleep disorders\",\"Sudden behavioral changes\"]','[\"Epilepsy\",\"Neurological disorders\",\"Brain injury\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Abnormal brain activity\"]','[\"History of seizures\",\"Neurological illness\",\"Head injury\",\"Family history of epilepsy\",\"Chronic sleep disorders\"]','[\"Follow neurological treatment plans\",\"Maintain healthy sleep patterns\",\"Avoid seizure triggers if identified\",\"Attend regular neurological follow-ups\",\"Take prescribed medications consistently\"]','[\"Electroencephalogram (EEG)\",\"Neurological examination\",\"MRI brain scan\",\"CT brain scan\",\"Sleep study evaluation\"]','<p>Electroencephalogram testing involves placing small electrodes on the scalp to record electrical brain activity. The test helps identify abnormal brain wave patterns associated with seizures, neurological disorders, sleep disturbances, and psychiatric conditions. EEG is painless, non-invasive, and commonly performed in neurological evaluation.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Routine EEG\",\"description\":\"A standard EEG test performed to evaluate brain electrical activity and detect abnormalities.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Sleep-Deprived EEG\",\"description\":\"EEG testing performed after reduced sleep to increase the likelihood of detecting abnormal brain activity.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Video EEG Monitoring\",\"description\":\"Continuous EEG recording combined with video monitoring to evaluate seizure activity and neurological events.\"}]','[]','[\"Resume normal activities after the test\",\"Wash hair to remove electrode gel\",\"Follow neurologist recommendations\",\"Monitor symptoms if seizures occur\",\"Attend follow-up consultations for results\"]','[\"Mild scalp irritation from electrodes\",\"Temporary discomfort during testing\",\"Rare seizure triggering during stimulation tests\",\"Anxiety during the procedure\",\"Sleep deprivation-related fatigue if required\"]','<p>EEG helps guide accurate diagnosis and treatment planning for neurological and psychiatric conditions, improving long-term management.</p>','<p>Electroencephalogram testing is an important diagnostic tool for evaluating brain activity and neurological conditions. Early diagnosis and proper follow-up help improve treatment outcomes and long-term neurological health.</p>','Electroencephalogram | EEG Brain Activity Diagnostic Test','Learn about Electroencephalogram (EEG) including seizure evaluation, neurological diagnosis, brain activity testing, risks, and follow-up care.','electroencephalogram, EEG test, brain wave test, seizure diagnosis, neurological diagnostic evaluation',1,'2026-05-09 08:30:57','2026-05-09 10:23:49',NULL),(110,'Video EEG','procedures/banners/58292de4-b35c-4b69-9ad1-7d996b1c6901.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/968a8859-5d28-4069-b7c5-1d2a1194257a.webp','video-eeg','<p>Video EEG combines continuous EEG monitoring with video recording to evaluate seizures and abnormal neurological activity.</p>','<p>It helps specialists correlate physical movements and behaviors with brain wave activity for accurate diagnosis of epilepsy and seizure disorders.</p>','[\"Recurrent seizures\",\"Unexplained fainting episodes\",\"Sudden behavioral changes\",\"Memory lapses\",\"Episodes of confusion\"]','[\"Epilepsy\",\"Seizure disorders\",\"Neurological abnormalities\",\"Brain injury\",\"Abnormal electrical brain activity\"]','[\"History of seizures\",\"Family history of epilepsy\",\"Neurological disorders\",\"Head trauma\",\"Chronic sleep disturbances\"]','[\"Take prescribed seizure medications regularly\",\"Maintain healthy sleep patterns\",\"Avoid known seizure triggers\",\"Attend regular neurological follow-up appointments\",\"Follow recommended lifestyle modifications\"]','[\"Video EEG monitoring\",\"Routine EEG\",\"MRI brain scan\",\"Neurological examination\",\"Seizure assessment evaluation\"]','<p>Video EEG monitoring involves continuous recording of brain electrical activity along with synchronized video observation. This allows neurologists to analyze seizure activity, physical movements, and behavioral changes during episodes for accurate diagnosis and treatment planning.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Inpatient Video EEG Monitoring\",\"description\":\"Continuous EEG and video monitoring performed in a hospital setting for detailed seizure evaluation.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Ambulatory Video EEG\",\"description\":\"Portable video EEG monitoring conducted while the patient continues normal daily activities.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Long-Term Video EEG Monitoring\",\"description\":\"Extended monitoring over multiple days to capture infrequent seizure events and abnormal brain activity.\"}]','[]','[\"Rest after prolonged monitoring\",\"Follow neurologist instructions carefully\",\"Continue prescribed seizure medications\",\"Monitor seizure activity closely\",\"Attend follow-up evaluations\"]','[\"Temporary discomfort from prolonged monitoring\",\"Sleep deprivation-related fatigue\",\"Risk of seizure occurrence during testing\",\"Anxiety during hospital monitoring\",\"Skin irritation from electrodes\"]','<p>Video EEG improves diagnostic accuracy and helps create effective treatment plans for epilepsy and seizure-related disorders.</p>','<p>Video EEG is an important neurological diagnostic tool that helps accurately evaluate seizures and abnormal brain activity. Early diagnosis and appropriate treatment planning improve long-term seizure control and neurological health.</p>','Video EEG Monitoring | Epilepsy and Seizure Diagnosis','Learn about Video EEG monitoring including seizure evaluation, epilepsy diagnosis, brain activity recording, risks, and neurological follow-up care.','video EEG, epilepsy diagnosis, seizure monitoring, neurological evaluation, brain activity monitoring',1,'2026-05-09 08:31:39','2026-05-09 10:24:53',NULL),(111,'Electromyography','procedures/banners/f5d7011f-d719-47e4-9943-1e6a3b4644ac.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/4d6e625f-de99-47d6-a926-73d476bedaf5.webp','electromyography','<p>Electromyography (EMG) evaluates muscle and nerve function by measuring electrical activity within muscles.</p>','<p>It helps diagnose nerve disorders, muscle diseases, neuropathies, and neuromuscular conditions.</p>','[\"Muscle weakness\",\"Numbness or tingling\",\"Muscle cramps\",\"Difficulty moving limbs\",\"Nerve pain\"]','[\"Neuromuscular disorders\",\"Peripheral nerve damage\",\"Muscle diseases\",\"Nerve compression syndromes\",\"Chronic neurological conditions\"]','[\"History of nerve injury\",\"Diabetes-related neuropathy\",\"Muscle disorders\",\"Chronic neurological illness\",\"Repetitive nerve compression injuries\"]','[\"Maintain healthy nerve and muscle function\",\"Control chronic medical conditions like diabetes\",\"Avoid repetitive strain injuries\",\"Follow neurological treatment recommendations\",\"Attend regular medical follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Electromyography (EMG)\",\"Nerve conduction studies\",\"Neurological examination\",\"MRI scan\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>Electromyography is a diagnostic procedure used to measure electrical activity in muscles and nerves. Small needle electrodes are inserted into specific muscles to evaluate nerve signals and muscle responses. EMG helps identify neuromuscular disorders, nerve injuries, and muscle dysfunction accurately.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Needle Electromyography\",\"description\":\"Uses fine needle electrodes inserted into muscles to measure electrical activity and muscle response.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Nerve Conduction Study\",\"description\":\"Measures how quickly electrical signals travel through nerves to identify nerve damage or dysfunction.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Surface Electromyography\",\"description\":\"Uses external electrodes placed on the skin to evaluate muscle activity non-invasively.\"}]','[]','[\"Rest the tested muscles if sore\",\"Apply ice for mild discomfort if needed\",\"Follow medical advice regarding results\",\"Monitor for unusual swelling or bleeding\",\"Attend follow-up neurological evaluations\"]','[\"Mild pain from needle insertion\",\"Temporary muscle soreness\",\"Minor bruising\",\"Bleeding risk in sensitive patients\",\"Anxiety during the procedure\"]','<p>EMG assists in accurate diagnosis and long-term management of neuromuscular disorders.</p>','<p>Electromyography is an important neurological diagnostic test that helps evaluate muscle and nerve function. Early diagnosis and proper treatment planning improve long-term management of neuromuscular conditions.</p>','Electromyography | EMG Nerve and Muscle Function Test','Learn about Electromyography (EMG) including nerve testing, muscle evaluation, neuromuscular diagnosis, risks, and follow-up care.','electromyography, EMG test, nerve conduction study, muscle function test, neuromuscular diagnostic evaluation',1,'2026-05-09 08:32:15','2026-05-09 10:28:45',NULL),(112,'Nerve Conduction Study (NCS)','procedures/banners/a6bfd78b-2483-48c8-96e9-ee7af285d5ee.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/b9353af3-ff0a-4ef3-9518-68c950925df6.webp','nerve-conduction-study-ncs','<p>Nerve Conduction Study measures the speed and strength of electrical signals traveling through nerves.</p>','<p>NCS helps diagnose nerve damage, neuropathy, nerve compression disorders, and neuromuscular conditions.</p>','[\"Tingling sensations\",\"Numbness in limbs\",\"Muscle weakness\",\"Burning nerve pain\",\"Loss of coordination\"]','[\"Peripheral neuropathy\",\"Nerve compression disorders\",\"Diabetes-related nerve damage\",\"Neuromuscular disorders\",\"Nerve injuries\"]','[\"Diabetes mellitus\",\"Chronic neurological conditions\",\"History of nerve injury\",\"Vitamin deficiencies\",\"Repetitive strain or compression injuries\"]','[\"Maintain healthy blood sugar levels\",\"Avoid repetitive nerve strain\",\"Follow neurological treatment plans\",\"Maintain proper nutrition and vitamin intake\",\"Attend regular medical follow-up appointments\"]','[\"Nerve Conduction Study (NCS)\",\"Electromyography (EMG)\",\"Neurological examination\",\"MRI scan\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>Nerve Conduction Study is a diagnostic procedure that measures how quickly and effectively electrical signals travel through nerves. Small electrodes are placed on the skin to stimulate nerves and record their responses. The test helps identify nerve damage, compression, and neuromuscular disorders accurately.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Motor Nerve Conduction Study\",\"description\":\"Evaluates electrical signal transmission in motor nerves controlling muscle movement.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Sensory Nerve Conduction Study\",\"description\":\"Measures sensory nerve responses related to touch, pain, and sensation.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Combined NCS and EMG Testing\",\"description\":\"Uses both nerve conduction studies and electromyography for comprehensive neuromuscular evaluation.\"}]','[]','[\"Resume normal activities after testing\",\"Follow neurological treatment recommendations\",\"Monitor persistent nerve symptoms\",\"Maintain follow-up appointments\",\"Continue medications if prescribed\"]','[\"Mild discomfort from electrical stimulation\",\"Temporary muscle twitching\",\"Anxiety during testing\",\"Rare skin irritation\",\"Temporary soreness after the test\"]','<p>NCS supports accurate nerve disorder diagnosis and helps guide effective long-term treatment.</p>','<p>Nerve Conduction Study is an important diagnostic tool for evaluating nerve function and detecting neurological disorders. Early diagnosis and appropriate treatment planning help improve long-term nerve health and patient outcomes.</p>','Nerve Conduction Study | NCS Diagnostic Nerve Function Test','Learn about Nerve Conduction Study (NCS) including nerve testing, neuropathy diagnosis, nerve damage evaluation, risks, and neurological care.','nerve conduction study, NCS test, neuropathy diagnosis, nerve function test, neurological diagnostic evaluation',1,'2026-05-09 08:34:28','2026-05-09 10:52:37',NULL),(113,'Magnetic Resonance Imaging — Brain / Spine','procedures/banners/130daf12-77ed-480e-ada4-472a8ab3b6f2.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/5d796a1b-3454-447e-9246-e6fd3849f66e.webp','magnetic-resonance-imaging-brain-spine','<p>Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) uses strong magnetic fields and radio waves to create detailed images of the brain and spine.</p>','<p>MRI helps detect tumors, stroke, spinal disorders, nerve compression, infections, and neurological abnormalities.</p>','[\"Persistent headaches\",\"Seizures\",\"Weakness or numbness\",\"Back or neck pain\",\"Memory or neurological disturbances\"]','[\"Neurological disorders\",\"Brain tumors\",\"Spinal cord abnormalities\",\"Nerve compression\",\"Stroke or vascular conditions\"]','[\"History of neurological disease\",\"Spinal injury\",\"Chronic headaches\",\"Family history of neurological disorders\",\"Previous stroke or brain injury\"]','[\"Maintain regular neurological checkups\",\"Seek early medical attention for neurological symptoms\",\"Manage chronic medical conditions effectively\",\"Avoid head and spinal injuries\",\"Follow specialist treatment recommendations\"]','[\"MRI Brain\",\"MRI Spine\",\"Neurological examination\",\"CT scan\",\"Contrast-enhanced MRI studies\"]','<p>Magnetic Resonance Imaging is a non-invasive diagnostic procedure that uses magnetic fields and radio waves to generate detailed images of the brain and spinal structures. MRI helps neurologists accurately diagnose neurological abnormalities, spinal disorders, tumors, infections, vascular conditions, and nerve-related problems.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. MRI Brain Scan\",\"description\":\"Detailed imaging of the brain used to evaluate neurological conditions, tumors, stroke, and seizures.\"},{\"name\":\"2. MRI Spine Scan\",\"description\":\"Imaging of the spinal cord and vertebral structures to detect disc disorders, nerve compression, and spinal abnormalities.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Contrast MRI\",\"description\":\"MRI performed with contrast dye to improve visualization of blood vessels, tumors, and inflammatory conditions.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink fluids if contrast dye was used\",\"Resume normal activities unless advised otherwise\",\"Follow specialist recommendations\",\"Monitor for allergic symptoms if contrast was given\",\"Attend follow-up consultations for results\"]','[\"Claustrophobia during scanning\",\"Anxiety in enclosed spaces\",\"Rare allergic reaction to contrast dye\",\"Loud machine noise discomfort\",\"Incompatibility with metal implants\"]','<p>MRI provides highly accurate diagnostic information that supports early treatment and improved neurological outcomes.</p>','<p>Magnetic Resonance Imaging is an essential diagnostic tool for evaluating brain and spinal conditions. Early detection and accurate diagnosis help improve treatment planning and long-term neurological health outcomes.</p>','MRI Brain and Spine | Neurological Diagnostic Imaging','Learn about MRI Brain and Spine imaging including neurological diagnosis, spinal evaluation, risks, contrast MRI, and follow-up care.','MRI brain scan, MRI spine scan, neurological MRI, spinal imaging, brain diagnostic imaging',1,'2026-05-09 08:35:08','2026-05-09 10:30:44',NULL),(114,'Computed Tomography — CT Brain','procedures/banners/71c0837d-f8dc-456e-8ea1-dba13b8dfa67.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/862de0e6-9f63-47e8-95c2-3f40427824f5.webp','computed-tomography-ct-brain','<p>CT Brain scanning uses X-rays and computer imaging to evaluate brain structures quickly and accurately.</p>','<p>CT scans help diagnose head injuries, stroke, bleeding, tumors, infections, and neurological emergencies.</p>','[\"Severe headache\",\"Head injury\",\"Sudden weakness or paralysis\",\"Seizures\",\"Confusion or unconsciousness\"]','[\"Head trauma\",\"Stroke\",\"Brain hemorrhage\",\"Brain tumors\",\"Neurological infections\"]','[\"History of neurological disease\",\"High blood pressure\",\"Head injuries\",\"Previous stroke\",\"Chronic neurological symptoms\"]','[\"Manage blood pressure and chronic medical conditions\",\"Use protective measures to prevent head injuries\",\"Seek immediate medical attention for neurological symptoms\",\"Maintain regular neurological follow-up\",\"Follow specialist treatment recommendations\"]','[\"CT Brain Scan\",\"Contrast CT Brain\",\"Neurological examination\",\"MRI Brain\",\"Blood investigations\"]','<p>Computed Tomography of the brain is a rapid imaging procedure that uses X-rays and computer technology to create detailed cross-sectional images of brain structures. CT Brain scans are commonly used in emergency settings to diagnose strokes, bleeding, trauma, tumors, infections, and other neurological conditions quickly and accurately.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Non-Contrast CT Brain\",\"description\":\"Standard CT brain imaging used to detect bleeding, fractures, stroke, and brain abnormalities.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Contrast CT Brain\",\"description\":\"CT imaging performed with contrast dye to improve visualization of blood vessels, tumors, and infections.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Emergency CT Brain Scan\",\"description\":\"Rapid imaging performed during neurological emergencies such as stroke or head trauma.\"}]','[]','[\"Drink adequate fluids after contrast studies\",\"Follow emergency treatment instructions if needed\",\"Monitor for allergic symptoms\",\"Attend neurological follow-up appointments\",\"Resume activities as advised by the doctor\"]','[\"Radiation exposure\",\"Allergic reaction to contrast dye\",\"Anxiety during scanning\",\"Kidney stress from contrast in sensitive patients\",\"Rare nausea after contrast injection\"]','<p>CT Brain scans help rapidly diagnose critical neurological conditions, supporting timely treatment and better recovery.</p>','<p>CT Brain imaging is an important diagnostic tool for evaluating neurological emergencies and brain disorders. Early diagnosis and rapid treatment planning improve patient safety and long-term neurological outcomes.</p>','CT Brain Scan | Neurological and Emergency Brain Imaging','Learn about CT Brain scanning including stroke diagnosis, head injury evaluation, neurological imaging, risks, and follow-up care.','CT brain scan, computed tomography brain, neurological imaging, stroke diagnosis, emergency brain scan',1,'2026-05-09 08:37:41','2026-05-09 10:32:04',NULL),(115,'Cognitive Testing','procedures/banners/7552b1e4-d567-4dfa-b5b7-1cbc09774979.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/548e8614-603e-44b8-a8c0-ef30fb7ea303.webp','cognitive-testing','<p>Cognitive testing evaluates memory, attention, problem-solving, language, and thinking abilities.</p>','<p>It helps identify cognitive decline, dementia, learning difficulties, and mental processing disorders.</p>','[\"Memory loss\",\"Difficulty concentrating\",\"Confusion or disorientation\",\"Learning difficulties\",\"Reduced problem-solving abilities\"]','[\"Dementia\",\"Neurological disorders\",\"Brain injury\",\"Learning disabilities\",\"Age-related cognitive decline\"]','[\"Advanced age\",\"Family history of dementia\",\"Neurological illnesses\",\"Head injuries\",\"Chronic mental health conditions\"]','[\"Maintain regular mental stimulation\",\"Follow healthy sleep habits\",\"Engage in physical activity regularly\",\"Manage chronic medical conditions effectively\",\"Attend regular neurological evaluations\"]','[\"Memory assessment tests\",\"Neuropsychological evaluation\",\"Attention and concentration tests\",\"Language and reasoning assessment\",\"Cognitive function screening\"]','<p>Cognitive testing involves structured assessments that evaluate memory, reasoning, attention, language, and problem-solving abilities. These evaluations help specialists diagnose cognitive disorders, monitor mental functioning, and plan rehabilitation or treatment strategies for neurological and psychiatric conditions.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Neuropsychological Testing\",\"description\":\"Comprehensive evaluation of memory, attention, language, and executive brain functions.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Dementia Cognitive Screening\",\"description\":\"Focused cognitive assessments used to detect early signs of dementia and cognitive decline.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Learning and Cognitive Assessment\",\"description\":\"Testing designed to evaluate learning difficulties, processing disorders, and cognitive performance.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow specialist recommendations\",\"Continue cognitive rehabilitation if advised\",\"Maintain mental stimulation activities\",\"Attend follow-up assessments regularly\",\"Support healthy sleep and nutrition habits\"]','[\"Emotional frustration during testing\",\"Anxiety regarding performance\",\"Fatigue during lengthy assessments\",\"Stress from diagnostic outcomes\",\"Temporary emotional discomfort\"]','<p>Cognitive testing helps early identification and management of cognitive disorders, improving long-term mental function and care planning.</p>','<p>Cognitive testing is an important diagnostic tool for evaluating memory, attention, and thinking abilities. Early assessment and proper follow-up help improve long-term cognitive health and treatment planning.</p>','Cognitive Testing | Memory and Cognitive Function Assessment','Learn about Cognitive Testing including memory evaluation, dementia screening, neuropsychological assessment, risks, and cognitive health management.','cognitive testing, memory assessment, neuropsychological evaluation, dementia screening, cognitive function test',1,'2026-05-09 08:38:49','2026-05-09 10:33:43',NULL),(116,'Neuropsychological Testing','procedures/banners/83f62093-3713-4800-9333-46659eb66e1c.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/417feb47-d4bf-4c6a-b742-b64eb45811cb.webp','neuropsychological-testing','<p>Neuropsychological testing is a detailed assessment of brain-related cognitive, emotional, and behavioral functions.</p>','<p>It helps diagnose neurological and psychiatric disorders affecting memory, attention, intelligence, emotional regulation, and executive functioning.</p>','[\"Memory problems\",\"Behavioral changes\",\"Difficulty concentrating\",\"Learning or language difficulties\",\"Emotional instability\"]','[\"Neurological disorders\",\"Brain injury\",\"Dementia\",\"Psychiatric illnesses\",\"Learning and cognitive disorders\"]','[\"Family history of neurological disease\",\"History of head injury\",\"Age-related cognitive decline\",\"Chronic psychiatric conditions\",\"Neurological abnormalities\"]','[\"Maintain regular mental stimulation\",\"Follow healthy sleep and lifestyle habits\",\"Manage chronic medical conditions effectively\",\"Attend neurological and psychiatric follow-up appointments\",\"Seek early evaluation for cognitive or behavioral changes\"]','[\"Neuropsychological assessment\",\"Memory and intelligence testing\",\"Attention and executive function evaluation\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Language and cognitive processing tests\"]','<p>Neuropsychological testing involves comprehensive assessments designed to evaluate cognitive abilities, emotional functioning, behavior, memory, language skills, attention, and executive brain functions. The results help specialists diagnose neurological and psychiatric conditions, develop rehabilitation strategies, and guide long-term treatment planning.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Cognitive Function Assessment\",\"description\":\"Detailed testing of memory, attention, reasoning, and executive brain functions.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Behavioral and Emotional Assessment\",\"description\":\"Evaluation of emotional regulation, personality changes, and behavioral functioning.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Learning and Intelligence Evaluation\",\"description\":\"Assessment of intellectual abilities, learning disorders, and language-related cognitive functions.\"}]','[]','[\"Follow rehabilitation recommendations\",\"Continue cognitive therapy if prescribed\",\"Maintain brain-stimulating activities\",\"Attend regular follow-up evaluations\",\"Support emotional and mental wellness\"]','[\"Mental fatigue during assessment\",\"Anxiety regarding results\",\"Emotional discomfort discussing symptoms\",\"Frustration during difficult tasks\",\"Stress related to diagnosis\"]','<p>Neuropsychological testing supports accurate diagnosis, rehabilitation planning, and long-term management of neurological and psychiatric conditions.</p>','<p>Neuropsychological testing is an important diagnostic tool that helps evaluate cognitive, emotional, and behavioral functioning. Early assessment and proper rehabilitation planning improve long-term neurological and psychological outcomes.</p>','Neuropsychological Testing | Cognitive and Behavioral Brain ','Learn about Neuropsychological Testing including memory evaluation, behavioral assessment, cognitive diagnosis, rehabilitation planning, and neurological care.','neuropsychological testing, cognitive assessment, behavioral evaluation, memory testing, neurological psychological assessment',1,'2026-05-09 08:39:44','2026-05-09 10:36:26',NULL),(117,'EEG Caps','procedures/banners/b3b02f9b-c322-40b1-abf7-13d868565e4d.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/bbae0c29-002f-4449-ae6f-f586be1e05df.webp','eeg-caps','<p>EEG caps are specialized headgear containing electrodes used for recording brain electrical activity during EEG testing.</p>','<p>These caps improve electrode placement accuracy and enhance the quality of brain wave recordings.</p>','[\"Seizure evaluation needs\",\"Neurological assessment requirements\",\"Sleep disorder investigations\",\"Brain activity monitoring\",\"Cognitive or behavioral assessments\"]','[\"Epilepsy\",\"Neurological disorders\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Brain activity abnormalities\",\"Behavioral or cognitive conditions\"]','[\"History of seizures\",\"Neurological illnesses\",\"Chronic sleep disorders\",\"Brain injuries\",\"Cognitive dysfunction\"]','[\"Attend regular neurological evaluations\",\"Follow prescribed neurological treatments\",\"Maintain healthy sleep habits\",\"Avoid seizure triggers if identified\",\"Seek early medical attention for neurological symptoms\"]','[\"Electroencephalogram (EEG)\",\"Video EEG monitoring\",\"Neurological examination\",\"Sleep study evaluation\",\"Brain activity assessment\"]','<p>EEG caps are specially designed headgear fitted with multiple electrodes to record electrical activity in the brain during EEG testing. These caps improve electrode positioning accuracy, reduce setup time, and enhance the quality of neurological and psychiatric brain wave recordings.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Standard EEG Cap Recording\",\"description\":\"Routine EEG testing using electrode caps to monitor brain electrical activity.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Video EEG Cap Monitoring\",\"description\":\"Continuous EEG monitoring combined with synchronized video recording for seizure evaluation.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Sleep EEG Monitoring\",\"description\":\"EEG recording performed during sleep to evaluate sleep disorders and abnormal brain activity.\"}]','[]','[\"Clean scalp after testing\",\"Remove gel residue carefully\",\"Monitor for skin irritation\",\"Follow specialist recommendations\",\"Resume normal activities after use\"]','[\"Mild scalp irritation\",\"Temporary discomfort from tight fitting\",\"Anxiety during testing\",\"Skin sensitivity reactions\",\"Minor inconvenience during prolonged monitoring\"]','<p>EEG caps improve diagnostic accuracy and support effective neurological and psychiatric evaluations.</p>','<p>EEG caps are an important component of modern neurological testing that improve the accuracy and efficiency of brain activity monitoring. Early diagnosis and proper neurological follow-up support better long-term health outcomes.</p>','EEG Caps | Brain Activity Monitoring and Neurological ','Learn about EEG Caps including brain wave monitoring, seizure evaluation, neurological testing, risks, and EEG diagnostic support.','EEG caps, brain wave monitoring, EEG testing equipment, neurological evaluation, seizure diagnostic testing',1,'2026-05-09 08:42:35','2026-05-09 10:37:57',NULL),(118,'EEG Amplifiers','procedures/banners/f3ad4b9a-537d-47e5-9d85-488ed781a7ad.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/93187a4d-13e0-4138-a7f0-d1d272ecd53c.webp','eeg-amplifiers','<p>EEG amplifiers are devices used to enhance and process weak electrical signals recorded from the brain.</p>','<p>They improve signal quality for accurate EEG interpretation in neurological and psychiatric assessments.</p>','[\"Seizure disorders\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Neurological dysfunction\",\"Cognitive abnormalities\",\"Brain activity monitoring requirements\"]','[\"Epilepsy\",\"Neurological disorders\",\"Abnormal brain activity\",\"Sleep-related neurological conditions\",\"Cognitive and behavioral disorders\"]','[\"History of seizures\",\"Neurological diseases\",\"Chronic sleep disorders\",\"Brain injury\",\"Cognitive dysfunction\"]','[\"Maintain regular neurological follow-up\",\"Follow prescribed neurological treatments\",\"Attend early evaluation for abnormal neurological symptoms\",\"Maintain healthy sleep habits\",\"Use properly calibrated EEG systems\"]','[\"Electroencephalogram (EEG)\",\"Video EEG monitoring\",\"Sleep EEG studies\",\"Neurological examination\",\"Brain activity assessment\"]','<p>EEG amplifiers are specialized devices used during EEG testing to strengthen and process weak electrical signals generated by brain activity. These devices improve recording clarity, reduce signal noise, and enhance the accuracy of neurological and psychiatric evaluations.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Standard EEG Amplifier Systems\",\"description\":\"Amplification systems used during routine EEG recordings for neurological evaluation.\"},{\"name\":\"2. High-Density EEG Amplifiers\",\"description\":\"Advanced EEG systems designed for detailed brain activity mapping and research applications.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Video EEG Amplifier Integration\",\"description\":\"Amplifier systems integrated with continuous video EEG monitoring for seizure assessment.\"}]','[]','[\"Ensure proper maintenance of equipment\",\"Verify accurate calibration regularly\",\"Follow technical safety guidelines\",\"Review results with specialists\",\"Continue recommended neurological care\"]','[\"Technical recording errors\",\"Signal interference issues\",\"Inaccurate readings if improperly calibrated\",\"Minor testing discomfort\",\"Delays due to equipment adjustments\"]','<p>EEG amplifiers improve the reliability and precision of brain activity assessments for better patient care.</p>','<p>EEG amplifiers are essential components of neurological diagnostic systems that improve the accuracy and quality of brain activity recordings. Proper equipment use and specialist interpretation support effective neurological diagnosis and long-term patient management.</p>','EEG Amplifiers | Brain Signal Processing and EEG Diagnostics','Learn about EEG Amplifiers including brain signal enhancement, EEG diagnostics, neurological monitoring, equipment accuracy, and patient care.','EEG amplifiers, brain signal processing, EEG diagnostic equipment, neurological brain monitoring, EEG technology',1,'2026-05-09 09:43:34','2026-05-09 10:38:52',NULL),(119,'Biofeedback Devices','procedures/banners/5a923a59-b797-4560-9aa1-17cf4d80ab41.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/0686383e-7a00-4513-8067-c21d7857ab95.webp','biofeedback-devices','<p>Biofeedback devices monitor body functions such as heart rate, muscle tension, and breathing patterns to assist stress and emotional regulation therapy.</p>','<p>These devices help individuals learn how to control physical stress responses through guided training.</p>','[\"Anxiety disorders\",\"Stress-related symptoms\",\"Muscle tension\",\"Sleep disturbances\",\"Emotional dysregulation\"]','[\"Chronic stress\",\"Anxiety disorders\",\"Poor emotional regulation\",\"Sleep-related disturbances\",\"Stress-induced physical symptoms\"]','[\"High stress levels\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"Untreated anxiety disorders\",\"Emotional instability\",\"Lack of stress management practices\"]','[\"Practice regular relaxation techniques\",\"Maintain healthy sleep habits\",\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Follow stress management strategies consistently\",\"Maintain a balanced lifestyle\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Stress evaluation\",\"Behavioral assessment\",\"Physiological monitoring\",\"Mental health evaluation\"]','<p>Biofeedback devices are specialized tools used to monitor physiological functions such as heart rate, breathing, muscle tension, and skin temperature. These devices provide real-time feedback that helps individuals learn relaxation techniques and improve stress management, emotional regulation, and overall mental wellness.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Heart Rate Biofeedback Devices\",\"description\":\"Devices used to monitor heart rate patterns and improve stress and emotional regulation.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Muscle Tension Biofeedback Devices\",\"description\":\"Monitors muscle activity to help reduce stress-related muscle tension and discomfort.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Neurofeedback Devices\",\"description\":\"Advanced biofeedback systems used to monitor brain activity and support emotional regulation training.\"}]','[]','[\"Practice relaxation techniques regularly\",\"Maintain device hygiene and maintenance\",\"Attend therapy follow-ups consistently\",\"Monitor stress response improvements\",\"Follow therapist instructions carefully\"]','[\"Frustration during training\",\"Inconsistent results with irregular use\",\"Technical device errors\",\"Temporary emotional discomfort\",\"Dependence on device-guided feedback\"]','<p>Biofeedback devices support improved stress control, emotional balance, and long-term mental wellness.</p>','<p>Biofeedback devices are valuable tools for stress management and emotional regulation therapy. Consistent use, guided training, and regular follow-up help improve mental wellness and long-term emotional stability.</p>','Biofeedback Devices | Stress and Emotional Regulation ','Learn about Biofeedback Devices including stress monitoring, emotional regulation therapy, relaxation training, and mental wellness support.','biofeedback devices, stress management devices, emotional regulation therapy, neurofeedback equipment, relaxation therapy tools',1,'2026-05-09 09:48:07','2026-05-09 10:39:49',NULL),(120,'Neurophysiology Lab','procedures/banners/8286824d-3a69-4af3-a5c9-ea0087491b9b.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/83e7109c-b3fd-4971-97fe-bc40b91009a5.webp','neurophysiology-lab','A Neurophysiology Lab is a specialized diagnostic facility designed to evaluate the electrical activity and functional health of the brain, spinal cord, peripheral nerves, and muscles. These laboratories use advanced neurodiagnostic technologies to help diagnose neurological, neuromuscular, seizure-related, sleep-related, and nerve conduction disorders affecting the nervous system.','Neurophysiology laboratories are equipped with advanced diagnostic systems such as EEG, Video EEG, EMG, Nerve Conduction Studies (NCS), Evoked Potential systems, and sleep monitoring equipment. These facilities support neurologists and neurophysiology specialists in diagnosing epilepsy, neuropathies, muscle disorders, nerve injuries, movement disorders, spinal conditions, and other neurological abnormalities. Neurophysiology labs play an essential role in early diagnosis, treatment planning, rehabilitation monitoring, and long-term neurological care.','[{\"value\":\"Seizures, blackouts, or episodes of loss of consciousness\"},{\"value\":\"Numbness, tingling, or muscle weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic nerve pain or abnormal muscle movements\"},{\"value\":\"Sleep disturbances or unexplained neurological symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty with movement, coordination, balance, or speech\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Epilepsy and seizure disorders\"},{\"value\":\"Peripheral neuropathy and nerve compression syndromes\"},{\"value\":\"Muscular and neuromuscular disorders\"},{\"value\":\"Brain injuries, stroke, or spinal cord abnormalities\"},{\"value\":\"Autoimmune, metabolic, or degenerative neurological conditions\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Mild discomfort during certain neurophysiological procedures\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary muscle soreness after EMG testing\"},{\"value\":\"Rare triggering of seizures during activation procedures in EEG studies\"},{\"value\":\"Requirement for prolonged monitoring in complex neurological conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Need for specialized interpretation by trained neurophysiology professionals\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Neurophysiology labs support accurate diagnosis and comprehensive neurological care by providing advanced functional assessments of the nervous system. Based on the diagnostic findings, treatment may include anti-seizure medications, neurological rehabilitation, physiotherapy, pain management, nerve decompression procedures, sleep disorder management, surgical planning, lifestyle modification, and long-term neurological follow-up. Neurophysiological monitoring also assists physicians in evaluating treatment effectiveness, disease progression, and recovery after neurological injury or intervention.\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Neurophysiology labs support accurate diagnosis and comprehensive neurological care by providing advanced functional assessments of the nervous system. Based on the diagnostic findings, treatment may include anti-seizure medications, neurological rehabilitation, physiotherapy, pain management, nerve decompression procedures, sleep disorder management, surgical planning, lifestyle modification, and long-term neurological follow-up. Neurophysiological monitoring also assists physicians in evaluating treatment effectiveness, disease progression, and recovery after neurological injury or intervention.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Follow-up consultation to review neurophysiological test results\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring symptoms and neurological function after testing\"},{\"value\":\"Continuation of medications or rehabilitation programs if advised\"},{\"value\":\"Additional imaging or neurological evaluation when required\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term neurological monitoring and specialist follow-up care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Mild discomfort during certain neurophysiological procedures\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary muscle soreness after EMG testing\"},{\"value\":\"Rare triggering of seizures during activation procedures in EEG studies\"},{\"value\":\"Requirement for prolonged monitoring in complex neurological conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Need for specialized interpretation by trained neurophysiology professionals\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Neurophysiology labs support accurate diagnosis and comprehensive neurological care by providing advanced functional assessments of the nervous system. Based on the diagnostic findings, treatment may include anti-seizure medications, neurological rehabilitation, physiotherapy, pain management, nerve decompression procedures, sleep disorder management, surgical planning, lifestyle modification, and long-term neurological follow-up. Neurophysiological monitoring also assists physicians in evaluating treatment effectiveness, disease progression, and recovery after neurological injury or intervention.\"}]','Neurophysiology laboratories play a vital role in early neurological diagnosis, treatment planning, rehabilitation monitoring, and long-term nervous system care. Advancements in digital neurodiagnostic systems, AI-assisted neurological analysis, prolonged monitoring technologies, and minimally invasive diagnostic techniques continue to improve diagnostic accuracy, treatment outcomes, neurological recovery, and overall patient quality of life.','','Neurophysiology Lab','A Neurophysiology Lab is a specialized diagnostic facility designed to evaluate the electrical activity and functional health of the brain, spinal cord, peripheral nerves, and muscles. These laboratories use advanced neurodiagnostic technologies to help diagnose neurological, neuromuscular, seizure-related, sleep-related, and nerve conduction disorders affecting the nervous system.','',1,'2026-05-09 09:48:58','2026-06-10 01:58:10',NULL),(121,'Telepsychiatry / Consultation Facilities','procedures/banners/97b223a9-fcab-457e-a6f6-5d9af55bd9b9.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/a1e12d91-a200-402a-9cf8-f12d1be4570a.webp','telepsychiatry-consultation-facilities','Telepsychiatry and consultation facilities are advanced digital mental healthcare systems designed to provide psychiatric consultations, psychological counseling, therapy sessions, medication management, crisis support, and long-term mental health follow-up through secure virtual communication platforms. These facilities improve accessibility to mental healthcare services while supporting continuity of treatment, emotional support, and remote patient monitoring.','Telepsychiatry facilities integrate secure video conferencing systems, digital patient management platforms, electronic medical records, online therapy tools, remote monitoring technologies, and virtual counseling services to deliver comprehensive mental healthcare. These facilities are widely used in psychiatry clinics, hospitals, rehabilitation centers, counseling services, and behavioral health departments for managing depression, anxiety disorders, addiction, stress-related conditions, sleep disorders, trauma, and chronic psychiatric illnesses. Teleconsultation systems also support multidisciplinary collaboration, follow-up care, and remote mental wellness programs.','[{\"value\":\"Persistent anxiety, depression, or emotional distress\"},{\"value\":\"Stress, panic attacks, or sleep disturbances\"},{\"value\":\"Social withdrawal, mood changes, or behavioral difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Need for regular psychiatric follow-up or counseling support\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional or psychological symptoms affecting daily functioning\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Depression, anxiety disorders, and stress-related conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Trauma, grief, or emotional burnout\"},{\"value\":\"Relationship difficulties and social isolation\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic illness or long-term mental health conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Need for accessible psychiatric and psychological care services\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Limited physical observation during virtual consultations\"},{\"value\":\"Dependence on internet connectivity and digital infrastructure\"},{\"value\":\"Privacy and cybersecurity concerns in online healthcare systems\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty managing severe psychiatric emergencies remotely\"},{\"value\":\"Requirement for in-person evaluation in complex or high-risk cases\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Telepsychiatry and consultation facilities support virtual psychiatric evaluations, psychotherapy sessions, medication management, emotional wellness counseling, CBT, DBT, stress management programs, family counseling, addiction recovery support, sleep management guidance, and crisis intervention services. These facilities may also provide remote monitoring, digital therapy platforms, rehabilitation support, lifestyle counseling, and multidisciplinary care coordination involving psychiatrists, psychologists, counselors, and primary care providers to improve long-term mental healthcare outcomes.\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Telepsychiatry and consultation facilities support virtual psychiatric evaluations, psychotherapy sessions, medication management, emotional wellness counseling, CBT, DBT, stress management programs, family counseling, addiction recovery support, sleep management guidance, and crisis intervention services. These facilities may also provide remote monitoring, digital therapy platforms, rehabilitation support, lifestyle counseling, and multidisciplinary care coordination involving psychiatrists, psychologists, counselors, and primary care providers to improve long-term mental healthcare outcomes.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Regular virtual psychiatric and counseling follow-up sessions\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring treatment response and emotional well-being remotely\"},{\"value\":\"Medication review and psychotherapy progress evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Patient education regarding coping strategies and mental wellness\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term digital mental healthcare support and relapse prevention planning\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Limited physical observation during virtual consultations\"},{\"value\":\"Dependence on internet connectivity and digital infrastructure\"},{\"value\":\"Privacy and cybersecurity concerns in online healthcare systems\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty managing severe psychiatric emergencies remotely\"},{\"value\":\"Requirement for in-person evaluation in complex or high-risk cases\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Telepsychiatry and consultation facilities support virtual psychiatric evaluations, psychotherapy sessions, medication management, emotional wellness counseling, CBT, DBT, stress management programs, family counseling, addiction recovery support, sleep management guidance, and crisis intervention services. These facilities may also provide remote monitoring, digital therapy platforms, rehabilitation support, lifestyle counseling, and multidisciplinary care coordination involving psychiatrists, psychologists, counselors, and primary care providers to improve long-term mental healthcare outcomes.\"}]','Telepsychiatry and consultation facilities significantly improve access to mental healthcare, continuity of treatment, emotional support, and patient convenience. Advancements in secure telemedicine systems, digital counseling platforms, AI-assisted mental health technologies, and remote monitoring tools continue to enhance treatment accessibility, patient engagement, emotional resilience, long-term mental wellness, and overall quality of life.','','Telepsychiatry / Consultation Facilities','Telepsychiatry and consultation facilities are advanced digital mental healthcare systems designed to provide psychiatric consultations, psychological counseling, therapy sessions, medication management, crisis support, and long-term mental health follow-up through secure virtual communication platforms. These facilities improve accessibility to mental healthcare services while supporting continuity of treatment, emotional support, and remote patient monitoring.','',1,'2026-05-09 09:49:45','2026-06-10 01:58:10',NULL),(122,'Psychiatric Counseling Rooms','procedures/banners/9f2842fc-56d0-4f49-9cbb-aa326ec3d523.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/642c3b3b-72ab-4ddc-9d33-2be53a7d06c3.webp','psychiatric-counseling-rooms','<p>Psychiatric counseling rooms are private and therapeutic spaces designed for mental health consultations and therapy sessions.</p>','<p>These rooms provide a safe, confidential, and comfortable environment for emotional discussions and psychiatric evaluations.</p>','[\"Emotional distress\",\"Anxiety or depression\",\"Behavioral concerns\",\"Relationship or family conflicts\",\"Stress-related disorders\"]','[\"Mental health disorders\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Stress-related conditions\",\"Relationship difficulties\",\"Behavioral and psychological challenges\"]','[\"Untreated emotional distress\",\"Lack of mental health support\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"Social isolation\",\"Chronic psychological stress\"]','[\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain regular counseling sessions\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Build healthy emotional support systems\",\"Maintain open communication about mental health\"]','[\"Psychiatric evaluation\",\"Mental health assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Emotional wellness screening\",\"Clinical interview\"]','<p>Psychiatric counseling rooms are specially designed therapeutic environments used for psychiatric consultations, counseling sessions, psychotherapy, and emotional support services. These private and confidential spaces help create a calm and supportive atmosphere that improves patient comfort, communication, and therapy effectiveness.</p>','[{\"name\":\"1. Individual Counseling Sessions\",\"description\":\"Private therapeutic consultations focused on emotional support and mental health treatment.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Family and Couples Counseling\",\"description\":\"Counseling sessions involving family members or couples to improve communication and emotional relationships.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Psychotherapy Consultation Rooms\",\"description\":\"Dedicated therapeutic spaces used for structured psychotherapy and psychiatric evaluations.\"}]','[]','[\"Attend counseling sessions consistently\",\"Practice coping strategies regularly\",\"Maintain open communication with therapists\",\"Follow treatment recommendations carefully\",\"Build supportive emotional environments\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during discussions\",\"Anxiety related to therapy sessions\",\"Temporary emotional triggering\",\"Privacy concerns if improperly managed\",\"Reduced effectiveness without patient engagement\"]','<p>Proper counseling environments improve therapy effectiveness, emotional comfort, and long-term mental wellness outcomes.</p>','<p>Psychiatric counseling rooms play an important role in providing safe and supportive environments for mental health care. Comfortable therapeutic settings, regular counseling, and professional guidance help improve emotional well-being and long-term recovery outcomes.</p>','Psychiatric Counseling Rooms | Safe Mental Health Therapy.','Learn about Psychiatric Counseling Rooms including therapy environments, mental health consultations, emotional support, and psychiatric care services.','psychiatric counseling rooms, mental health therapy rooms, psychotherapy consultation spaces, emotional support counseling, psychiatric care facilities',1,'2026-05-09 09:50:30','2026-05-09 10:43:23',NULL),(123,'Therapy Rooms',NULL,NULL,'therapy-rooms','Therapy rooms are specialized spaces designed for psychological therapy, counseling, behavioral therapy, and rehabilitation sessions.','They support individual, family, group, and behavioral therapies in a structured and calming environment.','[\"Emotional stress\",\"Behavioral difficulties\",\"Anxiety or depression\",\"Communication challenges\",\"Rehabilitation or therapy needs\"]','[\"Mental health disorders\",\"Emotional trauma\",\"Behavioral challenges\",\"Stress-related conditions\",\"Psychological rehabilitation requirements\"]','[\"Untreated emotional distress\",\"Poor coping mechanisms\",\"Lack of psychological support\",\"Chronic stress exposure\",\"Behavioral or relationship difficulties\"]','[\"Seek mental health support early\",\"Maintain regular therapy sessions\",\"Practice stress management techniques\",\"Build healthy emotional support systems\",\"Follow therapist recommendations consistently\"]','[\"Psychological assessment\",\"Behavioral evaluation\",\"Mental health screening\",\"Clinical interview\",\"Emotional wellness assessment\"]','Therapy rooms are professionally designed spaces used for psychological counseling, psychotherapy, behavioral therapy, rehabilitation sessions, and emotional support services. These environments provide privacy, comfort, and a calming atmosphere that supports effective communication and therapeutic progress.','[{\"name\":\"1. Individual Therapy Rooms\",\"description\":\"Private therapy spaces designed for one-on-one psychological counseling and psychotherapy sessions.\"},{\"name\":\"2. Family and Group Therapy Rooms\",\"description\":\"Structured therapy environments used for family counseling and group therapy sessions.\"},{\"name\":\"3. Behavioral Rehabilitation Therapy Rooms\",\"description\":\"Specialized spaces used for behavioral therapy, rehabilitation, and emotional regulation training.\"}]','[\"Emotional and behavioral improvement develops gradually through therapy sessions\",\"Coping and communication skills strengthen over time\",\"Long-term participation supports emotional wellness and rehabilitation\",\"Regular follow-up therapy may be required depending on the condition\"]','[\"Continue therapy sessions consistently\",\"Apply learned coping techniques daily\",\"Maintain emotional support systems\",\"Follow therapist recommendations carefully\",\"Monitor emotional and behavioral progress\"]','[\"Emotional discomfort during therapy\",\"Anxiety discussing sensitive issues\",\"Temporary emotional triggering\",\"Limited progress without active participation\",\"Resistance to therapeutic interventions\"]','Therapy rooms support effective treatment delivery, emotional recovery, behavioral improvement, and long-term psychological wellness.','Therapy rooms provide safe and supportive environments for psychological treatment and emotional rehabilitation. Consistent therapy participation and professional guidance help improve emotional stability, behavioral health, and long-term mental wellness.','Therapy Rooms | Psychological Counseling and Rehabilitation Spaces','Learn about Therapy Rooms including psychological counseling, behavioral therapy, emotional rehabilitation, and mental wellness support.','therapy rooms, psychological counseling spaces, behavioral therapy rooms, psychotherapy facilities, mental health rehabilitation rooms',1,'2026-05-09 09:51:14','2026-05-09 09:51:14',NULL),(124,'Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation',NULL,NULL,'physiotherapy-and-rehabilitation','Physiotherapy and rehabilitation are non-surgical treatment methods used to restore movement, strength, flexibility, balance, and physical function after injury, surgery, or chronic orthopedic conditions.','Physiotherapy involves guided exercises, stretching techniques, muscle strengthening, posture correction, and pain-relieving therapies performed under the supervision of trained physiotherapists. Rehabilitation programs help patients recover mobility, reduce pain, prevent disability, and improve overall quality of life.','[{\"value\":\"Joint stiffness and reduced mobility\"},{\"value\":\"Muscle weakness after injury or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty walking or performing daily activities\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic musculoskeletal pain\"},{\"value\":\"Poor balance and coordination\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary muscle soreness after exercises\"},{\"value\":\"Mild pain during rehabilitation sessions\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue from repetitive exercises\"},{\"value\":\"Slow recovery in severe conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of reinjury if exercises are done incorrectly\"}]','[]','[]','Physiotherapy and rehabilitation focus on restoring movement, strength, flexibility, and physical function.','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Attend physiotherapy sessions regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow prescribed home exercise programs\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain proper posture and body mechanics\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid excessive strain during recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor improvement in movement and strength\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary muscle soreness after exercises\"},{\"value\":\"Mild pain during rehabilitation sessions\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue from repetitive exercises\"},{\"value\":\"Slow recovery in severe conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of reinjury if exercises are done incorrectly\"}]','Consistent physiotherapy and rehabilitation can significantly improve mobility and physical function.','Physiotherapy and rehabilitation help patients regain movement, strength, and independence.','Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation Treatment','Learn about physiotherapy and rehabilitation for orthopedic recovery and pain relief.','physiotherapy, rehabilitation therapy, orthopedic physiotherapy',1,'2026-05-12 06:08:48','2026-07-29 00:28:09',NULL),(125,'Pain Management with Medications','procedures/banners/451fe222-6f5b-4520-ac49-cceda8da1301.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/ba6b6b6c-75e9-4b04-8e0a-248e855e1845.webp','pain-management-with-medications','<p>Pain management with medications involves the use of medicines to reduce inflammation, relieve pain, and improve mobility in orthopedic conditions.</p>','<p>Doctors may prescribe painkillers, anti-inflammatory medications, muscle relaxants, nerve pain medications, or topical treatments depending on the condition.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Persistent joint or bone pain\"},{\"value\":\"Muscle spasms and stiffness\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling and inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced physical activity due to pain\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty sleeping because of discomfort\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Pain Management with Medications as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Gastric irritation or ulcers\"},{\"value\":\"Drowsiness or dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic reactions to medications\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney or liver side effects with long-term use\"},{\"value\":\"Dependency on strong painkillers\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Medication therapy helps reduce inflammation and pain in orthopedic conditions.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid self-medication or overdose\"},{\"value\":\"Stay hydrated and maintain proper diet\"},{\"value\":\"Report side effects to the doctor promptly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up consultations regularly\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Gastric irritation or ulcers\"},{\"value\":\"Drowsiness or dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic reactions to medications\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney or liver side effects with long-term use\"},{\"value\":\"Dependency on strong painkillers\"}]','<p>Proper medication management can effectively control pain and improve daily functioning.</p>','<p>Pain management medications reduce discomfort and improve mobility.</p>','Pain Management with Medications','Learn about orthopedic pain management medications.','pain management, orthopedic medications',1,'2026-05-12 06:08:48','2026-07-29 00:28:09',NULL),(126,'Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction','procedures/banners/a57551a4-2889-4395-adbd-32d98e50094c.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/b75a2cfe-86d3-4391-aa61-c6040c360182.webp','activity-modification-and-ergonomic-correction','<p>Activity modification and ergonomic correction involve adjusting daily activities and posture to reduce stress on bones and joints.</p>','<p>This treatment focuses on preventing further injury and reducing pain through posture correction and movement improvement.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Pain during repetitive movements\"},{\"value\":\"Neck and back discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Joint strain during work activities\"},{\"value\":\"Muscle fatigue from poor posture\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced productivity due to pain\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty adapting to lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort during posture correction\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete symptom relief if habits continue\"},{\"value\":\"Slow improvement in chronic conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of recurrence without long-term compliance\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Ergonomic correction improves posture and reduces orthopedic strain.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain proper sitting and standing posture\"},{\"value\":\"Use ergonomic furniture and supports\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid repetitive strain activities\"},{\"value\":\"Take regular stretching breaks during work\"},{\"value\":\"Follow physiotherapy guidance consistently\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty adapting to lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort during posture correction\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete symptom relief if habits continue\"},{\"value\":\"Slow improvement in chronic conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of recurrence without long-term compliance\"}]','<p>Ergonomic correction can significantly reduce pain and prevent recurrence.</p>','<p>Activity modification improves long-term orthopedic health.</p>','Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction','Learn about ergonomic correction and activity modification.','ergonomic correction, posture improvement',1,'2026-05-12 06:08:48','2026-07-29 00:28:09',NULL),(127,'Weight Reduction and Lifestyle Modification','procedures/banners/0157fc84-b3a0-48a3-aae0-18ca5c76f0e3.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/e0bf3649-01d2-45fd-a3a0-0ecf5d423f67.webp','weight-reduction-and-lifestyle-modification','<p>Weight reduction and lifestyle modification help decrease stress on joints and improve orthopedic health.</p>','<p>Balanced nutrition, exercise, and healthy habits improve mobility and reduce orthopedic complications.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Joint pain during walking or climbing stairs\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced physical endurance\"},{\"value\":\"Back pain related to obesity\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue during daily activities\"},{\"value\":\"Progressive joint degeneration\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Weight Reduction and Lifestyle Modification is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"va