n about Percutaneous Nephrolithotomy for complex kidney stones.','PCNL, kidney stone surgery, nephrolithotomy',1,'2026-05-15 06:12:02','2026-07-29 00:28:15',NULL),(186,'Flexible & Rigid Ureteroscopy',NULL,NULL,'flexible-rigid-ureteroscopy','Flexible and rigid ureteroscopy systems are advanced endoscopic instruments used for diagnosing and treating ureteric and kidney diseases.','Rigid ureteroscopes are mainly used for lower ureteric stones, while flexible ureteroscopes access deep kidney structures for complex stone treatment.','[{\"value\":\"Kidney stones\"},{\"value\":\"Ureteric stones\"},{\"value\":\"Blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary obstruction\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent flank pain\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Flexible & Rigid Ureteroscopy is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary stent discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Ureteral injury\"},{\"value\":\"Residual stone fragments\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Direct stone visualization\"},{\"value\":\"Endoscopic ureter evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Laser stone fragmentation\"},{\"value\":\"Tumor inspection\"},{\"value\":\"Biopsy procedures\"}]','The scope is passed through the natural urinary tract into the ureter or kidney for diagnosis and minimally invasive treatment.','[{\"name\":\"Rigid Ureteroscopy\",\"description\":\"Used primarily for lower ureteric stones\"},{\"name\":\"Flexible Ureteroscopy\",\"description\":\"Used for kidney stones and complex urinary anatomy\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Recovery is usually rapid\"},{\"value\":\"Hospital stay is commonly short\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary stent placement may be required\"},{\"value\":\"Mild urinary discomfort may occur briefly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up imaging may be advised\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Drink adequate fluids\"},{\"value\":\"Follow stent care instructions\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for fever or severe pain\"},{\"value\":\"Attend scheduled follow-up visits\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary stent discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Ureteral injury\"},{\"value\":\"Residual stone fragments\"}]','Flexible and rigid ureteroscopy provide excellent minimally invasive stone treatment outcomes with rapid recovery.','Ureteroscopy is one of the most important minimally invasive procedures in modern endourology.','Flexible & Rigid Ureteroscopy','Learn about ureteroscopy systems for urinary stone treatment.','ureteroscopy, flexible ureteroscopy, rigid ureteroscopy',1,'2026-05-15 06:12:02','2026-07-29 00:28:16',NULL),(187,'Dialysis Access Coordination',NULL,NULL,'dialysis-access-coordination','Dialysis access coordination is a specialized healthcare service that manages the planning, creation, maintenance, and monitoring of vascular or peritoneal access for patients requiring dialysis treatment.','This coordination system plays a critical role in patients with chronic kidney disease or kidney failure because successful dialysis depends on reliable and safe access to the bloodstream or abdominal cavity. The service involves close collaboration between urologists, nephrologists, vascular surgeons, interventional radiologists, dialysis technicians, and nursing staff to ensure timely and effective dialysis preparation.','[{\"value\":\"Advanced kidney failure\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced urine output\"},{\"value\":\"High creatinine levels\"},{\"value\":\"Fluid retention and swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Requirement for long-term dialysis\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Dialysis Access Coordination as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection at access site\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clot formation\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Access blockage or narrowing\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed dialysis treatment\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Patient evaluation and counseling\"},{\"value\":\"AV fistula planning\"},{\"value\":\"AV graft placement coordination\"},{\"value\":\"Dialysis catheter insertion scheduling\"},{\"value\":\"Imaging and vascular assessment\"}]','Dialysis access coordination ensures that patients receive the appropriate vascular or peritoneal access at the correct time to support effective and life-saving dialysis treatment.','[{\"name\":\"AV Fistula\",\"description\":\"Surgical connection between artery and vein for long-term dialysis access\"},{\"name\":\"AV Graft\",\"description\":\"Artificial graft placement to support dialysis blood flow\"},{\"name\":\"Dialysis Catheter\",\"description\":\"Temporary or tunneled catheter insertion for urgent dialysis\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Initial access healing occurs over several weeks\"},{\"value\":\"Regular monitoring ensures access maturation\"},{\"value\":\"Dialysis may begin immediately for temporary catheters\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term follow-up is essential\"},{\"value\":\"Continuous maintenance improves access durability\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Protect the dialysis access arm carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain proper hygiene around access site\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for redness or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Attend dialysis appointments regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow nephrology and surgical advice strictly\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Infection at access site\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clot formation\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Access blockage or narrowing\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed dialysis treatment\"}]','Effective dialysis access coordination significantly improves long-term dialysis success and patient quality of life. Well-maintained dialysis access can function effectively for many years and supports safer, more efficient dialysis treatment.','Dialysis access coordination plays a critical role in safe and successful long-term dialysis care.','Dialysis Access Coordination','Learn about dialysis access coordination for long-term kidney failure management.','dialysis access, AV fistula, dialysis catheter coordination',1,'2026-05-15 06:13:19','2026-07-29 00:28:16',NULL),(188,'Urology OT with C-Arm',NULL,NULL,'urology-ot-with-c-arm','A Urology Operation Theatre (OT) with C-Arm is a highly specialized surgical facility equipped with advanced fluoroscopic imaging technology used during minimally invasive urological procedures.','The C-Arm is a mobile imaging device that provides real-time X-ray visualization during surgery. It allows surgeons to accurately guide instruments, place stents, identify stones, and perform complex procedures with high precision.','[{\"value\":\"Kidney or ureteric stones\"},{\"value\":\"Urinary obstruction\"},{\"value\":\"Need for stent placement\"},{\"value\":\"Complex reconstructive surgeries\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent urinary tract abnormalities\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Urology OT with C-Arm is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Radiation exposure\"},