abnormal readings\"},{\"value\":\"Need for additional investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort from monitoring belts\"}]','<p>Fetal monitoring systems improve early detection of fetal distress and reduce risks during pregnancy and labor.</p>','<p>NST and CTG monitoring are essential tools in modern obstetric care.</p>','Fetal Monitoring NST CTG','Learn about NST and CTG fetal monitoring during pregnancy.','NST monitoring, CTG fetal monitoring, fetal distress monitoring',1,'2026-05-15 06:27:43','2026-07-29 00:28:16',NULL),(194,'Labor Room with Birthing Beds','procedures/banners/efe4c0c6-b739-4ef5-a808-2508208b4cc4.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/8995b2b2-c6ac-414d-bf72-fb9306785333.webp','labor-room-with-birthing-beds','<p>A Labor Room with Birthing Beds is a specialized maternity care facility designed for safe labor, childbirth, maternal monitoring, and emergency obstetric management.</p>','<p>The labor room includes advanced birthing beds, fetal monitoring systems, emergency resuscitation equipment, oxygen support, and neonatal care facilities to ensure safe delivery for both mother and baby.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Active labor pain\"},{\"value\":\"Regular uterine contractions\"},{\"value\":\"Rupture of membranes\"},{\"value\":\"Vaginal bleeding during labor\"},{\"value\":\"High-risk labor conditions\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Labor Room with Birthing Beds is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Labor complications\"},{\"value\":\"Maternal bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal distress\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency surgical requirements\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maternal vital sign monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal heart monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Labor progression assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency obstetric evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal monitoring\"}]','<p>Modern labor rooms support normal vaginal delivery, assisted delivery, and emergency obstetric care under continuous medical supervision.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Normal Vaginal Delivery\",\"description\":\"Routine childbirth under medical supervision\"},{\"name\":\"Assisted Delivery\",\"description\":\"Instrument-assisted vaginal delivery\"},{\"name\":\"Emergency Obstetric Management\",\"description\":\"Urgent intervention during labor complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor maternal vital signs regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Support breastfeeding initiation\"},{\"value\":\"Observe for post-delivery bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Provide pain management support\"},{\"value\":\"Continue newborn monitoring carefully\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Labor complications\"},{\"value\":\"Maternal bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal distress\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency surgical requirements\"}]','<p>Modern labor room facilities improve maternal and neonatal safety through continuous monitoring and emergency readiness.</p>','<p>Labor rooms with birthing beds are essential for safe childbirth and emergency obstetric care.</p>','Labor Room with Birthing Beds','Learn about labor room facilities and birthing beds for safe childbirth.','labor room, birthing beds, maternity care facility',1,'2026-05-15 06:27:43','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(195,'Modular Obstetric OT','procedures/banners/34778ec0-442a-47ea-be21-c5398a8fc87a.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/bef9b79f-ec06-4dfb-90e1-d1e12b29493c.webp','modular-obstetric-ot','<p>A Modular Obstetric Operation Theatre is a highly advanced surgical facility designed specifically for obstetric and gynecological surgeries including cesarean sections and emergency maternal procedures.</p>','<p>The modular design supports sterile conditions, infection control, efficient workflow, and rapid emergency response during obstetric surgeries.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Complicated labor\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal distress\"},{\"value\":\"Placental complications\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency cesarean requirement\"},{\"value\":\"Severe maternal bleeding\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Modular Obstetric OT is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Surgical bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Anesthesia complications\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency maternal instability\"},{\"value\":\"Post-operative recovery complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maternal surgical monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Anesthesia monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal emergency assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Postpartum hemorrhage evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal stabilization support\"}]','<p>The facility includes modular sterile systems, operating tables, anesthesia workstations, surgical instruments, and emergency neonatal support systems.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Cesarean Section\",\"description\":\"Surgical delivery of the baby\"},{\"name\":\"Emergency Obstetric Surgery\",\"description\":\"Urgent maternal surgical procedures\"},{\"name\":\"Gynecological Surgery\",\"description\":\"Advanced gynecological operative procedures\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor maternal recovery closely\"},{\"value\":\"Assess surgical wound healing\"},{\"value\":\"Provide pain management support\"},{\"value\":\"Encourage early mobilization if advised\"},{\"value\":\"Continue newborn and maternal observation\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Surgical bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Anesthesia complications\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency maternal instability\"},{\"value\":\"Post-operative recovery complications\"}]','<p>Modular obstetric OTs improve surgical precision, reduce infection rates, and enhance maternal-fetal safety.</p>','<p>Modular obstetric operation theatres are essential for modern emergency obstetric and gynecological care.</p>','Modular Obstetric OT','Learn about modular obstetric operation theatres and emergency obstetric surgery.','modular obstetric OT, cesarean OT, obstetric surgery facility',1,'2026-05-15 06:27:43','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(196,'Laparoscopy & Hysteroscopy Setup','procedures/banners/6dabe8f1-c850-44c7-b39f-dabc9fff01e0.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/ab764e93-1f4d-49c4-8e3f-f851497138a1.webp','laparoscopy-hysteroscopy-setup','<p>Laparoscopy and hysteroscopy setups are minimally invasive gynecological surgical systems used for diagnosing and treating reproductive and pelvic disorders.</p>','<p>Laparoscopy uses a camera inserted through small abdominal incisions while hysteroscopy uses a thin scope inserted through the cervix to examine the uterine cavity.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Pelvic pain\"},{\"value\":\"Infertility\"},{\"value\":\"Abnormal uterine bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Ovarian cysts\"},{\"value\":\"Suspected endometriosis\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Laparoscopy & Hysteroscopy Setup is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to nearby organs\"},{\"value\":\"Anesthesia-related complications\"},{\"value\":\"Rare surgical conversion to open procedure\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Pelvic organ visualization\"},{\"value\":\"Infertility evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Fibroid assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Endometriosis diagnosis\"},{\"value\":\"Uterine cavity examination\"}]','<p>The setup includes HD camera systems, insufflation devices, hysteroscopes, laparoscopes, electrosurgical units, and advanced minimally invasive surgical instruments.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Laparoscopy\",\"description\":\"Minimally invasive pelvic surgery\"},{\"name\":\"Hysteroscopy\",\"description\":\"Endoscopic uterine cavity examination\"},{\"name\":\"Fibroid and Cyst Surgery\",\"description\":\"Minimally invasive reproductive surgery\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain wound hygiene carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid heavy lifting temporarily\"},{\"value\":\"Follow medication instructions properly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for fever or excessive pain\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk\"},{\"value\":\"Injury to nearby organs\"},{\"value\":\"Anesthesia-related complications\"},{\"value\":\"Rare surgical conversion to open procedure\"}]','<p>Laparoscopy and hysteroscopy improve surgical precision, reduce complications, and support fertility preservation.</p>','<p>Laparoscopy and hysteroscopy are essential components of modern minimally invasive gynecological surgery.</p>','Laparoscopy & Hysteroscopy Setup','Learn about laparoscopy and hysteroscopy systems in gynecology.','laparoscopy, hysteroscopy, minimally invasive gynecology',1,'2026-05-15 06:27:43','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(197,'Family Planning & Counseling Facility','procedures/banners/a1a28758-9070-439c-a5ea-5541eb038fd8.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/8bfe77bc-5359-40af-8f85-907ec220f52c.webp','family-planning-counseling-facility','<p>A Family Planning &amp; Counseling Facility is a specialized reproductive healthcare service that provides education, counseling, contraceptive guidance, fertility planning, and reproductive health support for individuals and couples.</p>','<p>The facility helps patients make informed decisions regarding pregnancy planning, birth spacing, contraception, maternal health, and reproductive well-being. Family planning services improve maternal health, reduce unintended pregnancies, and support healthier families and communities.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Need for contraception guidance\"},{\"value\":\"Pregnancy planning concerns\"},{\"value\":\"Irregular reproductive health issues\"},{\"value\":\"Fertility-related counseling needs\"},{\"value\":\"Requests for birth spacing support\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Family Planning & Counseling Facility as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Side effects of contraceptive methods\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional stress regarding reproductive decisions\"},{\"value\":\"Failure of contraception methods\"},{\"value\":\"Lack of compliance with treatment advice\"},{\"value\":\"Misunderstanding of contraceptive use\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Reproductive health assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Contraceptive counseling evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Fertility planning consultation\"},{\"value\":\"Maternal health screening\"},{\"value\":\"Sexual health education assessment\"}]','<p>The facility includes counseling rooms, contraceptive services, fertility awareness education, reproductive health assessments, and trained healthcare professionals specializing in family planning.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Contraceptive Counseling\",\"description\":\"Guidance regarding suitable contraception methods\"},{\"name\":\"Birth Spacing Counseling\",\"description\":\"Support for healthy pregnancy spacing\"},{\"name\":\"Permanent Sterilization Counseling\",\"description\":\"Education regarding permanent contraception procedures\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Attend regular follow-up consultations\"},{\"value\":\"Use contraceptive methods correctly\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain reproductive health check-ups\"},{\"value\":\"Seek counseling support when needed\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Side effects of contraceptive methods\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional stress regarding reproductive decisions\"},{\"value\":\"Failure of contraception methods\"},{\"value\":\"Lack of compliance with treatment advice\"},{\"value\":\"Misunderstanding of contraceptive use\"}]','<p>Family planning and counseling services significantly improve maternal health, reproductive autonomy, and long-term family well-being.</p>','<p>Family planning and counseling facilities are essential for safe reproductive healthcare and healthier pregnancy outcomes.</p>','Family Planning & Counseling Facility','Learn about family planning and reproductive counseling services.','family planning, reproductive counseling, contraception guidance',1,'2026-05-15 06:29:55','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(198,'NABH-Compliant Labor & Delivery Records',NULL,NULL,'nabh-compliant-labor-delivery-records','NABH-Compliant Labor & Delivery Records refer to standardized obstetric documentation systems designed according to National Accreditation Board for Hospitals quality and safety standards.','These records ensure accurate documentation of maternal care, labor monitoring, delivery procedures, newborn status, emergency interventions, and postnatal management.','[{\"value\":\"Need for standardized obstetric records\"},{\"value\":\"High-risk pregnancy documentation requirements\"},{\"value\":\"Labor monitoring documentation needs\"},{\"value\":\"Hospital accreditation compliance\"},{\"value\":\"Maternal and neonatal safety management\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which NABH-Compliant Labor & Delivery Records is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Incomplete medical records\"},{\"value\":\"Documentation errors\"},{\"value\":\"Communication failures between staff\"},{\"value\":\"Legal compliance issues\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced patient safety without proper documentation\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maternal history documentation\"},{\"value\":\"Labor progress charting\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal monitoring record maintenance\"},{\"value\":\"Medication and consent documentation\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal record management\"}]','The documentation system includes antenatal reports, labor charts, fetal monitoring records, surgical notes, neonatal records, and discharge summaries to improve continuity of care and patient safety.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Documentation begins during patient admission\"},{\"value\":\"Records are continuously updated during labor and delivery\"},{\"value\":\"Postnatal records support follow-up care\"},{\"value\":\"Quality audits improve system performance\"},{\"value\":\"Digital systems support long-term record preservation\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain accurate delivery records consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Update maternal and neonatal charts regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow hospital documentation protocols\"},{\"value\":\"Conduct regular quality audits\"},{\"value\":\"Ensure proper consent documentation\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Incomplete medical records\"},{\"value\":\"Documentation errors\"},{\"value\":\"Communication failures between staff\"},{\"value\":\"Legal compliance issues\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced patient safety without proper documentation\"}]','NABH-compliant labor and delivery records improve healthcare quality, reduce medical errors, and support safer maternal and neonatal outcomes.','Standardized obstetric documentation systems are essential for high-quality maternal healthcare.','NABH-Compliant Labor & Delivery Records','Learn about NABH-compliant obstetric documentation systems.','NABH labor records, obstetric documentation, maternity records',1,'2026-05-15 06:29:55','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(199,'Emergency Obstetric Care Infrastructure','procedures/banners/52a30dcb-a2dc-4ca7-a266-c28e29421869.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/dfdbd725-6f79-4775-aa62-12d08cd4f397.webp','emergency-obstetric-care-infrastructure','<p>Emergency Obstetric Care Infrastructure refers to specialized healthcare systems, facilities, equipment, and trained personnel required to manage life-threatening maternal and fetal emergencies.</p>','<p>This infrastructure is essential for reducing maternal and neonatal mortality by ensuring rapid diagnosis, emergency treatment, surgical intervention, and intensive monitoring during obstetric crises.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Severe bleeding during pregnancy or delivery\"},{\"value\":\"High blood pressure with seizures\"},{\"value\":\"Prolonged or obstructed labor\"},{\"value\":\"Fetal distress signs\"},{\"value\":\"Maternal shock or collapse\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Emergency Obstetric Care Infrastructure is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Maternal mortality\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal complications\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infection\"},{\"value\":\"Multi-organ failure\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed emergency intervention\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Emergency fetal monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Maternal vital sign assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Blood loss evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Placental complication assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Critical care monitoring\"}]','<p>The infrastructure includes emergency labor rooms, modular obstetric OTs, blood bank access, neonatal resuscitation units, ICU support, ambulance services, and trained multidisciplinary teams.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Emergency Cesarean Section\",\"description\":\"Urgent surgical delivery during maternal or fetal emergencies\"},{\"name\":\"Postpartum Hemorrhage Management\",\"description\":\"Emergency bleeding control and stabilization\"},{\"name\":\"Critical Obstetric Surgery\",\"description\":\"Life-saving maternal surgical intervention\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Continue intensive maternal monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor newborn condition closely\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain fluid and blood replacement therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Follow infection prevention protocols\"},{\"value\":\"Attend long-term postnatal follow-up care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Maternal mortality\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal complications\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infection\"},{\"value\":\"Multi-organ failure\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed emergency intervention\"}]','<p>Strong emergency obstetric care infrastructure significantly reduces maternal and neonatal mortality and improves long-term pregnancy outcomes.</p>','<p>Emergency obstetric care infrastructure is one of the most critical components of modern maternal healthcare systems.</p>','Emergency Obstetric Care Infrastructure','Learn about emergency obstetric care systems and maternal emergency management.','emergency obstetric care, maternal emergency infrastructure, obstetric ICU',1,'2026-05-15 06:29:55','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(200,'Pediatric Outpatient Consultation','procedures/banners/6acc28ca-8d41-414e-ad54-c3dd6f6470b8.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/f99bbdf9-55a5-4c3b-bc8e-33ae4daa2813.webp','pediatric-outpatient-consultation','<p>Pediatric outpatient consultation is a specialized medical service designed to evaluate, diagnose, treat, and monitor the health conditions of infants, children, and adolescents without requiring hospital admission.</p>','<p>This service focuses on preventive healthcare, growth monitoring, developmental assessment, vaccination guidance, nutritional counseling, and treatment of childhood illnesses. Pediatric outpatient care plays a major role in maintaining healthy physical, emotional, and developmental growth during childhood. Pediatricians are specially trained to understand the unique medical needs of children and provide age-appropriate healthcare management.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Fever or recurrent infections\"},{\"value\":\"Poor growth or weight gain\"},{\"value\":\"Cough, cold, or breathing problems\"},{\"value\":\"Digestive complaints\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental or behavioral concerns\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Pediatric Outpatient Consultation is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Delayed diagnosis if follow-up is missed\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of untreated illness\"},{\"value\":\"Anxiety in children during examinations\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Missed vaccination schedules\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Growth and developmental assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Vaccination status evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Physical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Laboratory investigations when required\"}]','<p>During the consultation, the pediatrician evaluates the child’s symptoms, medical history, growth pattern, developmental milestones, nutritional status, and vaccination records.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Follow prescribed medications properly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular pediatric follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain vaccination schedules\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor symptoms carefully at home\"},{\"value\":\"Ensure balanced nutrition and hydration\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Delayed diagnosis if follow-up is missed\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of untreated illness\"},{\"value\":\"Anxiety in children during examinations\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Missed vaccination schedules\"}]','<p>Regular pediatric outpatient care significantly improves childhood health outcomes by promoting early diagnosis, disease prevention, and healthy development.</p>','<p>Pediatric outpatient consultation plays a vital role in ensuring healthy childhood growth, disease prevention, and early medical intervention.</p>','Pediatric Outpatient Consultation','Learn about pediatric outpatient consultation services for children’s healthcare and preventive care.','pediatric consultation, child healthcare, pediatric checkup',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(201,'Emergency Pediatric Care','procedures/banners/cef9636f-f065-4039-b5d6-2f9bcafc0ae6.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/e5a5b537-aac9-4a7b-a962-e8582cf71bb6.webp','emergency-pediatric-care','<p>Emergency pediatric care is a specialized medical service designed to provide immediate evaluation and treatment for critically ill or injured infants and children requiring urgent medical attention.</p>','<p>Children have unique emergency healthcare needs that differ from adults, and pediatric emergency services are specifically equipped to manage childhood emergencies safely and effectively.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty breathing\"},{\"value\":\"High fever with lethargy\"},{\"value\":\"Convulsions or seizures\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden loss of consciousness\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Emergency Pediatric Care is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Rapid progression of illness\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory failure\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration complications\"},{\"value\":\"Shock or organ dysfunction\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed emergency treatment\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Airway and breathing assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Vital sign monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Hydration assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency laboratory investigations\"}]','<p>The emergency pediatric unit is equipped with child-specific emergency equipment, oxygen systems, resuscitation devices, monitoring systems, emergency medications, and trained pediatric emergency specialists.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Emergency Resuscitation\",\"description\":\"Immediate stabilization of critically ill children\"},{\"name\":\"Airway Management\",\"description\":\"Emergency respiratory support\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Continue prescribed medications carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor vital signs and symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend emergency follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Seek immediate care if symptoms worsen\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Rapid progression of illness\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory failure\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration complications\"},{\"value\":\"Shock or organ dysfunction\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed emergency treatment\"}]','<p>Advanced pediatric emergency care significantly improves survival rates and reduces complications from childhood emergencies.</p>','<p>Emergency pediatric care is essential for rapid stabilization and life-saving treatment in critically ill children.</p>','Emergency Pediatric Care','Learn about emergency pediatric care services for critically ill and injured children.','emergency pediatric care, pediatric emergency treatment, child emergency services',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(202,'Fever Evaluation and Management','procedures/banners/b9ee6606-244b-48ca-a031-cfe875fbf4e1.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/5d177346-1bb2-4002-8695-016caaef5ff4.webp','fever-evaluation-and-management','<p>Fever evaluation and management is a pediatric medical service focused on identifying the underlying cause of elevated body temperature in children and providing appropriate treatment and monitoring.</p>','<p>Fever is one of the most common reasons for pediatric consultation and may occur due to infections, inflammatory conditions, immune responses, or other medical illnesses.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Elevated body temperature\"},{\"value\":\"Chills or sweating\"},{\"value\":\"Poor feeding or appetite loss\"},{\"value\":\"Irritability or lethargy\"},{\"value\":\"Body pain or weakness\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Clinical suspicion of disease based on history and examination\"},{\"value\":\"Abnormal blood reports or previous investigation findings\"},{\"value\":\"Need to differentiate between similar conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Assessment before starting medical or surgical treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up of previously diagnosed disease or treatment response\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Febrile seizures\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Underlying serious infection\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed diagnosis\"},{\"value\":\"High fever complications in infants\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Temperature monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Physical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Infection screening\"},{\"value\":\"Assessment for serious illness signs\"}]','<p>Management depends on the cause and severity of fever and may include fever-reducing medications, hydration therapy, antibiotic treatment, monitoring for complications, and supportive care.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor temperature regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate fluid intake\"},{\"value\":\"Give medications as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Ensure proper rest for the child\"},{\"value\":\"Seek medical review if symptoms worsen\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Febrile seizures\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Underlying serious infection\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed diagnosis\"},{\"value\":\"High fever complications in infants\"}]','<p>Most childhood fevers resolve completely with proper treatment and monitoring.</p>','<p>Proper fever evaluation and management are essential for identifying serious illnesses and ensuring safe pediatric recovery.</p>','Fever Evaluation and Management','Learn about pediatric fever evaluation, diagnosis, and fever management in children.','pediatric fever management, child fever treatment, fever evaluation',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(203,'Medical Management of Infections','procedures/banners/055206f5-320a-457b-a2d3-d352d6f04de0.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/d9207b98-74ef-4ae3-b400-419e2926b198.webp','medical-management-of-infections','<p>Medical management of infections in children involves diagnosing, treating, and monitoring bacterial, viral, fungal, or parasitic infections affecting various body systems.</p>','<p>Children are more vulnerable to infections because their immune systems are still developing.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Fever and chills\"},{\"value\":\"Cough or breathing problems\"},{\"value\":\"Vomiting or diarrhea\"},{\"value\":\"Skin rashes or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue and poor appetite\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Medical Management of Infections as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Spread of infection\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory complications\"},{\"value\":\"Sepsis or bloodstream infection\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed recovery if untreated\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Clinical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Laboratory investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Imaging studies\"},{\"value\":\"Infection screening\"},{\"value\":\"Hydration assessment\"}]','<p>Treatment may involve antibiotics, antiviral medications, antifungal drugs, fever management, hydration therapy, and nutritional support.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Complete full medication course\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain proper hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor symptoms carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Follow hygiene and infection control measures\"},{\"value\":\"Attend pediatric follow-up visits\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Spread of infection\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory complications\"},{\"value\":\"Sepsis or bloodstream infection\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed recovery if untreated\"}]','<p>Most childhood infections recover completely with timely treatment and supportive care.</p>','<p>Medical management of infections is essential for preventing serious pediatric complications and supporting healthy recovery.</p>','Medical Management of Infections','Learn about pediatric infection diagnosis, treatment, and medical management.','pediatric infections, infection treatment, child infection management',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(204,'Antibiotic Therapy','procedures/banners/8af12096-3c95-4bf1-8a9d-afc174649736.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/989c2a28-2c1c-4a55-a387-00a199d8c2b4.webp','antibiotic-therapy','<p>Antibiotic therapy is a medical treatment used to manage bacterial infections in children using medications that kill or inhibit the growth of bacteria.</p>','<p>Antibiotics play an important role in treating serious bacterial illnesses and preventing complications.</p>','[{\"value\":\"High fever\"},{\"value\":\"Bacterial throat infection\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cough with infection\"},{\"value\":\"Painful urination\"},{\"value\":\"Skin swelling or pus formation\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Antibiotic Therapy as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Culture sensitivity testing\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Urine testing\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical infection assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory infection evaluation\"}]','<p>Doctors select antibiotics based on clinical findings, laboratory reports, culture sensitivity tests, and suspected infection sources.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Complete the full antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Follow dosage instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up evaluations if needed\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]','<p>Proper antibiotic therapy effectively treats bacterial infections and prevents severe complications in children.</p>','<p>Antibiotic therapy is essential for managing bacterial infections and reducing complications.</p>','Antibiotic Therapy','Learn about antibiotic therapy and pediatric bacterial infection treatment.','antibiotic therapy, pediatric antibiotics, bacterial infection treatment',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:17',NULL),(205,'Nebulization Therapy','procedures/banners/a79fb88f-d370-4824-a2e4-180c4bfa7f8f.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/cbedf568-396c-4693-b9d5-11754b1c6b7a.webp','nebulization-therapy','<p>Nebulization therapy is a respiratory treatment that delivers medication directly into the lungs in the form of a fine mist to help children breathe more easily.</p>','<p>It is commonly used for asthma, wheezing, bronchitis, respiratory infections, and airway inflammation.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Wheezing\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cough\"},{\"value\":\"Chest tightness\"},{\"value\":\"Asthma attacks\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Nebulization Therapy as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary fast heartbeat\"},{\"value\":\"Mild tremors\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk from poorly cleaned equipment\"},{\"value\":\"Overuse complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Respiratory examination\"},{\"value\":\"Oxygen saturation monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Asthma assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Lung function evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Airway inflammation assessment\"}]','<p>The therapy uses a nebulizer machine connected to a mask or mouthpiece to deliver medication directly into the lungs.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Clean nebulizer equipment properly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow medication schedules carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor breathing symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular pediatric reviews\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary fast heartbeat\"},{\"value\":\"Mild tremors\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Infection risk from poorly cleaned equipment\"},{\"value\":\"Overuse complications\"}]','<p>Nebulization therapy provides rapid relief from respiratory symptoms and improves breathing comfort.</p>','<p>Nebulization therapy is an effective treatment for pediatric respiratory conditions.</p>','Nebulization Therapy','Learn about nebulization therapy for asthma and respiratory diseases in children.','nebulization therapy, asthma treatment, pediatric respiratory care',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(206,'Oxygen Therapy','procedures/banners/44c791c1-8cd1-4b2b-966d-50baf08fba14.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/17cbd9c9-a7d4-4b1a-a71d-7279d7ca85ee.webp','oxygen-therapy','<p>Oxygen therapy is a medical treatment used to increase oxygen levels in children experiencing breathing difficulties or reduced oxygen supply.</p>','<p>This therapy is critical in respiratory illnesses, severe infections, newborn complications, asthma attacks, and emergency pediatric conditions.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty breathing\"},{\"value\":\"Low oxygen saturation\"},{\"value\":\"Bluish lips or skin\"},{\"value\":\"Rapid breathing\"},{\"value\":\"Severe respiratory infection\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Oxygen Therapy as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Oxygen dependency in prolonged cases\"},{\"value\":\"Nasal dryness or irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Improper oxygen delivery complications\"},{\"value\":\"Lung damage from excessive oxygen\"},{\"value\":\"Fire safety hazards\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Pulse oximetry\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory examination\"},{\"value\":\"Blood oxygen evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Chest assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Critical care monitoring\"}]','<p>Oxygen is administered using nasal prongs, face masks, oxygen hoods, or ventilatory support systems depending on the child’s condition.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor oxygen levels regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain proper equipment hygiene\"},{\"value\":\"Follow respiratory treatment plans\"},{\"value\":\"Encourage adequate hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up respiratory evaluations\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Oxygen dependency in prolonged cases\"},{\"value\":\"Nasal dryness or irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Improper oxygen delivery complications\"},{\"value\":\"Lung damage from excessive oxygen\"},{\"value\":\"Fire safety hazards\"}]','<p>Timely oxygen therapy significantly improves survival and recovery in children with respiratory illness.</p>','<p>Oxygen therapy is critical for supporting breathing and organ function in pediatric respiratory emergencies.</p>','Oxygen Therapy','Learn about oxygen therapy for pediatric respiratory illnesses and emergencies.','oxygen therapy, pediatric respiratory support, oxygen treatment',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(207,'Asthma Management Program','procedures/banners/0f1ac2fa-bb8b-463b-8db0-ab832692e4c6.webp',NULL,'asthma-management-program','<p>An asthma management program is a comprehensive pediatric healthcare service designed to diagnose, monitor, treat, and prevent asthma attacks in children.</p>','<p>Asthma is a long-term respiratory condition that causes airway narrowing, breathing difficulty, wheezing, and coughing.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Wheezing\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent cough\"},{\"value\":\"Chest tightness\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Night-time breathing difficulty\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Asthma Management Program as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Severe asthma attacks\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory distress\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent hospital admissions\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced physical activity\"},{\"value\":\"Poorly controlled chronic symptoms\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Respiratory evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Allergy assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Lung function monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Trigger identification\"},{\"value\":\"Breathing assessment\"}]','<p>Treatment may involve inhalers, nebulization therapy, steroid medications, allergy management, and trigger avoidance strategies.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Use inhalers correctly and regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid asthma triggers\"},{\"value\":\"Attend routine asthma follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor breathing symptoms daily\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain emergency asthma action plans\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Severe asthma attacks\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory distress\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent hospital admissions\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced physical activity\"},{\"value\":\"Poorly controlled chronic symptoms\"}]','<p>Proper asthma management allows most children to lead healthy and active lives with minimal symptoms.</p>','<p>Asthma management programs improve respiratory health and reduce emergency complications in children.</p>','Asthma Management Program','Learn about pediatric asthma management, treatment, and prevention strategies.','asthma management, pediatric asthma care, respiratory treatment',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:18','Best Asthma Management Program in bangalore'),(209,'Tonsillitis and ENT Infection Management','procedures/banners/518b70a6-00de-448f-9434-ad69c9f4930f.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/8d958633-a83d-4ab5-a910-32e965caac69.webp','tonsillitis-and-ent-infection-management','<p>Tonsillitis and ENT infection management is a pediatric healthcare service focused on diagnosing and treating infections affecting the tonsils, throat, ears, nose, and upper respiratory tract.</p>','<p>These infections are extremely common in childhood and may be caused by bacteria, viruses, or allergies.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Sore throat\"},{\"value\":\"Fever and difficulty swallowing\"},{\"value\":\"Ear pain\"},{\"value\":\"Nasal congestion\"},{\"value\":\"Enlarged tonsils or lymph nodes\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Tonsillitis and ENT Infection Management as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Recurrent infections\"},{\"value\":\"Breathing difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Ear hearing problems\"},{\"value\":\"Abscess formation\"},{\"value\":\"Spread of untreated infection\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Throat examination\"},{\"value\":\"Fever assessment\"},{\"value\":\"ENT evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Laboratory testing\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory assessment\"}]','<p>Treatment may involve antibiotics, fever medications, hydration therapy, nebulization, and supportive care.</p>','[{\"name\":\"Tonsillectomy\",\"description\":\"Surgical removal of tonsils in recurrent severe cases\"},{\"name\":\"Adenoidectomy\",\"description\":\"Removal of enlarged adenoids affecting breathing\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Complete prescribed medications fully\"},{\"value\":\"Encourage warm fluids and hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain proper oral hygiene\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor fever and breathing symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Attend ENT follow-up visits if needed\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Recurrent infections\"},{\"value\":\"Breathing difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Ear hearing problems\"},{\"value\":\"Abscess formation\"},{\"value\":\"Spread of untreated infection\"}]','<p>Most childhood ENT infections recover completely with timely treatment and supportive care.</p>','<p>Proper ENT infection management helps reduce complications and improve respiratory and throat health in children.</p>','Tonsillitis and ENT Infection Management','Learn about tonsillitis and ENT infection treatment in children.','tonsillitis treatment, ENT infections, pediatric ENT care',1,'2026-05-15 10:29:51','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(210,'Diarrhea Management and ORS Therapy','procedures/banners/e3d45afc-e2ee-4ade-9d51-3e869e19e5a2.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/67d93d97-e317-4394-b621-1f19068c178a.webp','diarrhea-management-and-ors-therapy','<p>Diarrhea management and ORS (Oral Rehydration Solution) therapy is an essential pediatric treatment service focused on preventing dehydration and restoring fluid balance in children suffering from loose stools and gastrointestinal infections.</p>','<p>Diarrhea is one of the most common childhood illnesses and can become dangerous if excessive fluid and electrolyte loss is not corrected promptly. ORS therapy is considered one of the most effective and life-saving treatments for childhood dehydration.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Frequent loose stools\"},{\"value\":\"Vomiting and dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Excessive thirst\"},{\"value\":\"Weakness or irritability\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced urine output\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Diarrhea Management and ORS Therapy as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance\"},{\"value\":\"Malnutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Shock in severe cases\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed growth if recurrent\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Hydration assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Stool examination\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Physical examination\"}]','<p>The treatment approach focuses on replacing lost fluids, maintaining electrolyte balance, preventing complications, and identifying the underlying cause of diarrhea. Treatment may include ORS therapy, zinc supplementation, nutritional management, IV fluids in severe dehydration, and antibiotics only when indicated.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Continue ORS therapy as advised\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate nutrition and breastfeeding\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor urine output and hydration status\"},{\"value\":\"Follow strict hygiene practices\"},{\"value\":\"Seek medical review if symptoms worsen\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance\"},{\"value\":\"Malnutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Shock in severe cases\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed growth if recurrent\"}]','<p>Most children recover completely with timely diarrhea management and proper hydration therapy. ORS has significantly reduced childhood deaths related to dehydration worldwide.</p>','<p>Diarrhea management and ORS therapy are essential for preventing dehydration and improving pediatric recovery outcomes.</p>','Diarrhea Management and ORS Therapy','Learn about pediatric diarrhea management and ORS therapy for dehydration prevention.','ORS therapy, diarrhea management, pediatric dehydration treatment',1,'2026-05-15 10:31:58','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(211,'IV Fluid Management','procedures/banners/6b5c353d-70ae-4f2c-bb39-7155c4cea9fb.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/f25faff0-0725-4650-81b8-2c39b45a3804.webp','iv-fluid-management','<p>IV (Intravenous) fluid management is a pediatric medical treatment used to restore fluids, electrolytes, and circulation in children who cannot maintain adequate hydration orally.</p>','<p>This therapy is commonly used in severe dehydration, infections, vomiting, diarrhea, shock, surgical recovery, and critically ill children requiring rapid fluid replacement.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent vomiting\"},{\"value\":\"Inability to drink fluids\"},{\"value\":\"Shock or low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infection or illness\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for IV Fluid Management as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Fluid overload\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance\"},{\"value\":\"IV site infection\"},{\"value\":\"Vein irritation or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect fluid administration complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Fluid balance monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte testing\"},{\"value\":\"Vital sign assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Urine output monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"}]','<p>The treatment involves administering sterile fluids directly into a vein using pediatric IV access systems and infusion pumps. Doctors calculate fluid requirements based on age, weight, dehydration severity, underlying illness, and electrolyte status.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor IV site regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain fluid balance monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Encourage oral intake when possible\"},{\"value\":\"Follow pediatric fluid instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up evaluations if advised\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Fluid overload\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance\"},{\"value\":\"IV site infection\"},{\"value\":\"Vein irritation or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect fluid administration complications\"}]','<p>Proper IV fluid management significantly improves recovery and survival in critically ill or dehydrated children.</p>','<p>IV fluid management is critical for restoring hydration and circulation in pediatric emergencies and severe illnesses.</p>','IV Fluid Management','Learn about pediatric IV fluid management and hydration therapy.','IV fluid therapy, pediatric hydration, intravenous fluid management',1,'2026-05-15 10:31:58','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(212,'Nutrition Assessment and Counseling',NULL,NULL,'nutrition-assessment-and-counseling','Nutrition assessment and counseling is a pediatric healthcare service focused on evaluating a child’s nutritional status, dietary intake, growth pattern, and feeding practices to promote healthy development.','Proper nutrition during childhood is essential for brain development, immunity, physical growth, learning ability, and disease prevention.','[{\"value\":\"Poor weight gain\"},{\"value\":\"Loss of appetite\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional deficiencies\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity or undernutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding difficulties\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Clinical suspicion of disease based on history and examination\"},{\"value\":\"Abnormal blood reports or previous investigation findings\"},{\"value\":\"Need to differentiate between similar conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Assessment before starting medical or surgical treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up of previously diagnosed disease or treatment response\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Malnutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed growth and development\"},{\"value\":\"Weak immunity\"},{\"value\":\"Learning difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic health problems\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Growth measurements\"},{\"value\":\"Dietary history evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding behavior analysis\"},{\"value\":\"Laboratory investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional risk assessment\"}]','Counseling may focus on balanced diet planning, breastfeeding guidance, complementary feeding advice, vitamin and mineral supplementation, weight management, and nutritional support during illness.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Nutritional assessment begins during consultation\"},{\"value\":\"Diet modifications improve nutritional status\"},{\"value\":\"Growth monitoring supports recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Supplements may be continued long-term\"},{\"value\":\"Healthy eating habits improve long-term outcomes\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Follow recommended diet plans carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor growth regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Encourage healthy eating habits\"},{\"value\":\"Continue nutritional supplements if prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up nutrition evaluations\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Malnutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed growth and development\"},{\"value\":\"Weak immunity\"},{\"value\":\"Learning difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic health problems\"}]','Proper nutrition assessment and counseling greatly improve physical growth, immunity, brain development, and overall child health.','Nutrition assessment and counseling are essential for supporting healthy pediatric growth and long-term development.','Nutrition Assessment and Counseling','Learn about pediatric nutrition assessment and dietary counseling services.','nutrition counseling, pediatric nutrition, child growth assessment',1,'2026-05-15 10:31:58','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(213,'Growth Monitoring','procedures/banners/a68825ad-eda9-4a04-8dda-6a66723fb247.webp','procedures/banners/relatedimages/d8c441c0-b1d0-45ee-a72f-cdba6c2b3ea2.webp','growth-monitoring','<p>Growth monitoring is a pediatric healthcare service used to regularly assess a child’s physical growth and development through measurements of weight, height, head circumference, and body proportions.</p>','<p>Monitoring growth helps identify nutritional problems, chronic illnesses, hormonal disorders, and developmental concerns at an early stage.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Poor weight gain\"},{\"value\":\"Short stature concerns\"},{\"value\":\"Excessive weight gain\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed physical development\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding or nutritional problems\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Growth Monitoring is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Missed developmental disorders\"},{\"value\":\"Malnutrition complications\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity-related health problems\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal disorder progression\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed medical intervention\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Weight measurement\"},{\"value\":\"Height assessment\"},{\"value\":\"BMI evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Growth chart analysis\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental milestone assessment\"}]','<p>The process includes periodic measurement and plotting of growth parameters on standardized growth charts appropriate for age and gender.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain balanced nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular pediatric growth evaluations\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor feeding and activity patterns\"},{\"value\":\"Follow specialist recommendations carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Keep vaccination schedules updated\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Missed developmental disorders\"},{\"value\":\"Malnutrition complications\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity-related health problems\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal disorder progression\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed medical intervention\"}]','<p>Regular growth monitoring significantly improves early diagnosis of childhood health problems and supports healthy development.</p>','<p>Growth monitoring is a vital preventive pediatric healthcare service for healthy child development.</p>','Growth Monitoring','Learn about pediatric growth monitoring and child development assessment.','growth monitoring, child development, pediatric growth assessment',1,'2026-05-15 10:31:58','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(215,'Preterm Baby Care',NULL,NULL,'preterm-baby-care','Preterm baby care is a specialized neonatal healthcare service focused on the treatment, monitoring, and developmental support of babies born before 37 weeks of pregnancy.','Premature babies often have underdeveloped organs and may face challenges related to breathing, feeding, temperature control, immunity, and growth.','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty breathing after birth\"},{\"value\":\"Low birth weight\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding problems\"},{\"value\":\"Poor temperature control\"},{\"value\":\"Weak muscle tone\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Preterm Baby Care is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Respiratory complications\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal infections\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental delays\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding intolerance\"},{\"value\":\"Vision or hearing problems\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Neonatal monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Weight and growth monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Temperature monitoring\"}]','The care program includes neonatal monitoring, incubator support, respiratory assistance, feeding management, infection prevention, temperature regulation, and developmental assessment.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Initial stabilization begins immediately after birth\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory and feeding support continue during NICU care\"},{\"value\":\"Growth and weight gain improve gradually\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental monitoring continues during infancy\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term follow-up supports healthy neurological development\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain regular neonatal follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor feeding and weight gain carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Prevent infection exposure\"},{\"value\":\"Continue vaccination schedules\"},{\"value\":\"Support developmental stimulation activities\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Respiratory complications\"},{\"value\":\"Neonatal infections\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental delays\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding intolerance\"},{\"value\":\"Vision or hearing problems\"}]','Modern neonatal medicine has significantly improved survival rates and long-term outcomes for premature babies.','Preterm baby care is essential for improving survival, growth, and neurological development in premature newborns.','Preterm Baby Care','Learn about specialized preterm baby care and neonatal developmental support.','preterm baby care, premature baby treatment, neonatal care',1,'2026-05-15 10:33:29','2026-07-29 00:28:18',NULL),(216,'NICU Support',NULL,NULL,'nicu-support','NICU (Neonatal Intensive Care Unit) support is an advanced neonatal healthcare service designed for critically ill newborns, premature babies, and infants requiring intensive monitoring and life-support treatment.','NICU care provides specialized medical management for newborns with severe respiratory, cardiac, neurological, infectious, or metabolic complications.','[{\"value\":\"Severe breathing difficulty\"},{\"value\":\"Prematurity-related complications\"},{\"value\":\"Low oxygen levels\"},{\"value\":\"Feeding inability\"},{\"value\":\"Critical neonatal illness\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for NICU Support as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Severe infections\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term developmental complications\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory dependency\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological injury\"},{\"value\":\"Extended hospitalization\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Vital sign monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Metabolic evaluations\"}]','The NICU is equipped with incubators, ventilators, oxygen systems, infusion pumps, phototherapy units, neonatal monitors, and emergency resuscitation equipment.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Critical care begins immediately after NICU admission\"},{\"value\":\"Continuous monitoring supports stabilization\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory and nutritional support continue during recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental monitoring improves long-term outcomes\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up rehabilitation supports healthy growth\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Attend regular NICU follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor developmental milestones carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Continue feeding and nutritional support\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain infection prevention measures\"},{\"value\":\"Follow specialist rehabilitation advice\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Severe infections\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term developmental complications\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory dependency\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological injury\"},{\"value\":\"Extended hospitalization\"}]','NICU support has dramatically improved newborn survival and long-term developmental outcomes.','