cs consultation improves access to pediatric healthcare and follow-up support.','Tele-Pediatrics Consultation','Learn about tele-pediatrics consultation and remote child healthcare services.','tele pediatrics, online pediatric consultation, remote child healthcare',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:52','2026-07-29 00:28:20',NULL),(236,'Follow-Up and Long-Term Pediatric Care',NULL,NULL,'follow-up-and-long-term-pediatric-care','Follow-up and long-term pediatric care is a continuous healthcare service focused on monitoring a child’s recovery, growth, development, chronic illnesses, and overall well-being.','Long-term pediatric monitoring is essential for children recovering from serious illnesses, developmental disorders, surgeries, chronic diseases, or neurological conditions.','[{\"value\":\"Chronic medical conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental concerns\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term medication needs\"},{\"value\":\"Recurring health problems\"},{\"value\":\"Ongoing rehabilitation requirements\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Follow-Up and Long-Term Pediatric Care is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease recurrence or progression\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental delays\"},{\"value\":\"Poor treatment compliance\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional or social difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term physical complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Growth and developmental monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Medication review\"},{\"value\":\"Behavioral assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist follow-up evaluations\"}]','Long-term pediatric care may include rehabilitation support, medication management, developmental monitoring, nutritional assessment, vaccination follow-up, and specialist referrals.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Regular follow-up visits monitor long-term recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental evaluations identify complications early\"},{\"value\":\"Medication and therapy plans are adjusted as needed\"},{\"value\":\"Rehabilitation improves physical and emotional health\"},{\"value\":\"Continuous pediatric care supports healthier futures\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Attend all scheduled follow-up appointments\"},{\"value\":\"Continue medications and therapies regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor growth and developmental milestones\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain healthy nutrition and lifestyle habits\"},{\"value\":\"Communicate new symptoms promptly to healthcare providers\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease recurrence or progression\"},{\"value\":\"Developmental delays\"},{\"value\":\"Poor treatment compliance\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional or social difficulties\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term physical complications\"}]','Comprehensive long-term pediatric care greatly improves disease management, developmental outcomes, and quality of life in children with ongoing medical needs.','Long-term pediatric follow-up care supports healthier development and improved chronic disease management.','Follow-Up and Long-Term Pediatric Care','Learn about follow-up and long-term pediatric healthcare services.','long term pediatric care, child follow-up care, chronic pediatric management',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:52','2026-07-29 00:28:20',NULL),(237,'Infection Prevention and Control','procedures/banners/dae6cc66-b4e2-4b81-a536-dcfa5460913d.webp',NULL,'infection-prevention-and-control','<p>Infection prevention and control is a pediatric healthcare service focused on reducing the spread of infectious diseases within hospitals, clinics, schools, and community settings.</p>','<p>Children are especially vulnerable to infections because their immune systems are still developing and they are frequently exposed to contagious illnesses through close social interaction.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Fever and chills\"},{\"value\":\"Cough or breathing difficulty\"},{\"value\":\"Vomiting or diarrhea\"},{\"value\":\"Skin rashes or infections\"},{\"value\":\"General weakness or irritability\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Infection Prevention and Control is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hospital-acquired infections\"},{\"value\":\"Spread of contagious diseases\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infections in high-risk children\"},{\"value\":\"Antibiotic-resistant infections\"},{\"value\":\"Increased hospitalization rates\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Infection monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Vaccination assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Hygiene evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Environmental safety monitoring\"}]','<p>This service includes hygiene protocols, vaccination support, sterilization practices, isolation precautions, and education for healthcare workers and families.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Maintain proper hand hygiene practices\"},{\"value\":\"Follow vaccination schedules regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Clean frequently touched surfaces properly\"},{\"value\":\"Use protective equipment when advised\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor children for early infection symptoms\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hospital-acquired infections\"},{\"value\":\"Spread of contagious diseases\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infections in high-risk children\"},{\"value\":\"Antibiotic-resistant infections\"},{\"value\":\"Increased hospitalization rates\"}]','<p>Strong infection prevention programs significantly reduce pediatric illness, hospitalization, and healthcare-associated infections.</p>','<p>Infection prevention and control services are essential for protecting children and improving healthcare safety.</p>','Infection Prevention and Control','Learn about pediatric infection prevention and hospital infection control services.','infection prevention, pediatric infection control, hospital hygiene',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:58','2026-07-29 00:28:20',NULL),(238,'Isolation Care When Required',NULL,NULL,'isolation-care-when-required','Isolation care is a specialized infection-control service used to protect children, healthcare workers, and visitors from contagious diseases.','Children with serious infectious diseases may require temporary separation and special precautions to prevent transmission within hospitals or healthcare facilities.','[{\"value\":\"Highly contagious infection\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent fever\"},{\"value\":\"Severe respiratory symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Infectious skin lesions\"},{\"value\":\"Confirmed communicable disease\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Isolation Care When Required is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Spread of infection to others\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional stress during isolation\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced social interaction\"},{\"value\":\"Hospital-acquired infections\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed recovery in severe illness\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Infection screening\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Laboratory investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Isolation risk assessment\"}]','Isolation care includes dedicated isolation rooms, protective equipment, hygiene protocols, controlled visitor access, and specialized nursing care.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Isolation precautions begin immediately\"},{\"value\":\"Continuous monitoring supports recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Strict infection-control measures reduce transmission\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up evaluations monitor health improvement\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term recovery improves with controlled infection management\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Follow all isolation instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain proper hygiene and sanitation\"},{\"value\":\"Use protective equipment correctly\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor symptoms regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up medical evaluations\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Spread of infection to others\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional stress during isolation\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced social interaction\"},{\"value\":\"Hospital-acquired infections\"},{\"value\":\"Delayed recovery in severe illness\"}]','Proper isolation care effectively reduces infection transmission and protects vulnerable patients.','Isolation care plays a major role in preventing the spread of contagious pediatric illnesses.','Isolation Care When Required','Learn about pediatric isolation care and infection-control services.','isolation care, infection control, contagious disease management',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:58','2026-07-29 00:28:20',NULL),(239,'Pediatric Day-Care Procedures',NULL,NULL,'pediatric-day-care-procedures','Pediatric day-care procedures are minor medical or diagnostic treatments performed in children without requiring overnight hospitalization.','These services allow children to receive necessary medical care safely while minimizing hospital stay, emotional stress, and disruption to family routines.','[{\"value\":\"Conditions requiring short medical procedures\"},{\"value\":\"Mild infections needing IV treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Minor injuries\"},{\"value\":\"Diagnostic evaluation needs\"},{\"value\":\"Short-duration therapeutic procedures\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Pediatric Day-Care Procedures is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Mild medication reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Procedure-related anxiety\"},{\"value\":\"Minor bleeding or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Rare procedural complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Pre-procedure evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Vital sign monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Diagnostic screening\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical examination\"},{\"value\":\"Procedure safety assessment\"}]','Common pediatric day-care procedures may include nebulization therapy, wound care, IV medication administration, diagnostic procedures, vaccinations, and minor surgeries.','[{\"name\":\"Minor Surgical Procedures\",\"description\":\"Short-duration pediatric surgical interventions\"},{\"name\":\"Diagnostic Procedures\",\"description\":\"Short pediatric diagnostic evaluations\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Pre-procedure evaluation begins during admission\"},{\"value\":\"Children are monitored during the procedure\"},{\"value\":\"Recovery observation continues after treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Discharge usually occurs on the same day\"},{\"value\":\"Follow-up visits ensure complete recovery\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Follow discharge instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Ensure adequate rest and hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for fever or complications\"},{\"value\":\"Give medications as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up appointments if advised\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Mild medication reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Procedure-related anxiety\"},{\"value\":\"Minor bleeding or swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Rare procedural complications\"}]','Pediatric day-care services provide safe, efficient, and less stressful treatment for many childhood conditions.','Pediatric day-care procedures improve treatment convenience and recovery comfort for children.','Pediatric Day-Care Procedures','Learn about pediatric day-care medical and diagnostic procedures.','pediatric day care, minor pediatric procedures, outpatient child treatment',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:58','2026-07-29 00:28:20',NULL),(240,'Pediatric Emergency Stabilization',NULL,NULL,'pediatric-emergency-stabilization','Pediatric emergency stabilization is a critical emergency healthcare service focused on rapidly assessing and stabilizing children with life-threatening illnesses or injuries.','Children may deteriorate quickly during emergencies, making immediate medical intervention essential to preserve breathing, circulation, brain function, and overall survival.','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty breathing\"},{\"value\":\"Loss of consciousness\"},{\"value\":\"Severe dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent seizures\"},{\"value\":\"Trauma or severe injury\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Pediatric Emergency Stabilization is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Organ failure\"},{\"value\":\"Brain injury\"},{\"value\":\"Cardiac arrest\"},{\"value\":\"Shock and circulatory collapse\"},{\"value\":\"Life-threatening complications\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Vital sign monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Airway assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological examination\"},{\"value\":\"Cardiac monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Emergency laboratory investigations\"}]','Emergency stabilization includes airway management, oxygen support, IV fluid resuscitation, seizure control, trauma management, cardiac monitoring, and emergency medication administration.','[{\"name\":\"Emergency Resuscitation\",\"description\":\"Life-saving stabilization procedures\"},{\"name\":\"Trauma Stabilization\",\"description\":\"Emergency care for severe injuries\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Emergency assessment begins immediately\"},{\"value\":\"Stabilization procedures support survival\"},{\"value\":\"Continuous monitoring tracks recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Advanced treatment follows stabilization\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term rehabilitation may be required\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Continue close medical monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Attend emergency follow-up reviews\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and medications\"},{\"value\":\"Watch for recurrence of symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Follow rehabilitation recommendations if needed\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Organ failure\"},{\"value\":\"Brain injury\"},{\"value\":\"Cardiac arrest\"},{\"value\":\"Shock and circulatory collapse\"},{\"value\":\"Life-threatening complications\"}]','Rapid pediatric emergency stabilization greatly improves survival and reduces serious complications.','Pediatric emergency stabilization is essential for life-saving care in critically ill children.','Pediatric Emergency Stabilization','Learn about pediatric emergency stabilization and critical care services.','emergency stabilization, pediatric emergency care, critical child treatment',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:58','2026-07-29 00:28:20',NULL),(241,'Pediatric Intensive Care Support',NULL,NULL,'pediatric-intensive-care-support','Pediatric intensive care support is a highly specialized medical service designed for critically ill children requiring advanced monitoring, life-support systems, and intensive treatment.','The Pediatric Intensive Care Unit (PICU) manages severe illnesses, injuries, and complex medical conditions requiring continuous observation.','[{\"value\":\"Severe breathing difficulty\"},{\"value\":\"Critical infection or sepsis\"},{\"value\":\"Shock or low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Organ dysfunction\"},{\"value\":\"Altered consciousness\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Pediatric Intensive Care Support as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Organ failure\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infections\"},{\"value\":\"Long ICU stays\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological complications\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional stress for families\"}]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Continuous cardiac monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Organ function evaluation\"}]','PICU support includes mechanical ventilation, oxygen therapy, IV medications, emergency resuscitation, neurological monitoring, and organ support systems.','[]','[{\"value\":\"Critical care begins immediately after PICU admission\"},{\"value\":\"Continuous monitoring supports stabilization\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory and organ support continue during recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Rehabilitation improves functional recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term monitoring supports developmental health\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Attend regular follow-up appointments\"},{\"value\":\"Continue rehabilitation therapies if needed\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor developmental recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain nutritional support\"},{\"value\":\"Follow specialist recommendations carefully\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Organ failure\"},{\"value\":\"Severe infections\"},{\"value\":\"Long ICU stays\"},{\"value\":\"Neurological complications\"},{\"value\":\"Emotional stress for families\"}]','Advances in pediatric intensive care medicine have greatly improved survival rates and recovery outcomes.','Pediatric intensive care support is essential for managing life-threatening childhood illnesses.','Pediatric Intensive Care Support','Learn about PICU support and pediatric intensive care services.','PICU care, pediatric intensive care, critical pediatric treatment',1,'2026-05-15 11:50:58','2026-07-29 00:28:21',NULL),(242,'Lifestyle Modification (Diet, Exercise, Smoking Cessation)','procedures/banners/d4cd57e6-ccaf-46d9-a670-a82241838ad5.webp',NULL,'lifestyle-modification-diet-exercise-smoking-cessation','Lifestyle modification is a fundamental part of cardiology care that focuses on improving heart health through healthy daily habits, dietary changes, regular physical activity, weight management, and avoidance of harmful substances such as tobacco and excessive alcohol. These changes help reduce the risk of heart disease, stroke, hypertension, diabetes, and other cardiovascular complications. Lifestyle improvement is often recommended alongside medications and medical procedures for better long-term heart health.','Lifestyle modification programs are designed to improve cardiovascular function and reduce risk factors associated with heart disease. Key components include: Heart-healthy diet Regular physical activity Smoking cessation Weight management Stress reduction Adequate sleep and hydration Patients are guided by cardiologists, dietitians, physiotherapists, and counselors to adopt sustainable habits. Lifestyle management is beneficial in: Hypertension Coronary artery disease Heart failure High cholesterol Obesity Diabetes-related heart disease Consistent lifestyle changes can significantly reduce hospitalizations and improve quality of life.','[{\"value\":\"High blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity or weight gain\"},{\"value\":\"Chest discomfort during exertion\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue and poor stamina\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated cholesterol or blood sugar levels\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Lifestyle Modification (Diet, Exercise, Smoking Cessation) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty maintaining long-term lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary muscle soreness after exercise initiation\"},{\"value\":\"Withdrawal symptoms during smoking cessation\"},{\"value\":\"Stress related to dietary restrictions\"},{\"value\":\"Poor compliance affecting treatment outcomes\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Lifestyle Modification (Diet, Exercise, Smoking Cessation) is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Lifestyle modification programs are designed to improve cardiovascular function and reduce risk factors associated with heart disease. Key components include: Heart-healthy diet Regular physical activity Smoking cessatio...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Follow a balanced low-salt and low-fat diet\"},{\"value\":\"Exercise regularly as medically advised\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid smoking and tobacco products completely\"},{\"value\":\"Attend routine cardiac follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor blood pressure, sugar, and cholesterol regularly\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty maintaining long-term lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary muscle soreness after exercise initiation\"},{\"value\":\"Withdrawal symptoms during smoking cessation\"},{\"value\":\"Stress related to dietary restrictions\"},{\"value\":\"Poor compliance affecting treatment outcomes\"}]','Long-term lifestyle modification greatly improves cardiovascular health, reduces heart disease progression, lowers the risk of heart attack and stroke, and enhances overall longevity and quality of life.','','Lifestyle Modification (Diet, Exercise, Smoking Cessation)','Lifestyle modification is a fundamental part of cardiology care that focuses on improving heart health through healthy daily habits, dietary changes, regular physical activity, weight management, and avoidance of harmful substances such as tobacco and excessive alcohol. These changes help reduce the risk of heart disease, stroke, hypertension, diabetes, and other cardiovascular complications. Lifestyle improvement is often recommended alongside medications and medical procedures for better long-term heart health.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:21',NULL),(243,'Antiplatelet Therapy (Aspirin, P2Y12 Inhibitors)','procedures/banners/53c90152-3ef3-4bed-b131-03d5966904ba.webp',NULL,'antiplatelet-therapy-aspirin-p2y12-inhibitors','Antiplatelet therapy involves medications that reduce platelet aggregation and prevent blood clot formation within arteries. These medications are commonly used to prevent heart attacks, strokes, and complications after coronary interventions such as angioplasty and stenting. Antiplatelet agents are essential in the treatment and prevention of cardiovascular disease.','Common antiplatelet medications include: Aspirin Clopidogrel Ticagrelor Prasugrel These medicines help prevent clot formation in narrowed or stented coronary arteries. They are used in: Coronary artery disease Acute coronary syndrome Post-angioplasty care Stroke prevention Peripheral arterial disease Treatment duration varies depending on the patient’s cardiac condition and procedural history.','[{\"value\":\"Chest pain or angina\"},{\"value\":\"Previous heart attack history\"},{\"value\":\"Coronary artery blockage\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke or transient ischemic attack history\"},{\"value\":\"Post-stent placement management\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Antiplatelet Therapy (Aspirin, P2Y12 Inhibitors) as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Increased bleeding tendency\"},{\"value\":\"Gastric irritation or ulcers\"},{\"value\":\"Bruising easily\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of bleeding during surgery or trauma\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Antiplatelet Therapy (Aspirin, P2Y12 Inhibitors) is planned as a structured care pathway to relieve symptoms, improve function, and support long-term recovery. Treatment is personalised after clinical assessment and may be combined with medicines, lifestyle guidance, and follow-up reviews.</p><p>Common antiplatelet medications include: Aspirin Clopidogrel Ticagrelor Prasugrel These medicines help prevent clot formation in narrowed or stented coronary arteries. They are used in: Coronary artery disease Acute coro...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Do not stop therapy without medical advice\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for unusual bleeding or bruising\"},{\"value\":\"Inform doctors before any surgical procedures\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular cardiology follow-up appointments\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Increased bleeding tendency\"},{\"value\":\"Gastric irritation or ulcers\"},{\"value\":\"Bruising easily\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of bleeding during surgery or trauma\"}]','Antiplatelet therapy significantly reduces the risk of heart attack, stroke, and stent blockage, improving long-term cardiovascular survival and stability.','','Antiplatelet Therapy (Aspirin, P2Y12 Inhibitors)','Antiplatelet therapy involves medications that reduce platelet aggregation and prevent blood clot formation within arteries. These medications are commonly used to prevent heart attacks, strokes, and complications after coronary interventions such as angioplasty and stenting. Antiplatelet agents are essential in the treatment and prevention of cardiovascular disease.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:22',NULL),(244,'Anticoagulation (Warfarin, NOACs)','procedures/banners/78003615-3280-4cf8-bf16-65b17249ba1b.webp',NULL,'anticoagulation-warfarin-noacs','Anticoagulation therapy involves medications that reduce blood clot formation by interfering with the body’s clotting mechanisms. These medicines help prevent stroke, deep vein thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, and clot-related complications in heart conditions. Anticoagulation is especially important in patients with atrial fibrillation and artificial heart valves.','Common anticoagulants include: Warfarin Apixaban Rivaroxaban Dabigatran Edoxaban These medications are used for: Atrial fibrillation Venous thromboembolism Mechanical heart valves Pulmonary embolism Stroke prevention Regular monitoring may be required depending on the medication type. Treatment plans are individualized according to bleeding risk and cardiovascular condition.','[{\"value\":\"Irregular heartbeat\"},{\"value\":\"Previous stroke or clot history\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling or pain in the legs\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath from pulmonary embolism\"},{\"value\":\"Heart valve replacement history\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Anticoagulation (Warfarin, NOACs) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Increased bleeding risk\"},{\"value\":\"Nosebleeds or gum bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Internal bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Drug and food interactions\"},{\"value\":\"Need for frequent blood monitoring with warfarin\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Anticoagulation (Warfarin, NOACs) is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Common anticoagulants include: Warfarin Apixaban Rivaroxaban Dabigatran Edoxaban These medications are used for: Atrial fibrillation Venous thromboembolism Mechanical heart valves Pulmonary embolism Stroke prevention Reg...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take anticoagulants consistently at the same time daily\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular blood monitoring if advised\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid high-risk activities causing injury\"},{\"value\":\"Inform healthcare providers before procedures\"},{\"value\":\"Report bleeding or black stools immediately\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Increased bleeding risk\"},{\"value\":\"Nosebleeds or gum bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Internal bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Drug and food interactions\"},{\"value\":\"Need for frequent blood monitoring with warfarin\"}]','Proper anticoagulation therapy greatly reduces clot-related complications and improves long-term survival in patients with cardiovascular and thromboembolic disorders.','','Anticoagulation (Warfarin, NOACs)','Anticoagulation therapy involves medications that reduce blood clot formation by interfering with the body’s clotting mechanisms. These medicines help prevent stroke, deep vein thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, and clot-related complications in heart conditions. Anticoagulation is especially important in patients with atrial fibrillation and artificial heart valves.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(245,'Statin Therapy / Lipid-Lowering Agents','procedures/banners/32284219-2bbb-485b-b639-06d4bfab64b5.webp',NULL,'statin-therapy-lipid-lowering-agents','Statin therapy and lipid-lowering medications are treatments used to reduce cholesterol levels and decrease the risk of cardiovascular disease. These medications help stabilize arterial plaques and reduce the risk of heart attack and stroke. They form a major component of preventive cardiology care.','Common lipid-lowering medications include: Atorvastatin Rosuvastatin Simvastatin Ezetimibe PCSK9 inhibitors The therapy helps: Lower LDL cholesterol Reduce arterial inflammation Prevent plaque progression Improve vascular health Treatment is commonly recommended in: Coronary artery disease Diabetes High cholesterol Stroke prevention Familial hyperlipidemia Lifestyle modification is usually combined with medication therapy.','[{\"value\":\"High cholesterol levels\"},{\"value\":\"Previous heart attack or stroke\"},{\"value\":\"Coronary artery disease\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity or diabetes-related risk factors\"},{\"value\":\"Family history of cardiovascular disease\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Underlying illness or injury requiring ongoing supportive care\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete recovery after acute disease or surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic symptoms needing structured rehabilitation or therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Lifestyle, occupational, or medical factors contributing to persistence\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist recommendation for Statin Therapy \\/ Lipid-Lowering Agents as part of comprehensive care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Muscle pain or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Mild liver enzyme elevation\"},{\"value\":\"Digestive discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Rare severe muscle injury\"},{\"value\":\"Medication interactions\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Statin Therapy / Lipid-Lowering Agents is planned as a structured care pathway to relieve symptoms, improve function, and support long-term recovery. Treatment is personalised after clinical assessment and may be combined with medicines, lifestyle guidance, and follow-up reviews.</p><p>Common lipid-lowering medications include: Atorvastatin Rosuvastatin Simvastatin Ezetimibe PCSK9 inhibitors The therapy helps: Lower LDL cholesterol Reduce arterial inflammation Prevent plaque progression Improve vascula...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take cholesterol medications regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow a heart-healthy diet consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Exercise regularly as advised\"},{\"value\":\"Attend routine lipid profile monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Report persistent muscle pain promptly\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Muscle pain or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Mild liver enzyme elevation\"},{\"value\":\"Digestive discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Rare severe muscle injury\"},{\"value\":\"Medication interactions\"}]','Lipid-lowering therapy significantly reduces cardiovascular risk, slows disease progression, and improves long-term heart and vascular health.','','Statin Therapy / Lipid-Lowering Agents','Statin therapy and lipid-lowering medications are treatments used to reduce cholesterol levels and decrease the risk of cardiovascular disease. These medications help stabilize arterial plaques and reduce the risk of heart attack and stroke. They form a major component of preventive cardiology care.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(246,'Beta-Blockers','procedures/banners/99d40010-e990-4b59-ab16-380fabdab205.webp',NULL,'beta-blockers','Beta-blockers are cardiovascular medications that reduce heart rate, lower blood pressure, and decrease the workload on the heart. They are widely used in the treatment of hypertension, heart failure, arrhythmias, and coronary artery disease. These medications improve cardiac efficiency and reduce stress on the cardiovascular system.','Common beta-blockers include: Metoprolol Bisoprolol Atenolol Carvedilol Propranolol They are used for: High blood pressure Heart failure Angina Arrhythmias Post-heart attack management Beta-blockers help reduce oxygen demand by slowing heart activity. They may also help control symptoms such as palpitations and anxiety-related tachycardia.','[{\"value\":\"High blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Fast heartbeat or palpitations\"},{\"value\":\"Chest pain\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Irregular heart rhythm\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Beta-Blockers is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Slow heart rate\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue or dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Worsening asthma symptoms in some patients\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden withdrawal complications if stopped abruptly\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Beta-Blockers is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Common beta-blockers include: Metoprolol Bisoprolol Atenolol Carvedilol Propranolol They are used for: High blood pressure Heart failure Angina Arrhythmias Post-heart attack management Beta-blockers help reduce oxygen de...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications regularly without missing doses\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor pulse and blood pressure routinely\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid sudden discontinuation of medication\"},{\"value\":\"Report severe dizziness or breathing problems\"},{\"value\":\"Attend cardiology follow-up visits consistently\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Slow heart rate\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue or dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Worsening asthma symptoms in some patients\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden withdrawal complications if stopped abruptly\"}]','Beta-blocker therapy improves heart function, reduces cardiovascular complications, and enhances survival in many cardiac conditions.','','Beta-Blockers','Beta-blockers are cardiovascular medications that reduce heart rate, lower blood pressure, and decrease the workload on the heart. They are widely used in the treatment of hypertension, heart failure, arrhythmias, and coronary artery disease. These medications improve cardiac efficiency and reduce stress on the cardiovascular system.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(247,'ACE Inhibitors / ARBs / ARNI','procedures/banners/8020abbd-fff9-4ece-b7db-8733e4fc8b93.webp',NULL,'ace-inhibitors-arbs-arni','ACE inhibitors, ARBs, and ARNI medications are cardiovascular drugs used to lower blood pressure, improve heart function, and protect the kidneys and blood vessels. These medications are commonly used in hypertension, heart failure, and post-heart attack care. They help reduce strain on the heart and improve long-term cardiovascular outcomes.','Common medications include: Enalapril Ramipril Losartan Telmisartan Sacubitril/Valsartan (ARNI) The therapy helps: Relax blood vessels Reduce blood pressure Improve heart pumping efficiency Protect kidney function Reduce heart failure progression These medications are essential in modern heart failure management.','[{\"value\":\"High blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs or breathlessness\"},{\"value\":\"Weak heart pumping function\"},{\"value\":\"Diabetic kidney involvement\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which ACE Inhibitors \\/ ARBs \\/ ARNI is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent dry cough with ACE inhibitors\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated potassium levels\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic swelling reactions\"}]','[]','[]','<p>ACE Inhibitors / ARBs / ARNI is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Common medications include: Enalapril Ramipril Losartan Telmisartan Sacubitril/Valsartan (ARNI) The therapy helps: Relax blood vessels Reduce blood pressure Improve heart pumping efficiency Protect kidney function Reduce...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor blood pressure regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend kidney function and electrolyte testing\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid excessive salt intake\"},{\"value\":\"Report swelling or breathing difficulty immediately\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent dry cough with ACE inhibitors\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated potassium levels\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic swelling reactions\"}]','These medications improve heart function, reduce hospitalizations, protect kidney health, and improve long-term cardiovascular survival.','','ACE Inhibitors / ARBs / ARNI','ACE inhibitors, ARBs, and ARNI medications are cardiovascular drugs used to lower blood pressure, improve heart function, and protect the kidneys and blood vessels. These medications are commonly used in hypertension, heart failure, and post-heart attack care. They help reduce strain on the heart and improve long-term cardiovascular outcomes.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(248,'Calcium Channel Blockers','procedures/banners/507d07db-4aa3-49ba-93ad-10d2697da410.webp',NULL,'calcium-channel-blockers','<p>Calcium channel blockers are medications that relax blood vessels and reduce heart workload by affecting calcium movement in the heart and blood vessel walls. They are commonly used to treat hypertension, angina, and certain arrhythmias. These medications improve blood flow and reduce cardiovascular stress.</p>','<p>Common calcium channel blockers include: Amlodipine Diltiazem Verapamil Nifedipine They are used for: High blood pressure Chest pain (angina) Coronary artery spasm Certain irregular heart rhythms The therapy improves oxygen supply to the heart and lowers blood pressure effectively.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Elevated blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Chest pain during exertion\"},{\"value\":\"Palpitations\"},{\"value\":\"Coronary artery disease symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Vascular spasms\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Calcium Channel Blockers is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs or ankles\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Constipation with some medications\"},{\"value\":\"Slow heart rate in certain patients\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Calcium Channel Blockers is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Common calcium channel blockers include: Amlodipine Diltiazem Verapamil Nifedipine They are used for: High blood pressure Chest pain (angina) Coronary artery spasm Certain irregular heart rhythms The therapy improves oxy...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications regularly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor blood pressure consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Reduce excessive salt intake\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up cardiac evaluations\"},{\"value\":\"Report persistent swelling or dizziness promptly\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs or ankles\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Constipation with some medications\"},{\"value\":\"Slow heart rate in certain patients\"}]','<p>Calcium channel blockers help improve blood pressure control, reduce angina symptoms, and support long-term cardiovascular stability.</p>','<p></p>','Calcium Channel Blockers','Calcium channel blockers are medications that relax blood vessels and reduce heart workload by affecting calcium movement in the heart and blood vessel walls. ',NULL,1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23','Best Calcium Channel Blockers '),(249,'Diuretics (Loop, Thiazide, Potassium-Sparing)','procedures/banners/8c0529e4-9e53-4684-bad2-e0808ae232f3.webp',NULL,'diuretics-loop-thiazide-potassium-sparing','Diuretics are medications that help the body remove excess salt and fluid through urine, reducing fluid overload and lowering blood pressure. They are commonly used in heart failure, hypertension, and edema-related conditions. Diuretics reduce strain on the heart and improve breathing and circulation.','Types of diuretics include: Loop diuretics Thiazide diuretics Potassium-sparing diuretics These medications are used for: Heart failure High blood pressure Leg swelling Fluid retention Kidney-related fluid overload Diuretics improve symptoms such as breathlessness and swelling. Electrolyte and kidney function monitoring may be required during therapy.','[{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs or abdomen\"},{\"value\":\"Breathlessness due to fluid overload\"},{\"value\":\"High blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Rapid weight gain from fluid retention\"},{\"value\":\"Congestive heart failure symptoms\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Diuretics (Loop, Thiazide, Potassium-Sparing) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Diuretics (Loop, Thiazide, Potassium-Sparing) is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Types of diuretics include: Loop diuretics Thiazide diuretics Potassium-sparing diuretics These medications are used for: Heart failure High blood pressure Leg swelling Fluid retention Kidney-related fluid overload Diure...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Monitor body weight regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Follow fluid and salt restrictions if advised\"},{\"value\":\"Attend blood test monitoring appointments\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications at recommended times\"},{\"value\":\"Report severe weakness or dizziness immediately\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"}]','Diuretic therapy improves symptom control, reduces fluid overload, and enhances quality of life in cardiovascular patients.','','Diuretics (Loop, Thiazide, Potassium-Sparing)','Diuretics are medications that help the body remove excess salt and fluid through urine, reducing fluid overload and lowering blood pressure. They are commonly used in heart failure, hypertension, and edema-related conditions. Diuretics reduce strain on the heart and improve breathing and circulation.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(250,'Anti-arrhythmic Medications','procedures/banners/b8b732f9-3fe5-457b-9fcd-61aae8dab8aa.webp',NULL,'anti-arrhythmic-medications','Anti-arrhythmic medications are drugs used to control abnormal heart rhythms and stabilize electrical activity within the heart. These medications help manage fast, slow, or irregular heartbeats and reduce arrhythmia-related complications. They play an important role in both emergency and long-term cardiology care.','Common anti-arrhythmic medications include: Amiodarone Sotalol Flecainide Digoxin Lidocaine These medications are used for: Atrial fibrillation Ventricular arrhythmias Supraventricular tachycardia Palpitations Rhythm stabilization after cardiac events Careful monitoring is often necessary due to potential side effects and rhythm-related risks.','[{\"value\":\"Palpitations\"},{\"value\":\"Irregular heartbeat\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness or fainting\"},{\"value\":\"Rapid heart rate\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath related to arrhythmias\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Anti-arrhythmic Medications is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Slow or excessively fast heart rhythms\"},{\"value\":\"Medication-related toxicity\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness or low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Organ-related side effects with long-term use\"},{\"value\":\"Drug interactions\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Anti-arrhythmic Medications is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Common anti-arrhythmic medications include: Amiodarone Sotalol Flecainide Digoxin Lidocaine These medications are used for: Atrial fibrillation Ventricular arrhythmias Supraventricular tachycardia Palpitations Rhythm sta...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Attend ECG and rhythm monitoring appointments\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid self-adjusting medication doses\"},{\"value\":\"Report fainting or worsening palpitations immediately\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain regular cardiology follow-up care\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Slow or excessively fast heart rhythms\"},{\"value\":\"Medication-related toxicity\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness or low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Organ-related side effects with long-term use\"},{\"value\":\"Drug interactions\"}]','Anti-arrhythmic therapy helps control heart rhythm disorders, reduces symptoms, and improves long-term cardiac stability and quality of life.','','Anti-arrhythmic Medications','Anti-arrhythmic medications are drugs used to control abnormal heart rhythms and stabilize electrical activity within the heart. These medications help manage fast, slow, or irregular heartbeats and reduce arrhythmia-related complications. They play an important role in both emergency and long-term cardiology care.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:47','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(251,'Emergency Thrombolysis (as per STEMI protocols)','procedures/banners/0e2a3c13-7fe8-487c-a513-638550d8e88a.webp',NULL,'emergency-thrombolysis-as-per-stemi-protocols','Emergency thrombolysis is a life-saving treatment used to dissolve blood clots causing acute heart attacks, particularly ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (STEMI). The therapy restores blood flow to the heart muscle and reduces permanent heart damage. Rapid treatment significantly improves survival outcomes.','Thrombolytic medications are administered urgently in eligible patients when immediate angioplasty is not available. Common thrombolytic agents include: Streptokinase Tenecteplase Alteplase The treatment is used for: Acute STEMI heart attack Selected clot-related emergencies Early administration is critical and is often performed in emergency cardiac care settings under strict protocols. Continuous monitoring is required during and after treatment.','[{\"value\":\"Severe chest pain\"},{\"value\":\"Sweating and breathlessness\"},{\"value\":\"Pain radiating to arm or jaw\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden weakness or collapse\"},{\"value\":\"ECG evidence of STEMI\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Emergency Thrombolysis (as per STEMI protocols) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Serious bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke due to bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete clot dissolution\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Emergency Thrombolysis (as per STEMI protocols) is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Thrombolytic medications are administered urgently in eligible patients when immediate angioplasty is not available. Common thrombolytic agents include: Streptokinase Tenecteplase Alteplase The treatment is used for: Acu...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Continue intensive cardiac monitoring\"},{\"value\":\"Take prescribed cardiac medications consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid smoking and unhealthy diet\"},{\"value\":\"Attend cardiac rehabilitation and follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Seek immediate care for recurrent chest pain\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Serious bleeding complications\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke due to bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete clot dissolution\"}]','Successful emergency thrombolysis reduces heart muscle damage, improves survival, and supports better long-term heart function after acute heart attack treatment.','','Emergency Thrombolysis (as per STEMI protocols)','Emergency thrombolysis is a life-saving treatment used to dissolve blood clots causing acute heart attacks, particularly ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (STEMI). The therapy restores blood flow to the heart muscle and reduces permanent heart damage. Rapid treatment significantly improves survival outcomes.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:23',NULL),(252,'Congenital Heart Disease ',NULL,NULL,'congenital-heart-disease','<p>Congenital heart disease (CHD) refers to structural abnormalities of the heart that are present from birth. These defects may affect the heart chambers, valves, blood vessels, or blood flow patterns. Some congenital heart defects are diagnosed during infancy, while others may remain unnoticed until adolescence or adulthood. Modern cardiology and cardiac surgery treatments allow many children and adults with CHD to lead healthy and active lives.</p>','<p>Congenital heart disease includes a wide range of conditions such as: Atrial septal defect (ASD) Ventricular septal defect (VSD) Tetralogy of Fallot Patent ductus arteriosus (PDA) Congenital valve abnormalities Cyanotic heart disease The severity varies from mild defects requiring observation to complex abnormalities needing surgery or catheter-based intervention. Diagnosis may involve: Echocardiography ECG Cardiac MRI CT angiography Cardiac catheterization Long-term cardiology follow-up is important for monitoring heart function and preventing complications.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Poor growth in children\"},{\"value\":\"Cyanosis (bluish discoloration)\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue during activity\"},{\"value\":\"Heart murmur or palpitations\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Congenital Heart Disease is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Heart failure\"},{\"value\":\"Arrhythmias\"},{\"value\":\"Pulmonary hypertension\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke or clot formation\"},{\"value\":\"Infective endocarditis\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Congenital Heart Disease is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Congenital heart disease includes a wide range of conditions such as: Atrial septal defect (ASD) Ventricular septal defect (VSD) Tetralogy of Fallot Patent ductus arteriosus (PDA) Congenital valve abnormalities Cyanotic...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Attend regular pediatric or adult cardiology follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor exercise tolerance and symptoms carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain infection prevention and dental hygiene\"},{\"value\":\"Follow activity recommendations provided by specialists\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Heart failure\"},{\"value\":\"Arrhythmias\"},{\"value\":\"Pulmonary hypertension\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke or clot formation\"},{\"value\":\"Infective endocarditis\"}]','<p>With early diagnosis and appropriate treatment, many patients with congenital heart disease achieve improved survival, better heart function, and enhanced quality of life into adulthood.</p>','<p></p>','Congenital Heart Disease (Pediatric and Adult)','Congenital heart disease (CHD) refers to structural abnormalities of the heart that are present from birth. ',NULL,1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24','Congenital  Heart Disease causes and symptoms'),(253,'Pericardial Diseases (Pericarditis, Pericardial Effusion, Tamponade)','procedures/banners/5f13eee6-e92d-4873-8c8c-99fb64880af8.webp',NULL,'pericardial-diseases-pericarditis-pericardial-effusion-tamponade','Pericardial diseases involve disorders affecting the pericardium, the protective sac surrounding the heart. Common conditions include: Pericarditis (inflammation) Pericardial effusion (fluid accumulation) Cardiac tamponade (life-threatening pressure on the heart) These conditions may occur due to infections, autoimmune diseases, trauma, cancer, kidney failure, or after heart surgery.','Pericardial disorders can range from mild inflammation to severe emergencies requiring urgent treatment. Diagnosis may involve: Echocardiography ECG Chest imaging Blood tests CT or MRI scans Treatment depends on severity and may include: Anti-inflammatory medications Antibiotics Pericardiocentesis (fluid drainage) Surgical procedures Cardiac tamponade is a medical emergency that can severely impair heart pumping function.','[{\"value\":\"Sharp chest pain\"},{\"value\":\"Breathlessness\"},{\"value\":\"Fever or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Rapid heartbeat\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling or low blood pressure in severe cases\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Pericardial Diseases (Pericarditis, Pericardial Effusion, Tamponade) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Cardiac tamponade\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent pericarditis\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic constrictive pericarditis\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden cardiovascular collapse in severe cases\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Pericardial Diseases (Pericarditis, Pericardial Effusion, Tamponade) is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Pericardial disorders can range from mild inflammation to severe emergencies requiring urgent treatment. Diagnosis may involve: Echocardiography ECG Chest imaging Blood tests CT or MRI scans Treatment depends on severity...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications regularly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid strenuous physical activity temporarily\"},{\"value\":\"Attend repeat echocardiography evaluations\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor chest pain or breathing difficulty\"},{\"value\":\"Seek emergency care for worsening symptoms\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Cardiac tamponade\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent pericarditis\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic constrictive pericarditis\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden cardiovascular collapse in severe cases\"}]','Most patients recover well with timely treatment, although some may require long-term monitoring for recurrence or chronic pericardial complications.','','Pericardial Diseases (Pericarditis, Pericardial Effusion, Tamponade)','Pericardial diseases involve disorders affecting the pericardium, the protective sac surrounding the heart. Common conditions include: Pericarditis (inflammation) Pericardial effusion (fluid accumulation) Cardiac tamponade (life-threatening pressure on the heart) These conditions may occur due to infections, autoimmune diseases, trauma, cancer, kidney failure, or after heart surgery.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24',NULL),(254,'Endocarditis ','procedures/banners/71b005ab-1a5a-4b63-9551-8a62809400f7.webp',NULL,'endocarditis','<p>Infective endocarditis is a serious infection of the inner lining of the heart and heart valves caused by bacteria or other microorganisms. The infection can damage heart valves and may spread to other organs if untreated. Prompt diagnosis and intensive treatment are critical to prevent life-threatening complications.</p>','<p>Infective endocarditis commonly affects: Damaged heart valves Artificial heart valves Congenital heart disease patients Intravenous drug users Diagnosis may include: Blood cultures Echocardiography ECG Laboratory tests Cardiac imaging Treatment usually involves prolonged intravenous antibiotics and sometimes cardiac surgery. Early recognition significantly improves outcomes.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Fever and chills\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue and weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Heart murmur\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Weight loss or night sweats\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Endocarditis is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Heart valve destruction\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke from infected clots\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney complications\"},{\"value\":\"Life-threatening sepsis\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Endocarditis is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Infective endocarditis commonly affects: Damaged heart valves Artificial heart valves Congenital heart disease patients Intravenous drug users Diagnosis may include: Blood cultures Echocardiography ECG Laboratory tests C...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Complete the full antibiotic course strictly\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain excellent dental hygiene\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular cardiology follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for recurrent fever or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Inform doctors before invasive procedures\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Heart valve destruction\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke from infected clots\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney complications\"},{\"value\":\"Life-threatening sepsis\"}]','<p>With timely treatment, many patients recover successfully, although severe cases may require valve surgery and long-term cardiac monitoring.</p>','<p></p>','Endocarditis (Infective)','Infective endocarditis is a serious infection of the inner lining of the heart and heart valves caused by bacteria or other microorganisms. ',NULL,1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24',' Endocarditis  causes and symptoms'),(255,'Hyperlipidemia / Dyslipidemia','procedures/banners/06938535-c591-4a79-a317-c147aff562cb.webp',NULL,'hyperlipidemia-dyslipidemia','Hyperlipidemia or dyslipidemia refers to abnormal levels of fats (lipids) in the blood, including cholesterol and triglycerides. High cholesterol contributes to plaque buildup in arteries and increases the risk of heart attack, stroke, and vascular disease. Proper management is essential for long-term cardiovascular health.','Common lipid abnormalities include: High LDL cholesterol Low HDL cholesterol Elevated triglycerides Risk factors include: Poor diet Obesity Diabetes Smoking Genetic disorders Sedentary lifestyle Diagnosis is performed using lipid profile blood tests. Treatment includes: Lifestyle modification Statin therapy Lipid-lowering medications Weight control and exercise Regular monitoring is important to reduce cardiovascular risk.','[{\"value\":\"Usually no symptoms initially\"},{\"value\":\"Chest pain from blocked arteries\"},{\"value\":\"Fat deposits around eyes or skin in severe cases\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity-related symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"History of cardiovascular disease\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Hyperlipidemia \\/ Dyslipidemia is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Coronary artery disease\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke\"},{\"value\":\"Peripheral vascular disease\"},{\"value\":\"Pancreatitis with high triglycerides\"},{\"value\":\"Atherosclerosis progression\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Hyperlipidemia / Dyslipidemia is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Common lipid abnormalities include: High LDL cholesterol Low HDL cholesterol Elevated triglycerides Risk factors include: Poor diet Obesity Diabetes Smoking Genetic disorders Sedentary lifestyle Diagnosis is performed us...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Follow a low-fat heart-healthy diet\"},{\"value\":\"Exercise regularly as advised\"},{\"value\":\"Take cholesterol medications consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid smoking and alcohol excess\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor lipid levels routinely\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Coronary artery disease\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke\"},{\"value\":\"Peripheral vascular disease\"},{\"value\":\"Pancreatitis with high triglycerides\"},{\"value\":\"Atherosclerosis progression\"}]','Proper lipid management significantly lowers cardiovascular risk and supports long-term heart and vascular health.','','Hyperlipidemia / Dyslipidemia','Hyperlipidemia or dyslipidemia refers to abnormal levels of fats (lipids) in the blood, including cholesterol and triglycerides. High cholesterol contributes to plaque buildup in arteries and increases the risk of heart attack, stroke, and vascular disease. Proper management is essential for long-term cardiovascular health.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24',NULL),(256,'Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD)','procedures/banners/abf7e002-5f6c-4c6f-9b90-22deb85a6601.webp',NULL,'peripheral-arterial-disease-pad','Peripheral arterial disease (PAD) is a circulatory condition caused by narrowing or blockage of arteries supplying blood to the limbs, most commonly the legs. The condition usually develops due to atherosclerosis and reduced blood flow. Early treatment helps prevent severe complications and limb damage.','PAD commonly affects older adults and individuals with: Diabetes Smoking history High cholesterol Hypertension Coronary artery disease Diagnosis may include: Ankle-brachial index (ABI) Doppler ultrasound CT angiography Peripheral angiography Treatment options include: Lifestyle modification Medications Exercise therapy Angioplasty or vascular surgery Severe cases may lead to critical limb ischemia.','[{\"value\":\"Leg pain during walking (claudication)\"},{\"value\":\"Cold feet or legs\"},{\"value\":\"Weak pulses in legs\"},{\"value\":\"Non-healing wounds\"},{\"value\":\"Leg numbness or weakness\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Limb ischemia\"},{\"value\":\"Ulcer formation\"},{\"value\":\"Gangrene\"},{\"value\":\"Heart attack or stroke risk\"},{\"value\":\"Amputation in severe cases\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD) is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>PAD commonly affects older adults and individuals with: Diabetes Smoking history High cholesterol Hypertension Coronary artery disease Diagnosis may include: Ankle-brachial index (ABI) Doppler ultrasound CT angiography P...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Stop smoking completely\"},{\"value\":\"Exercise regularly under supervision\"},{\"value\":\"Control diabetes and blood pressure properly\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain foot care and hygiene\"},{\"value\":\"Attend vascular follow-up appointments regularly\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Limb ischemia\"},{\"value\":\"Ulcer formation\"},{\"value\":\"Gangrene\"},{\"value\":\"Heart attack or stroke risk\"},{\"value\":\"Amputation in severe cases\"}]','Early diagnosis and treatment improve circulation, reduce complications, and preserve long-term limb and cardiovascular health.','','Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD)','Peripheral arterial disease (PAD) is a circulatory condition caused by narrowing or blockage of arteries supplying blood to the limbs, most commonly the legs. The condition usually develops due to atherosclerosis and reduced blood flow. Early treatment helps prevent severe complications and limb damage.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24',NULL),(257,'Aortic Aneurysm / Aortic Dissection','procedures/banners/3ff95406-5315-4de1-acaf-f32e23f72d03.webp',NULL,'aortic-aneurysm-aortic-dissection','<p>An aortic aneurysm is an abnormal enlargement of the aorta, while aortic dissection occurs when a tear develops within the aortic wall layers. Both conditions are potentially life-threatening cardiovascular emergencies. Early diagnosis and management are essential to prevent rupture and sudden death.</p>','<p>Risk factors include: Hypertension Smoking Genetic disorders Atherosclerosis Connective tissue disease Diagnosis may involve: CT angiography MRI Echocardiography Ultrasound imaging Treatment depends on severity and may include: Blood pressure control Emergency surgery Endovascular repair Long-term monitoring Aortic dissection requires urgent medical attention.</p>','[{\"value\":\"Sudden severe chest or back pain\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Fainting or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Unequal blood pressure in limbs\"},{\"value\":\"Pulsating abdominal mass in some aneurysms\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Aortic Aneurysm \\/ Aortic Dissection is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Aortic rupture\"},{\"value\":\"Internal bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke\"},{\"value\":\"Organ damage from poor blood flow\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden death\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Aortic Aneurysm / Aortic Dissection is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Risk factors include: Hypertension Smoking Genetic disorders Atherosclerosis Connective tissue disease Diagnosis may involve: CT angiography MRI Echocardiography Ultrasound imaging Treatment depends on severity and may i...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Control blood pressure strictly\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid heavy lifting and strain\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular imaging follow-up\"},{\"value\":\"Take prescribed medications consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Seek emergency care for sudden pain symptoms\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Aortic rupture\"},{\"value\":\"Internal bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Stroke\"},{\"value\":\"Organ damage from poor blood flow\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden death\"}]','<p>With proper treatment and monitoring, many patients achieve improved survival and reduced risk of life-threatening aortic complications.</p>','<p></p>','Aortic Aneurysm / Aortic Dissection','An aortic aneurysm is an abnormal enlargement of the aorta, while aortic dissection occurs when a tear develops within the aortic wall layers. Both conditions are potentially life-threatening cardiovascular emergencies.',NULL,1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24','Best Aortic Aneurysm / Aortic Dissection in Bangalore'),(258,'Pulmonary Hypertension','procedures/banners/357b8351-0ec9-421b-9093-f2d67e58faa5.webp',NULL,'pulmonary-hypertension','Pulmonary hypertension is a condition characterized by elevated blood pressure within the arteries supplying the lungs. The increased pressure places strain on the right side of the heart and can eventually lead to heart failure if untreated. Early diagnosis and specialized treatment improve outcomes and quality of life.','Pulmonary hypertension may occur due to: Heart disease Lung disease Blood clots Connective tissue disorders Idiopathic causes Diagnostic evaluation may include: Echocardiography Right heart catheterization CT scans Pulmonary function tests Blood investigations Treatment options include: Oxygen therapy Diuretics Vasodilator medications Anticoagulation Advanced pulmonary hypertension therapies Specialized cardiology and pulmonology care are often required.','[{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue\"},{\"value\":\"Chest discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness or fainting episodes\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Pulmonary Hypertension is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Right heart failure\"},{\"value\":\"Arrhythmias\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced oxygen levels\"},{\"value\":\"Progressive exercise intolerance\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Pulmonary Hypertension is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>Pulmonary hypertension may occur due to: Heart disease Lung disease Blood clots Connective tissue disorders Idiopathic causes Diagnostic evaluation may include: Echocardiography Right heart catheterization CT scans Pulmo...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Take medications consistently as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid excessive physical exertion\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor oxygen saturation if advised\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular cardiac and pulmonary reviews\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain vaccination and infection prevention measures\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Right heart failure\"},{\"value\":\"Arrhythmias\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced oxygen levels\"},{\"value\":\"Progressive exercise intolerance\"}]','Long-term treatment can improve symptoms, exercise capacity, and survival, although ongoing specialist monitoring is often necessary.','','Pulmonary Hypertension','Pulmonary hypertension is a condition characterized by elevated blood pressure within the arteries supplying the lungs. The increased pressure places strain on the right side of the heart and can eventually lead to heart failure if untreated. Early diagnosis and specialized treatment improve outcomes and quality of life.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24',NULL),(259,'Ischemic Cardiomyopathy','procedures/banners/861ec69f-8d53-4399-b4e3-76641c75adc2.webp',NULL,'ischemic-cardiomyopathy','Ischemic cardiomyopathy is a condition where the heart muscle becomes weakened due to reduced blood supply from coronary artery disease or previous heart attacks. The weakened heart struggles to pump blood effectively, leading to heart failure symptoms. It is one of the most common causes of chronic heart failure.','The condition develops when coronary artery blockages damage heart muscle tissue over time. Evaluation may include: Echocardiography Coronary angiography ECG Cardiac MRI Stress testing Treatment may involve: Heart failure medications Angioplasty or bypass surgery Lifestyle modification Implantable cardiac devices Comprehensive cardiac rehabilitation improves recovery and long-term management.','[{\"value\":\"Breathlessness\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue and weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs\"},{\"value\":\"Chest pain\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced exercise tolerance\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Ischemic Cardiomyopathy is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic condition that no longer responds adequately to medicines alone\"},{\"value\":\"Acute complications such as infection, obstruction, bleeding, or severe inflammation\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital issues, trauma, or degenerative changes affecting normal function\"},{\"value\":\"Specialist assessment confirming that procedural treatment is the safest next step\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Heart failure progression\"},{\"value\":\"Dangerous arrhythmias\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden cardiac death\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent heart attacks\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney dysfunction\"}]','[]','[]','<p>Ischemic Cardiomyopathy is considered when symptoms, investigation findings, or disease progression indicate that procedural treatment will offer safer or more lasting relief. At Nano Hospitals, specialists tailor the approach to the diagnosis, overall health, and recovery goals.</p><p>The condition develops when coronary artery blockages damage heart muscle tissue over time. Evaluation may include: Echocardiography Coronary angiography ECG Cardiac MRI Stress testing Treatment may involve: Heart failur...</p><p>Your care team will explain preparation, expected benefits, possible risks, and recovery guidance before proceeding.</p>','[]','[]','[{\"value\":\"Follow heart failure medication schedules carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Restrict salt intake if advised\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor weight and swelling regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend cardiac rehabilitation programs\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid smoking and unhealthy diet habits\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Heart failure progression\"},{\"value\":\"Dangerous arrhythmias\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden cardiac death\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrent heart attacks\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney dysfunction\"}]','Appropriate treatment improves heart function, reduces hospitalizations, and enhances long-term survival and quality of life.','','Ischemic Cardiomyopathy','Ischemic cardiomyopathy is a condition where the heart muscle becomes weakened due to reduced blood supply from coronary artery disease or previous heart attacks. The weakened heart struggles to pump blood effectively, leading to heart failure symptoms. It is one of the most common causes of chronic heart failure.','',1,'2026-05-18 01:33:48','2026-07-29 00:28:24',NULL),(260,'Stress Cardiomyopathy (Takotsubo)','procedures/banners/cd34787c-d6dc-4755-b34f-f676ea02f9ec.webp',NULL,'stress-cardiomyopathy-takotsubo','Stress cardiomyopathy, also called Takotsubo cardiomyopathy, is a temporary heart muscle weakness often triggered by severe emotional or physical stress. The condition mimics a heart attack but usually occurs without significant coronary artery blockage. Most patients recover heart function completely with proper care.','Common triggers include: Emotional trauma Severe illness Surgery Sudden stress events Diagnosis may involve: ECG Echocardiography Coronary angiography Cardiac MRI Blood tests Treatment focuses on supportive cardiac care and management of complications. The condition is more common in postmenopausal women.','[{\"value\":\"Sudden chest pain\"},{\"value\":\"Shortness of breath\"},{\"value\":\"Palpitations\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness\"},{\"value\":\"Symptoms similar to heart attack\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Disease or structural problem for which Stress Cardiomyopathy (Takotsubo) is commonly indicated\"},{\"value\":\"Progression of a chronic c